{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VwmbbtDD3vU6RsUFrwoezm","type":"tool_result","content":"1140\t;; =============================================================================\n1141\t;; Custody (draft §5.5 as ruled, UCF 7.2.1, 7.4.3, 7.7.8; phase-7 plan §3.1, §3.3)\n1142\t;; =============================================================================\n1143\t;;\n1144\t;; The root's slot 16 is the custody arm as plain data, by kind: nil for a\n1145\t;; fork root of any kind (owner, 2026-10-13: the fork is never spelled);\n1146\t;; {:yin.k/policy :yin.k/exclusive :yin.k/occurrence :yin.k/arbitration\n1147\t;; :yin.k/next-op-seq} plus :yin.k/origin on a successor for a blocked or\n1148\t;; parked exclusive root; {:yin.k/origin} alone for a halted exclusive\n1149\t;; root; nil on every install child. No other key: lease, epoch and holder\n1150\t;; never enter a body. `custody-baseline` is the one grammar over a task's\n1151\t;; slot and its carried operation ids: the rows inspector\n1152\t;; (yin.vm.ucf.rows.checkpoint) answers it, lower-task's custody stage runs\n1153\t;; it before the grant checks, and lift-task runs it before emitting.\n1154\t;; Refusals are :yin.k/undecodable with a path relative to the root task:\n1155\t;; [:custody k] for the slot, [:frames i :op-id] for a wait's id, both\n1156\t;; prefixed by [:installs <name>] inside an install child.\n1157\t\n1158\t(def max-exact\n1159\t  \"2^52-1, the largest sequence or counter (7.7.8).\"\n1160\t  4503599627370495)\n1161\t\n1162\t\n1163\t(def ^:private custody-keys\n1164\t  #{:yin.k/policy :yin.k/occurrence :yin.k/arbitration :yin.k/next-op-seq :yin.k/origin})\n1165\t\n1166\t\n1167\t(def write-slots\n1168\t  \"Retained write reason -> [target payload op-id], indices into its\n1169\t   :pending row's slots (the reason at 0).\"\n1170\t  {:put [1 2 3] :ffi-request [3 2 6] :link-request [3 6 7]})\n1171\t\n1172\t\n1173\t(defn- custody-refuse!\n1174\t  [kind path]\n1175\t  (refuse! :yin.k/undecodable kind path))\n1176\t\n1177\t\n1178\t(defn- check-origin!\n1179\t  [c]\n1180\t  (let [origin (get c :yin.k/origin) p [:custody :yin.k/origin]]\n1181\t    (when-not (and (map? origin)\n1182\t                   (custody/occurrence? (get origin :yin.k/occurrence))\n1183\t                   (some? (get origin :dao.lease/lease))\n1184\t                   (some? (get origin :yin.k/emitter)))\n1185\t      (custody-refuse! :malformed-origin p))\n1186\t    (when (cbor/content= (get origin :yin.k/occurrence) (get c :yin.k/occurrence))\n1187\t      (custody-refuse! :origin-is-self (conj p :yin.k/occurrence)))))\n1188\t\n1189\t\n1190\t(defn- check-root-custody!\n1191\t  \"A non-nil root slot by kind: the version-1 header rules\n1192\t   (checkpoint.cljc's check-root-header!) on the slot's map.\"\n1193\t  [c kind]\n1194\t  (when-not (map? c) (custody-refuse! :malformed-custody [:custody]))\n1195\t  (when-some [k (first (sort-by str (remove custody-keys (keys c))))]\n1196\t    (custody-refuse! :custody-key [:custody k]))\n1197\t  (if (= :halted kind)\n1198\t    (do (doseq [k [:yin.k/policy :yin.k/occurrence :yin.k/arbitration :yin.k/next-op-seq]\n1199\t                :when (contains? c k)]\n1200\t          (custody-refuse! :halted-header [:custody k]))\n1201\t        (when-not (contains? c :yin.k/origin) (custody-refuse! :missing-header [:custody :yin.k/origin]))\n1202\t        (check-origin! c))\n1203\t    (do (doseq [k [:yin.k/policy :yin.k/occurrence :yin.k/arbitration :yin.k/next-op-seq]\n1204\t                :when (not (contains? c k))]\n1205\t          (custody-refuse! :missing-header [:custody k]))\n1206\t        (when-not (= :yin.k/exclusive (get c :yin.k/policy))\n1207\t          (custody-refuse! :policy [:custody :yin.k/policy]))\n1208\t        (when (nil? (get c :yin.k/occurrence)) (custody-refuse! :nil-occurrence [:custody :yin.k/occurrence]))\n1209\t        (when-not (custody/occurrence? (get c :yin.k/occurrence))\n1210\t          (custody-refuse! :malformed-occurrence [:custody :yin.k/occurrence]))\n1211\t        (let [arb (get c :yin.k/arbitration)]\n1212\t          (when-not (and (map? arb) (some? (get arb :dao.stream/identity)) (map? (get arb :dao.stream/descriptor)))\n1213\t            (custody-refuse! :malformed-arbitration [:custody :yin.k/arbitration])))\n1214\t        (let [n (get c :yin.k/next-op-seq)]\n1215\t          (when-not (custody/exact? n) (custody-refuse! :inexact [:custody :yin.k/next-op-seq]))\n1216\t          (when (and (not (contains? c :yin.k/origin)) (not (cbor/num= 0 n)))\n1217\t            (custody-refuse! :first-export-counter [:custody :yin.k/next-op-seq])))\n1218\t        (when (contains? c :yin.k/origin) (check-origin! c)))))\n1219\t\n1220\t\n1221\t(defn- check-op-id!\n1222\t  \"One carried id against the root context: its shape, an origin present,\n1223\t   never the root's own occurrence, below the root counter (checkpoint.cljc's\n1224\t   check-op-id!, verbatim).\"\n1225\t  [ctx op-id p]\n1226\t  (when-not (and (map? op-id) (= 2 (count op-id))\n1227\t                 (custody/occurrence? (get op-id :yin.k/occurrence))\n1228\t                 (contains? op-id :yin.k/seq))\n1229\t    (custody-refuse! :malformed-op-id p))\n1230\t  (when-not (custody/exact? (get op-id :yin.k/seq)) (custody-refuse! :inexact (conj p :yin.k/seq)))\n1231\t  (when-not (contains? ctx :yin.k/origin) (custody-refuse! :op-id-without-origin p))\n1232\t  (when (cbor/content= (get op-id :yin.k/occurrence) (get ctx :yin.k/occurrence))\n1233\t    (custody-refuse! :op-id-own-occurrence p))\n1234\t  ;; a :halted root has no counter, so no id can be below it\n1235\t  (when-not (and (contains? ctx :yin.k/next-op-seq)\n1236\t                 (neg? (cbor/num-compare (get op-id :yin.k/seq) (get ctx :yin.k/next-op-seq))))\n1237\t    (custody-refuse! :op-seq-range (conj p :yin.k/seq))))\n1238\t\n1239\t\n1240\t(defn- wire-slot\n1241\t  \"A V slot as the wire holds it: a [:row n] is [:row id].\"\n1242\t  [x]\n1243\t  (if (and (vector? x) (= :row (first x))) [:row (first (emit-node (second x) {} {}))] x))\n1244\t\n1245\t\n1246\t(defn- task-ops\n1247\t  \"[path op-id intent] of every id the waits of task carry, then of each\n1248\t   install child in carried (module-name) order, in the root's context.\n1249\t   Checks each task's kind and role, each :install pending's install row,\n1250\t   and that a child's custody slot is nil.\"\n1251\t  [ctx task role path]\n1252\t  (let [[_ _ kind role' _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ installs waits] (:slots task)\n1253\t        names (into #{} (map #(first (:slots %))) installs)]\n1254\t    (when-not (contains? #{:blocked :parked :halted} kind) (custody-refuse! :kind (conj path :kind)))\n1255\t    (when-not (= role role') (custody-refuse! :role (conj path :role)))\n1256\t    (into (into []\n1257\t                (keep-indexed\n1258\t                  (fn [i w]\n1259\t                    (let [ss (:slots (second (:slots w)))\n1260\t                          reason (first ss)\n1261\t                          p (conj path :frames i)]\n1262\t                      (when (and (= :install reason) (not (contains? names (second ss))))\n1263\t                        (custody-refuse! :incomplete-install p))\n1264\t                      (when-let [[t payload o] (get write-slots reason)]\n1265\t                        (when-some [op-id (nth ss o)]\n1266\t                          (let [p (conj p :op-id)]\n1267\t                            (when (::fork ctx) (custody-refuse! :fork-op-id p))\n1268\t                            (check-op-id! ctx op-id p)\n1269\t                            [p op-id [:yin.k/append (first (:slots (nth ss t))) (wire-slot (nth ss payload))]]))))))\n1270\t                waits)\n1271\t          (mapcat (fn [inst]\n1272\t                    (let [[mn _ _ _ child] (:slots inst)\n1273\t                          p (conj path :installs mn)]\n1274\t                      (when (some? (nth (:slots child) 16)) (custody-refuse! :child-header (conj p :custody)))\n1275\t                      (task-ops ctx child :child p))))\n1276\t          installs)))\n1277\t\n1278\t\n1279\t(defn custody-baseline\n1280\t  \"The operation baseline of root task (decoded, or abstract before emit),\n1281\t   or the first refusal thrown as ex-data {:yin.k/status :yin.k/undecodable\n1282\t   :yin.k/kind :yin.k/path}. Answers {:yin.k/kind k :yin.k/ops {op-id\n1283\t   digest}} plus the slot's :yin.k/occurrence, :yin.k/origin,\n1284\t   :yin.k/arbitration and :yin.k/next-op-seq, or :yin.k/fork true for a nil\n1285\t   slot, whose tree carries no id. digest is the BLAKE3 hex of the canonical\n1286\t   bytes of [:yin.k/append target-identity payload], the payload as the wire\n1287\t   slot holds it ([:lit x], [:row id], or a :link-request's plain envelope).\"\n1288\t  [task]\n1289\t  (let [slots (:slots task) kind (nth slots 2) c (nth slots 16) fork? (nil? c)]\n1290\t    (when-not (contains? #{:blocked :parked :halted} kind) (custody-refuse! :kind [:kind]))\n1291\t    (when-not fork? (check-root-custody! c kind))\n1292\t    (let [ctx (cond-> (select-keys c [:yin.k/occurrence :yin.k/origin :yin.k/next-op-seq]) fork? (assoc ::fork true))\n1293\t          ops (reduce (fn [acc [p op-id in]]\n1294\t                        (let [k (cbor/content-key op-id)]\n1295\t                          (when (contains? (:seen acc) k) (custody-refuse! :duplicate-op-id p))\n1296\t                          (-> acc (update :seen conj k)\n1297\t                              (assoc-in [:ops op-id] (jing/digest-bytes :blake3 (cbor/encode in))))))\n1298\t                      {:seen #{} :ops {}}\n1299\t                      (task-ops ctx task :root []))]\n1300\t      (cond-> (merge (select-keys c [:yin.k/occurrence :yin.k/origin :yin.k/arbitration :yin.k/next-op-seq])\n1301\t                     {:yin.k/kind kind :yin.k/ops (:ops ops)})\n1302\t        fork? (assoc :yin.k/fork true)))))\n1303\t\n1304\t\n1305\t(defn pack-address\n1306\t  \"The storage identity of a carrier: the BLAKE3 segment address of its\n1307\t   canonical bytes, distinct from the semantic root id it carries (§3.3).\"\n1308\t  [wire]\n1309\t  (jing/segment-key wire))\n1310\t\n1311\t\n1312\t;; =============================================================================\n1313\t;; Task transport (continuation design §7): lift-task and lower-task\n1314\t;; =============================================================================\n1315\t;;\n1316\t;; The lift walks a quiescent semantic-register machine into the abstract\n1317\t;; task the codec above emits: waits, parked records, the store, module\n1318\t;; stores, the free environment, the result and install children, every\n1319\t;; value classified as [:lit x], [:row n] or [:cursor-cell source]. A\n1320\t;; cursor cell's source is the resource id of a cursor reference, or\n1321\t;; [response-resource position] for a link wait's kept response cursor,\n1322\t;; so one resource reached twice is one cursor cell. The lower decodes the\n1323\t;; carrier (gate to frames, §3.3), checks pendings, dependencies and\n1324\t;; custody for every task of the tree, and only then attaches streams and\n1325\t;; restores state. Restoration delivers nothing, runs nothing.\n1326\t\n1327\t(defn- outcome!\n1328\t  [status kind data]\n1329\t  (throw (ex-info \"Task transport refused\"\n1330\t                  (merge data (cond-> {:yin.k/status status}\n1331\t                                (some? kind) (assoc :yin.k/kind kind))))))\n1332\t\n1333\t\n1334\t(defn- unliftable-hold\n1335\t  \"The first hold of m with no wire pending (UCF 7.4.1, 7.4.3), or nil.\"\n1336\t  [m]\n1337\t  (let [waits (:wait-set m)\n1338\t        cells (filter map? (vals (:resources m)))\n1339\t        held? #(and (map? %) (contains? % :yin.k/held))]\n1340\t    (cond\n1341\t      (some #(= :observe (:reason %)) waits) :observe\n1342\t      (or (some held? waits) (some held? cells)) :held\n1343\t      (some :yin.k/unminted cells) :unminted-cursor\n1344\t      (seq (:yin.k/closes m)) :pending-close\n1345\t      (some #(and (= :link-request (:reason %)) (not (contains? % :cursor))) waits)\n1346\t      :link-cursor-not-installed\n1347\t      :else nil)))\n1348\t\n1349\t\n1350\t(defn- stream-row!\n1351\t  \"The :stream row of resource sid, served once per resource.\"\n1352\t  [ctx sid]\n1353\t  (or (get-in @(:acc ctx) [:streams sid])\n1354\t      (let [h (get (:resources (:m ctx)) sid)]\n1355\t        (when (nil? h)\n1356\t          (outcome! :yin.k/non-portable :forged-resource-reference {:yin.k/hint sid}))\n1357\t        (let [marker (remote/lift-marker (:serve! ctx) h)]\n1358\t          (when (nil? marker) (outcome! :yin.k/unsatisfied nil {}))\n1359\t          (let [n (node :stream [(:dao.stream/identity marker) (:dao.stream/descriptor marker)])]\n1360\t            (swap! (:acc ctx) assoc-in [:streams sid] n)\n1361\t            n)))))\n1362\t\n1363\t\n1364\t(defn- cell!\n1365\t  [ctx source sid position]\n1366\t  (when-not (contains? (:cells @(:acc ctx)) source)\n1367\t    (let [stream (stream-row! ctx sid)]\n1368\t      (swap! (:acc ctx) assoc-in [:cells source] (node :cursor-cell-body [stream position]))))\n1369\t  source)\n1370\t\n1371\t\n1372\t(defn- cell-for!\n1373\t  [ctx cid]\n1374\t  (let [cell (get (:resources (:m ctx)) cid)]\n1375\t    (when-not (and (map? cell) (contains? cell :stream-id))\n1376\t      (outcome! :yin.k/non-portable :forged-resource-reference {:yin.k/hint cid}))\n1377\t    (cell! ctx cid (:stream-id cell) (:cursor cell))))\n1378\t\n1379\t\n1380\t(defn- address!\n1381\t  [ctx seg]\n1382\t  (if-some [a (get-in (:m ctx) [:code seg :address])]\n1383\t    (do (swap! (:acc ctx) update :segments conj a) a)\n1384\t    (outcome! :yin.k/non-portable :unaddressed-segment {:yin.k/hint seg})))\n1385\t\n1386\t\n1387\t(defn- scalar-literal?\n1388\t  [x]\n1389\t  (or (nil? x) (boolean? x) (string? x) (keyword? x) (symbol? x) (number? x)\n1390\t      (and (not (cbor/byte-payload? x)) (cbor/numeric? x))))\n1391\t\n1392\t\n1393\t(defn- primitive-name\n1394\t  [ctx f]\n1395\t  (let [m (:m ctx)\n1396\t        n (vm/name-of (:primitives m) (or (:primitive-canonical-names m) {}) f)\n1397\t        profile (when (symbol? n) (vm/profile-of (:primitives m) n))]\n1398\t    (cond\n1399\t      (nil? n) (outcome! :yin.k/non-portable :unnamed-function {})\n1400\t      (not (symbol? n)) (outcome! :yin.k/non-portable :ambiguous-primitive {})\n1401\t      (= :host (:yin.k/class profile)) (outcome! :yin.k/non-portable :host-state-primitive {:yin.k/name n})\n1402\t      :else n)))\n1403\t\n1404\t\n1405\t(declare lift-value state-node)\n1406\t\n1407\t\n1408\t(defn- collection-value\n1409\t  \"A guest collection: a literal when no member is a reference.\"\n1410\t  [ctx kind members original]\n1411\t  (let [vs (mapv #(lift-value ctx %) members)]\n1412\t    (if (every? #(= :lit (first %)) vs) [:lit original] [:row (node kind vs)])))\n1413\t\n1414\t\n1415\t(defn- bindings-node\n1416\t  [ctx e]\n1417\t  (node :bindings (mapcat (fn [[k v]] [k (lift-value ctx v)]) e)))\n1418\t\n1419\t\n1420\t(defn- context!\n1421\t  \"Record that segment a can run from pc at under environment e: a\n1422\t   closure's entry, an :act's or a return frame's pc (§7.1's discharge).\"\n1423\t  [ctx a at e]\n1424\t  (swap! (:acc ctx) update :contexts conj {:a a :at at :env (or e {})}))\n1425\t\n1426\t\n1427\t(defn- store-of!\n1428\t  [ctx e]\n1429\t  (let [store-of (engine/env-store-of e)]\n1430\t    (when (some? store-of) (swap! (:acc ctx) update :stores conj store-of))\n1431\t    store-of))\n1432\t\n1433\t\n1434\t(defn- lift-env-node\n1435\t  [ctx e]\n1436\t  (let [e (or e {})]\n1437\t    (node :env [(bindings-node ctx (engine/without-store-of e)) (store-of! ctx e)])))\n1438\t\n1439\t\n1440\t(defn- closure-node\n1441\t  [ctx c]\n1442\t  (let [e (or (:env c) {})\n1443\t        a (address! ctx (:segment c))]\n1444\t    (context! ctx a (:entry c) e)\n1445\t    (node :closure [a (:entry c) (vec (:params c))\n1446\t                    (bindings-node ctx (engine/without-store-of e)) (store-of! ctx e)])))\n1447\t\n1448\t\n1449\t(defn- lift-value\n1450\t  \"One machine value as a carrier value: [:lit x], [:row n] or\n1451\t   [:cursor-cell source]. A reference is authenticated before it is\n1452\t   encoded; a foreign value, a heap cell and a host object refuse.\"\n1453\t  [ctx x]\n1454\t  (let [m (:m ctx)]\n1455\t    (cond\n1456\t      (values/host-typed? x)\n1457\t      (cond\n1458\t        (not (values/owned-by? x (:owner m)))\n1459\t        (outcome! :yin.k/non-portable :foreign-value {:yin.k/hint (values/kind-of x)})\n1460\t        (values/closure? x) [:row (closure-node ctx (values/payload x))]\n1461\t        (values/continuation? x) [:row (node :reified [(state-node ctx (values/payload x))])]\n1462\t        :else (outcome! :yin.k/non-portable :non-canonicalizable {:yin.k/hint (values/kind-of x)}))\n1463\t      (fn? x) [:row (node :prim [(primitive-name ctx x)])]\n1464\t      (map? x)\n1465\t      (case (:type x)\n1466\t        :stream-ref (if (engine/authentic-ref? m :stream-ref x)\n1467\t                      [:row (stream-row! ctx (:id x))]\n1468\t                      (outcome! :yin.k/non-portable :forged-resource-reference {:yin.k/hint :stream-ref}))\n1469\t        :cursor-ref (if (engine/authentic-ref? m :cursor-ref x)\n1470\t                      [:cursor-cell (cell-for! ctx (:id x))]\n1471\t                      (outcome! :yin.k/non-portable :forged-resource-reference {:yin.k/hint :cursor-ref}))\n1472\t        :parked-continuation (if (contains? (:parked m) (:id x))\n1473\t                               [:row (node :parked-ref [(:id x)])]\n1474\t                               (outcome! :yin.k/non-portable :inconsistent-state {:yin.k/hint :parked-reference}))\n1475\t        :cell-ref (outcome! :yin.k/non-portable :cell {:yin.k/hint (:id x)})\n1476\t        (collection-value ctx :map (mapcat identity x) x))\n1477\t      (vector? x) (collection-value ctx :vec x x)\n1478\t      (set? x) (collection-value ctx :set (vec x) x)\n1479\t      (seq? x) (collection-value ctx :list (vec x) x)\n1480\t      (scalar-literal? x) [:lit x]\n1481\t      :else (outcome! :yin.k/non-portable :host-object {}))))\n1482\t\n1483\t\n1484\t(defn- window-node\n1485\t  [ctx w]\n1486\t  (node :window (mapcat (fn [[r v]] [r (lift-value ctx v)]) w)))\n1487\t\n1488\t\n1489\t(defn- k-node\n1490\t  [ctx k]\n1491\t  (node :k (mapv (fn [f]\n1492\t                   (let [a (address! ctx (:segment f))]\n1493\t                     (context! ctx a (:pc f) (:env f))\n1494\t                     (node :kframe [a (:pc f) (lift-env-node ctx (:env f))\n1495\t                                    (window-node ctx (:window f)) (:rd f)])))\n1496\t                 (or k []))))\n1497\t\n1498\t\n1499\t(defn- state-node\n1500\t  \"An evaluator payload (wait entry, parked record, reified payload) as\n1501\t   its :act or :tail row; engine fields are the pending's.\"\n1502\t  [ctx p]\n1503\t  (if (contains? p :site)\n1504\t    ;; a tail state resumes through its K: its own segment never runs again\n1505\t    (node :tail [(address! ctx (:segment p)) (:site p) (k-node ctx (:k p))])\n1506\t    (let [a (address! ctx (:segment p))]\n1507\t      (context! ctx a (:pc p) (:env p))\n1508\t      (node :act [a (:pc p) (lift-env-node ctx (:env p))\n1509\t                  (window-node ctx (:window p)) (k-node ctx (:k p)) (get-in p [:deliver :rd])]))))\n1510\t\n1511\t\n1512\t(defn- pending-node\n1513\t  \"The observed wait's pending (draft §5.3): the reason is the entry's,\n1514\t   never the site's static kind.\"\n1515\t  [ctx e]\n1516\t  (let [m (:m ctx)]\n1517\t    (case (:reason e)\n1518\t      :next (if (contains? e :call-id)\n1519\t              (node :pending [:ffi (cell-for! ctx (get-in e [:cursor-ref :id])) (:call-id e) (:op e)])\n1520\t              (node :pending [:next (cell-for! ctx (get-in e [:cursor-ref :id]))]))\n1521\t      :put (if (:request-sent e)\n1522\t             (let [carried? (and (:response-cursor e) (:response-stream e))\n1523\t                   cursor (if carried? (:response-cursor e) vm/call-out-cursor-key)\n1524\t                   response (if carried? (:response-stream e) vm/call-out-stream-key)]\n1525\t               (when-not (get (:resources m) cursor) (outcome! :yin.k/unsatisfied nil {}))\n1526\t               (node :pending [:ffi-request (:call-id e) (lift-value ctx (:datom e)) (stream-row! ctx (:stream-id e))\n1527\t                               (stream-row! ctx response) (cell-for! ctx cursor) (:op-id e)]))\n1528\t             (do (when-not (contains? e :datom) (outcome! :yin.k/non-portable :incomplete-write {}))\n1529\t                 (node :pending [:put (stream-row! ctx (:stream-id e)) (lift-value ctx (:datom e)) (:op-id e)])))\n1530\t      (:link-request :link-response)\n1531\t      (let [c (cell! ctx [(:response e) (:cursor e)] (:response e) (:cursor e))\n1532\t            base [(:reason e) (:link-id e) (:name e) (stream-row! ctx (:request e)) (stream-row! ctx (:response e)) c]]\n1533\t        (node :pending (if (= :link-request (:reason e)) (conj base (:envelope e) (:op-id e)) base)))\n1534\t      :install (do (when-not (contains? (:installs m) (:name e))\n1535\t                     (outcome! :yin.k/non-portable :incomplete-install {:yin.k/name (:name e)}))\n1536\t                   (node :pending [:install (:name e)]))\n1537\t      (outcome! :yin.k/non-portable :reason-mismatch {:yin.k/reason (:reason e)}))))\n1538\t\n1539\t\n1540\t(defn- store-node\n1541\t  [ctx s]\n1542\t  (node :store (mapcat (fn [[k v]]\n1543\t                         (when-not (= :lit (first (lift-value ctx k)))\n1544\t                           (outcome! :yin.k/non-portable :store-key {}))\n1545\t                         [k (lift-value ctx v)])\n1546\t                       s)))\n1547\t\n1548\t\n1549\t(defn- module-store-nodes\n1550\t  \"Every module store an environment or closure reaches, transitively.\"\n1551\t  [ctx]\n1552\t  (loop [done {}]\n1553\t    (if-let [mid (first (sort-by str (remove #(contains? done %) (:stores @(:acc ctx)))))]\n1554\t      (let [stores (:module-stores (:m ctx))]\n1555\t        (when-not (contains? stores mid)\n1556\t          (outcome! :yin.k/non-portable :missing-module-store {:yin.k/hint mid}))\n1557\t        (recur (assoc done mid (node :module-store [mid (store-node ctx (get stores mid))]))))\n1558\t      (mapv val (sort-by #(str (key %)) done)))))\n1559\t\n1560\t\n1561\t(defn- installing-names\n1562\t  [m]\n1563\t  (into #{} (mapcat (fn [[mn inst]]\n1564\t                      (map #(symbol (name mn) (name %))\n1565\t                           (get-in inst [:response :manifest :yin.module/exports]))))\n1566\t        (:installs m)))\n1567\t\n1568\t\n1569\t(defn live-pcs\n1570\t  \"The pcs of v control flow can still reach from at: the successor\n1571\t   relation (§8.1), so a backward jump makes earlier code live, and from\n1572\t   each reachable :closure its body from the entry, since reachable code\n1573\t   can still construct it.\"\n1574\t  [v at]\n1575\t  (loop [seen #{at}\n1576\t         todo [at]]\n1577\t    (if-let [p (peek todo)]\n1578\t      (let [t (nth v p)\n1579\t            fresh (remove seen (cond-> (analysis/successors v p)\n1580\t                                 (= :closure (nth t 0)) (conj (nth t 3))))]\n1581\t        (recur (into seen fresh) (into (pop todo) fresh)))\n1582\t      seen)))\n1583\t\n1584\t\n1585\t(defn- discharge!\n1586\t  \"The dependency closure over the v4 vectors (§7.1), after the walk that\n1587\t   found the contexts: every free occurrence control flow can still reach\n1588\t   from a carried context (live-pcs) is answered there, in resolve-var's\n1589\t   order: that context's\n1590\t   E, then the one store engine/active-store selects for it (the root\n1591\t   store, or the module store its store-of names; both travel), then a\n1592\t   primitive, an installing module's export, the module registry. Else\n1593\t   the lift is :yin.k/unsatisfied, discovery :incomplete.\"\n1594\t  [ctx code]\n1595\t  (let [m (:m ctx)\n1596\t        installing (installing-names m)\n1597\t        answered? (fn [sym e]\n1598\t                    (let [store-of (engine/env-store-of e)\n1599\t                          store (if (some? store-of) (get (:module-stores m) store-of {}) (:store m))]\n1600\t                      (or (vm/reserved-name? sym) (contains? e sym) (contains? store sym)\n1601\t                          (let [profile (vm/profile-of (:primitives m) sym)]\n1602\t                            (when (= :host (:yin.k/class profile))\n1603\t                              (outcome! :yin.k/non-portable :host-state-primitive {:yin.k/name sym}))\n1604\t                            (or (some? profile) (contains? installing sym)\n1605\t                                (and (some? (namespace sym))\n1606\t                                     (some? (module/resolve-module (:modules m)\n1607\t                                                                   (symbol (str (namespace sym) \".\" (name sym)))))))))))\n1608\t        scanned (into {} (map (fn [[a v]] [a (scan/free-occurrences v)])) code)\n1609\t        missing (into #{}\n1610\t                      (mapcat (fn [{:keys [a at env]}]\n1611\t                                (let [live (live-pcs (get code a) at)]\n1612\t                                  (keep (fn [o]\n1613\t                                          (when (and (contains? live (:at o))\n1614\t                                                     (not (answered? (:name o) env)))\n1615\t                                            (:name o)))\n1616\t                                        (get scanned a)))))\n1617\t                      (:contexts @(:acc ctx)))]\n1618\t    (when (seq missing)\n1619\t      (outcome! :yin.k/unsatisfied nil {:yin.k/discovery :incomplete :yin.k/missing {:obligations missing}}))))\n1620\t\n1621\t\n1622\t(declare lift-task*)\n1623\t\n1624\t\n1625\t(defn- install-node\n1626\t  [ctx mn inst opts]\n1627\t  (let [{:keys [phase parent response]} inst]\n1628\t    (when-not (contains? #{:running :parked} phase)\n1629\t      (outcome! :yin.k/non-portable :incomplete-install {:yin.k/name mn :yin.k/phase phase}))\n1630\t    (when-not (try (cbor/encode response) true\n1631\t                   (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _e false))\n1632\t      (outcome! :yin.k/non-portable :install-response {:yin.k/name mn}))\n1633\t    (node :install [mn phase parent response\n1634\t                    (lift-task* (:vm inst) (:serve! ctx) (dissoc opts :free-env) :child)])))\n1635\t\n1636\t\n1637\t(defn- lift-task*\n1638\t  [m serve! opts role]\n1639\t  (when (seq (:ready-queue m))\n1640\t    (outcome! :yin.k/not-quiescent nil {:yin.k/ready (count (:ready-queue m))}))\n1641\t  (when-some [h (unliftable-hold m)]\n1642\t    (outcome! :yin.k/non-portable :reason-mismatch {:yin.k/hold h}))\n1643\t  (when (some? (:control m))\n1644\t    (outcome! :yin.k/not-at-safepoint nil {:yin.k/pc (get-in m [:control :pc])}))\n1645\t  (let [value (:value m)\n1646\t        active? (and (map? value) (= :parked-continuation (:type value)) (contains? (:parked m) (:id value)))\n1647\t        kind (cond active? :parked\n1648\t                   (seq (:wait-set m)) :blocked\n1649\t                   (engine/halted-with-empty-queue? m) :halted\n1650\t                   :else (outcome! :yin.k/not-at-safepoint nil {}))\n1651\t        ;; §6.3: the explicit argument overrides the kernel's retained field\n1652\t        free-env (cond (some? (:free-env opts)) (:free-env opts)\n1653\t                       (some? (:free-env m)) (:free-env m)\n1654\t                       :else (outcome! :yin.k/non-portable :missing-free-env {}))\n1655\t        ctx {:m m :serve! serve! :acc (atom {:streams {} :cells {} :stores #{} :segments #{} :contexts #{}})}\n1656\t        free-node (bindings-node ctx free-env)\n1657\t        waits (mapv (fn [e] (node :wait [(state-node ctx e) (pending-node ctx e)])) (:wait-set m))\n1658\t        parked (node :parked-table (mapcat (fn [[p rec]] [p (state-node ctx rec)]) (:parked m)))\n1659\t        store (store-node ctx (:store m))\n1660\t        result (when (= :halted kind) (lift-value ctx value))\n1661\t        installs (mapv (fn [[mn inst]] (install-node ctx mn inst opts)) (sort-by #(str (key %)) (:installs m)))\n1662\t        module-stores (module-store-nodes ctx)\n1663\t        acc @(:acc ctx)\n1664\t        segments (:segments acc)\n1665\t        code (into {} (map (fn [a]\n1666\t                             (if-some [v (get-in m [:code (get (:code-aliases m) a) :vector])]\n1667\t                               [a v]\n1668\t                               (outcome! :yin.k/unsatisfied nil {:yin.k/segment a}))))\n1669\t                   segments)\n1670\t        _ (discharge! ctx code)\n1671\t        index (or (:source-index opts) {})\n1672\t        missing-trees (into #{} (remove #(seq (get index %))) segments)\n1673\t        _ (when (seq missing-trees)\n1674\t            (outcome! :yin.k/unsatisfied nil {:yin.k/discovery :incomplete :yin.k/missing {:yin.k/trees missing-trees}}))\n1675\t        requires {:yin.k/cursor-profiles (if (seq (:cells acc)) remote/cursor-profiles #{})\n1676\t                  :yin.k/segments segments\n1677\t                  :yin.k/trees (select-keys index segments)}\n1678\t        task (node :task [3 profile kind role (or (:id-counter m) 0) free-node store module-stores parked\n1679\t                          (node :cursor-cells (mapcat identity (:cells acc))) requires code installs waits\n1680\t                          (when (= :parked kind) (:id value)) result nil])]\n1681\t    ;; §3.3: a frame the evaluator itself minted that fails is inconsistent\n1682\t    (when-let [d (validate-frames task)]\n1683\t      (outcome! :yin.k/non-portable :inconsistent-state {:yin.k/defect d}))\n1684\t    task))\n1685\t\n1686\t\n1687\t(declare task-tree)\n1688\t\n1689\t\n1690\t(defn- header-custody\n1691\t  \"The root's custody slot from the caller's header, by kind: blocked or\n1692\t   parked takes the occurrence, arbitration, counter and the exclusive\n1693\t   policy, and the origin when the header names one; halted the origin\n1694\t   alone (an empty map without one, which the grammar refuses). A nil\n1695\t   value is an absent key (handoff.cljc's header-of).\"\n1696\t  [header kind]\n1697\t  (into {}\n1698\t        (filter (comp some? val))\n1699\t        (if (= :halted kind)\n1700\t          (select-keys header [:yin.k/origin])\n1701\t          (assoc (select-keys header [:yin.k/occurrence :yin.k/arbitration :yin.k/next-op-seq :yin.k/origin])\n1702\t                 :yin.k/policy :yin.k/exclusive))))\n1703\t\n1704\t\n1705\t(defn- protect!\n1706\t  \"Every retained write of the tree under the header's enrolled set (UCF\n1707\t   7.4.3, 7.7.8; handoff.cljc's protected!): an enrolled target without an\n1708\t   operation id is :unprotected-pending, an id on an unenrolled target is\n1709\t   :yin.k/unsatisfied naming the stream.\"\n1710\t  [task enrolled]\n1711\t  (doseq [[t _] (task-tree task :root)\n1712\t          w (nth (:slots t) 13)]\n1713\t    (let [ss (:slots (second (:slots w)))]\n1714\t      (when-let [[ti _ oi] (get write-slots (first ss))]\n1715\t        (let [identity (first (:slots (nth ss ti)))\n1716\t              enrolled? (contains? enrolled identity)\n1717\t              carried? (some? (nth ss oi))]\n1718\t          (cond\n1719\t            (and enrolled? (not carried?))\n1720\t            (outcome! :yin.k/non-portable :unprotected-pending {:dao.stream/identity identity})\n1721\t            (and carried? (not enrolled?))\n1722\t            (outcome! :yin.k/unsatisfied nil {:dao.stream/identity identity})\n1723\t            :else nil))))))\n1724\t\n1725\t\n1726\t(defn lift-task\n1727\t  \"The lift of §7.1: quiescent semantic-register machine m as a version-3\n1728\t   carrier, or a refusal thrown as ex-data {:yin.k/status :yin.k/kind}.\n1729\t   serve! is the exporter's remote-table entry (yin.vm.ucf.remote).\n1730\t   opts: :free-env, the task's initial free environment (default: the\n1731\t   kernel's retained :free-env field; the explicit value overrides it);\n1732\t   :source-index, {A #{tree-address}} the composition knows (§6.1), which\n1733\t   must cover every carried segment; :budget, the numbering budget;\n1734\t   :header, the exclusive custody header (occurrence, arbitration,\n1735\t   next-op-seq, origin when the task has a predecessor, and\n1736\t   :yin.k/enrolled, the enrolled stream identities, a lift input that\n1737\t   never travels). No header is the fork: custody nil. A header writes the\n1738\t   root's slot by kind (header-custody), refuses :op-seq-exhausted at\n1739\t   2^52-1 on a blocked or parked root, and protects every retained write\n1740\t   of the tree (protect!). Before emitting, the lift runs custody-baseline\n1741\t   over the task, so it never emits a carrier the inspector refuses.\"\n1742\t  ([m serve!] (lift-task m serve! {}))\n1743\t  ([m serve! opts]\n1744\t   (let [opts (or opts {})\n1745\t         header (:header opts)\n1746\t         task (lift-task* m serve! opts :root)\n1747\t         kind (nth (:slots task) 2)\n1748\t         task (if (nil? header)\n1749\t                task\n1750\t                (let [n (:yin.k/next-op-seq header)]\n1751\t                  (when (and (not= :halted kind) (cbor/numeric? n) (cbor/num= n max-exact))\n1752\t                    (outcome! :yin.k/non-portable :op-seq-exhausted {:yin.k/next-op-seq n}))\n1753\t                  (protect! task (or (:yin.k/enrolled header) #{}))\n1754\t                  (assoc-in task [:slots 16] (header-custody header kind))))]\n1755\t     (custody-baseline task)\n1756\t     (emit task (merge default-budget (:budget opts))))))\n1757\t\n1758\t\n1759\t(def ^:private fixed-resource-keys\n1760\t  #{vm/call-in-stream-key vm/call-out-stream-key vm/call-out-cursor-key\n1761\t    module/link-request-resource module/link-response-resource})\n1762\t\n1763\t\n1764\t(defn- fresh-key!\n1765\t  [used]\n1766\t  (loop [n (inc (count @used))]\n1767\t    (let [k (keyword \"yin.k\" (str \"k-\" n))]\n1768\t      (if (contains? @used k) (recur (inc n)) (do (swap! used conj k) k)))))\n1769\t\n1770\t\n1771\t(defn- rows-of\n1772\t  \"Every row of kind under n; install children too unless own-only.\"\n1773\t  [n kind own-only?]\n1774\t  (let [out (atom [])]\n1775\t    (letfn [(visit\n1776\t              [n]\n1777\t              (when (= kind (:kind n)) (swap! out conj n))\n1778\t              (doseq [[d x] (map vector (descriptors (:kind n) (:slots n)) (:slots n))]\n1779\t                (cond\n1780\t                  (and (ref? d) (= :task (:kind x))) (when-not own-only? (visit x))\n1781\t                  (ref? d) (visit x)\n1782\t                  (refs? d) (run! visit x)\n1783\t                  (and (value-slot? d) (vector? x) (= :row (first x))) (visit (second x))\n1784\t                  :else nil)))]\n1785\t      (visit n)\n1786\t      @out)))\n1787\t\n1788\t\n1789\t(defn- task-tree\n1790\t  \"[task role] for the root and every install child, pre-order.\"\n1791\t  [task role]\n1792\t  (into [[task role]] (mapcat #(task-tree (nth (:slots %) 4) :child)) (nth (:slots task) 12)))\n1793\t\n1794\t\n1795\t(defn- check-stores!\n1796\t  \"Step 7's task context, beside X1: no root or module store key is a\n1797\t   reserved name (Rule R), refused here rather than by restore's store-put.\"\n1798\t  [_recv task _role]\n1799\t  (let [[_ _ _ _ _ _ store module-stores] (:slots task)]\n1800\t    (doseq [s (cons store (map #(second (:slots %)) module-stores))\n1801\t            k (take-nth 2 (:slots s))]\n1802\t      (when (vm/reserved-name? k)\n1803\t        (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :reserved-name {:yin.k/role :store-key :yin.k/name k})))))\n1804\t\n1805\t\n1806\t(defn- attaches?\n1807\t  \"The receiving kernel admits vector v (its loader's validation), under\n1808\t   address a when a is given.\"\n1809\t  [recv v a]\n1810\t  (try (let [r (module/attach-module recv v)] (or (nil? a) (contains? (:code-aliases r) a)))\n1811\t       (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _e false)))\n1812\t\n1813\t\n1814\t(defn- check-install!\n1815\t  \"One install record: a phase the engine holds a carried child in, the\n1816\t   retained response link-install reads (status, manifest naming this\n1817\t   module, exports) with the image spawn-child loads, and a child that\n1818\t   is blocked: the engine links a halted child in the sweep it halts in.\"\n1819\t  [recv inst]\n1820\t  (let [[mn phase _ response child] (:slots inst)\n1821\t        manifest (when (map? response) (:manifest response))\n1822\t        child-kind (nth (:slots child) 2)]\n1823\t    (when-not (contains? #{:running :parked} phase)\n1824\t      (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :install-phase {:yin.k/name mn :yin.k/phase phase}))\n1825\t    (when-not (and (map? response) (= :ok (:status response)) (map? manifest)\n1826\t                   (= mn (:yin.module/name manifest))\n1827\t                   (coll? (:yin.module/exports manifest)) (every? symbol? (:yin.module/exports manifest))\n1828\t                   (map? (:image response)) (attaches? recv (:value (:image response)) nil))\n1829\t      (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :install-response {:yin.k/name mn}))\n1830\t    (when-not (= :blocked child-kind)\n1831\t      (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :install-child {:yin.k/name mn :yin.k/task-kind child-kind}))))\n1832\t\n1833\t\n1834\t(defn- check-pendings!\n1835\t  \"Step 8, pending and operations: role, kind, parked id, every :install\n1836\t   pending names a carried install, every install record.\"\n1837\t  [recv task role]\n1838\t  (let [[_ _ kind role' _ _ _ _ parked _ _ _ installs waits parked-id] (:slots task)]\n1839\t    (when-not (= role role') (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :role {:yin.k/role role'}))\n1840\t    (let [names (into #{} (map #(first (:slots %))) installs)]\n1841\t      (doseq [w waits]\n1842\t        (let [[reason n] (:slots (second (:slots w)))]\n1843\t          (when (and (= :install reason) (not (contains? names n)))\n1844\t            (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :incomplete-install {:yin.k/name n})))))\n1845\t    (case kind\n1846\t      :halted (when (seq waits) (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :kind {:yin.k/task-kind kind}))\n1847\t      :blocked (when (empty? waits) (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :kind {:yin.k/task-kind kind}))\n1848\t      :parked (when-not (some #(= parked-id %) (take-nth 2 (:slots parked)))\n1849\t                (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :parked-id {}))\n1850\t      (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :kind {:yin.k/task-kind kind}))\n1851\t    (run! #(check-install! recv %) installs)))\n1852\t\n1853\t\n1854\t(defn- check-closure!\n1855\t  \"A closure row names a :closure tuple of its carried vector: the entry\n1856\t   (:closure-origin) and that tuple's binders (:closure-binders), as\n1857\t   lower-closure will demand.\"\n1858\t  [code c]\n1859\t  (let [[a entry params] (:slots c)\n1860\t        v (get code a)\n1861\t        _ (when (nil? v) (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :segment {:yin.k/segment a}))\n1862\t        tuple (first (filter #(and (= :closure (nth % 0)) (= entry (nth % 3))) v))]\n1863\t    (cond\n1864\t      (nil? tuple) (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :closure-origin {:yin.k/segment a :yin.k/entry entry})\n1865\t      (not= params (nth tuple 2)) (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :closure-binders {:yin.k/segment a :yin.k/entry entry})\n1866\t      :else nil)))\n1867\t\n1868\t\n1869\t(defn- check-dependencies!\n1870\t  \"Step 9, dependency closure: requires and code agree, every segment has\n1871\t   its trees (§6.1), every closure's and frame's store-of names a module\n1872\t   store of this task (not a parent's or sibling's of the same key), every\n1873\t   segment is a vector the receiver's kernel admits under its A, every\n1874\t   closure names a closure of its code, every :prim is the receiver's.\"\n1875\t  [recv task _role]\n1876\t  (let [[_ _ _ _ _ _ _ module-stores _ _ requires code] (:slots task)]\n1877\t    (when-not (and (map? requires) (= (set (:yin.k/segments requires)) (set (keys code))))\n1878\t      (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :requires {}))\n1879\t    (let [trees (:yin.k/trees requires)\n1880\t          missing (into #{} (remove #(seq (get trees %))) (keys code))]\n1881\t      (when (seq missing)\n1882\t        (outcome! :yin.k/unsatisfied nil {:yin.k/discovery :incomplete :yin.k/missing {:yin.k/trees missing}})))\n1883\t    ;; §2.6: every store-of resolves to a module store this task carries\n1884\t    (let [census (into #{} (map #(first (:slots %))) module-stores)\n1885\t          missing (into #{} (comp (keep #(nth (:slots %) (if (= :closure (:kind %)) 4 1)))\n1886\t                                  (remove census))\n1887\t                        (concat (rows-of task :closure true) (rows-of task :env true)))]\n1888\t      (when (seq missing)\n1889\t        (outcome! :yin.k/unsatisfied nil {:yin.k/discovery :incomplete :yin.k/missing {:yin.k/stores missing}})))\n1890\t    (doseq [[a v] (sort-by #(str (key %)) code)]\n1891\t      (when-not (attaches? recv v a)\n1892\t        (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :segment {:yin.k/segment a})))\n1893\t    (run! #(check-closure! code %) (rows-of task :closure true))\n1894\t    (doseq [p (rows-of task :prim true)]\n1895\t      (when-not (contains? (:primitives recv) (first (:slots p)))\n1896\t        (outcome! :yin.k/unsatisfied nil {:yin.k/name (first (:slots p))})))))\n1897\t\n1898\t\n1899\t(defn- accept-grant!\n1900\t  \"The grant checks of a blocked or parked exclusive root (handoff.cljc's\n1901\t   accept-grant!, ported verbatim, keyed off the root's custody slot c and\n1902\t   the carrier's pack address): evidence, binding, lease, holder,\n1903\t   arbitration, epoch, tenure and the input prefix; then protection in both\n1904\t   directions over every stream row of the tree, and op-id presence equal\n1905\t   to enrollment on every retained write. Answers the custody state the\n1906\t   restored root holds, its counter the slot's exactly.\"\n1907\t  [task c address opts]\n1908\t  (let [grant (:grant opts)\n1909\t        evidence (:evidence grant)]\n1910\t    (when-not (and (or (nil? grant) (map? grant))\n1911\t                   (or (nil? evidence) (map? evidence)))\n1912\t      (throw (ex-info \"Malformed lower grant or evidence\" {})))\n1913\t    (when-not evidence\n1914\t      (outcome! :yin.k/awaiting-grant nil {}))\n1915\t    (when-not (= :yin.k/ready (:yin.k/status evidence))\n1916\t      (outcome! (if (= :yin.k/awaiting-grant (:yin.k/status evidence))\n1917\t                  :yin.k/awaiting-grant :yin.k/unsatisfied)\n1918\t                nil (dissoc evidence :yin.k/status)))\n1919\t    (let [binding (:yin.k/binding evidence)\n1920\t          prefix (:yin.k/prefix evidence)\n1921\t          tenure (:tenure grant)\n1922\t          occurrence (:yin.k/occurrence c)\n1923\t          lease (:dao.lease/lease grant)\n1924\t          holder (:dao.lease/holder grant)\n1925\t          frontier (:yin.k/frontier prefix)\n1926\t          records (:yin.k/inputs prefix)]\n1927\t      (when-not (and (map? binding) (map? tenure))\n1928\t        (throw (ex-info \"Malformed lower binding or tenure\" {})))\n1929\t      (when (or (nil? prefix) (:yin.k/status prefix))\n1930\t        (outcome! :yin.k/unsatisfied nil {:yin.k/reason (or (:yin.k/reason prefix) :unavailable)}))\n1931\t      (when-not (and (= (:checkpoint grant) address)\n1932\t                     (= occurrence (:yin.k/occurrence binding))\n1933\t                     (some? lease) (= lease (:dao.lease/lease binding))\n1934\t                     (some? holder) (= holder (:dao.lease/holder binding))\n1935\t                     (= (get-in c [:yin.k/arbitration :dao.stream/identity])\n1936\t                        (get-in binding [:yin.k/transaction :yin.k/arbitration]))\n1937\t                     (custody/exact? (:yin.k/epoch binding))\n1938\t                     (true? (:live tenure))\n1939\t                     (number? (:now tenure)) (number? (:bound tenure))\n1940\t                     (< (:now tenure) (:bound tenure))\n1941\t                     (= occurrence (:yin.k/occurrence prefix))\n1942\t                     (= lease (:dao.lease/lease prefix))\n1943\t                     (custody/exact? frontier) (vector? records)\n1944\t                     (= frontier (count records))\n1945\t                     (every? true? (map-indexed\n1946\t                                     (fn [index record]\n1947\t                                       (and (custody/exact? (:yin.k/input-seq record))\n1948\t                                            (= index (:yin.k/input-seq record))))\n1949\t                                     records)))\n1950\t        (outcome! :yin.k/not-holder nil {}))\n1951\t      (let [classes (:protection opts)\n1952\t            enrolled (:yin.k/enrolled evidence)]\n1953\t        (when-not (and (map? classes)\n1954\t                       (every? #{:enrolled :at-least-once :fail-stop} (vals classes))\n1955\t                       (set? enrolled))\n1956\t          (throw (ex-info \"Malformed lower protection or enrollment\" {})))\n1957\t        (doseq [s (rows-of task :stream false)]\n1958\t          (let [identity (first (:slots s))\n1959\t                class (get classes identity)]\n1960\t            (when-not (and class (= (= class :enrolled) (contains? enrolled identity)))\n1961\t              (outcome! :yin.k/unsatisfied nil {:dao.stream/identity identity}))))\n1962\t        (doseq [[t _] (task-tree task :root)\n1963\t                w (nth (:slots t) 13)\n1964\t                :let [ss (:slots (second (:slots w)))\n1965\t                      [ti _ oi] (get write-slots (first ss))]\n1966\t                :when ti]\n1967\t          (let [identity (first (:slots (nth ss ti)))]\n1968\t            (when-not (= (= :enrolled (get classes identity)) (some? (nth ss oi)))\n1969\t              (outcome! :yin.k/unsatisfied nil {:dao.stream/identity identity}))))\n1970\t        {:yin.k/occurrence occurrence\n1971\t         :dao.lease/lease lease :dao.lease/holder holder\n1972\t         :yin.k/epoch (:yin.k/epoch binding)\n1973\t         :yin.k/arbitration (:yin.k/arbitration c)\n1974\t         :yin.k/next-op-seq (:yin.k/next-op-seq c)\n1975\t         :protection classes :input {:next 0 :prefix prefix}\n1976\t         :tenure {:bound (:bound tenure)}}))))\n1977\t\n1978\t\n1979\t(defn- check-custody!\n1980\t  \"Step 10, once for the tree after the three staged checks: the custody\n1981\t   grammar (custody-baseline), then by the root's slot: a fork (nil) is\n1982\t   refused under :exclusive as :yin.k/profile-mismatch; an exclusive\n1983\t   blocked or parked root runs the grant checks unless :fenced (an\n1984\t   administrative rehydration: no grant, gate :exporting); a halted\n1985\t   exclusive root needs no grant and is gated :ended. Answers\n1986\t   {:exclusive? :fenced? :state}, which restore applies to every task.\"\n1987\t  [task wire opts]\n1988\t  (custody-baseline task)\n1989\t  (let [[_ _ kind] (:slots task) c (nth (:slots task) 16) fenced? (boolean (:fenced opts))]\n1990\t    (if (nil? c)\n1991\t      (do (when (:exclusive opts)\n1992\t            (outcome! :yin.k/profile-mismatch nil {:yin.k/policy :yin.k/exclusive}))\n1993\t          {:exclusive? false :fenced? fenced?})\n1994\t      {:exclusive? true :fenced? fenced?\n1995\t       :state (when-not (or fenced? (= :halted kind)) (accept-grant! task c (pack-address wire) opts))})))\n1996\t\n1997\t\n1998\t(defn- with-custody\n1999\t  \"Restore's custody for one task of the tree: an exclusive tree numbers\n2000\t   its retained :put waits (:yin.k/issue, :yin.k/issued, in carried\n2001\t   order) and gates :running, a halted exclusive root :ended, the root\n2002\t   holding the grant's custody state; a fenced tree gates :exporting with\n2003\t   its waits outside the scheduler (:yin.k/recovery-waits).\"\n2004\t  [m {:keys [exclusive? fenced? state]} kind root?]\n2005\t  (let [m (if exclusive?\n2006\t            (let [[entries issued] (reduce (fn [[acc i] e]\n2007\t                                             (if (= :put (:reason e))\n2008\t                                               [(conj acc (assoc e :yin.k/issue i)) (inc i)]\n2009\t                                               [(conj acc e) i]))\n2010\t                                           [[] 0] (:wait-set m))]\n2011\t              (cond-> (assoc m :wait-set entries :yin.k/issued issued\n2012\t                             :yin.k/gate (if (and root? (= :halted kind)) :ended :running))\n2013\t                (and root? (some? state)) (assoc :yin.k/custody state)))\n2014\t            m)]\n2015\t    (if fenced?\n2016\t      (assoc m :yin.k/gate :exporting :yin.k/recovery-waits (:wait-set m) :wait-set [])\n2017\t      m)))\n2018\t\n2019\t\n2020\t(defn- attach-streams!\n2021\t  \"Step 11: one attach per distinct stream identity of the whole tree.\"\n2022\t  [attach! task]\n2023\t  (reduce (fn [acc s]\n2024\t            (let [[identity descriptor] (:slots s)]\n2025\t              (if (contains? acc identity)\n2026\t                acc\n2027\t                (if-some [h (remote/lower-marker attach! {:dao.stream/descriptor descriptor})]\n2028\t                  (assoc acc identity h)\n2029\t                  (outcome! :yin.k/unsatisfied nil {:dao.stream/identity identity})))))\n2030\t          {} (rows-of task :stream false)))\n2031\t\n2032\t\n2033\t(defn- spawn-child\n2034\t  \"A fresh install child of recv's composition (the engine's spawn\n2035\t   discipline): answers [child recv'].\"\n2036\t  [recv response mn]\n2037\t  (let [n (or (:origins recv) 0)\n2038\t        origin (keyword (str (name (or (:origin recv) :t0)) \".\" n))\n2039\t        registry (reduce (fn [r [m e]] (module/assoc-module r m (dissoc e :bindings)))\n2040\t                         (:modules recv) (module/module-entries (:modules recv)))\n2041\t        source (:secret-source recv)]\n2042\t    [(module/spawn-module recv (:value (:image response))\n2043\t                          {:modules registry :origin origin\n2044\t                           :ancestry (conj (vec (:ancestry recv)) mn)\n2045\t                           :capability-secret (when (fn? source) (source origin))})\n2046\t     (assoc recv :origins (inc n))]))\n2047\t\n2048\t\n2049\t(defn- restore-task\n2050\t  \"Step 12 for one task: code by A, fresh resource keys, values re-sealed\n2051\t   under recv, waits as engine entries, parked records, installs, and the\n2052\t   custody check-custody! answered (with-custody).\"\n2053\t  [recv task handles custody root?]\n2054\t  (let [[_ _ kind _ id-counter free-env store module-stores parked census _ code installs waits parked-id result]\n2055\t        (:slots task)\n2056\t        base (reduce (fn [r [_ v]] (module/attach-module r v))\n2057\t                     (assoc recv :code {} :code-aliases {} :program nil)\n2058\t                     (sort-by #(str (key %)) code))\n2059\t        aliases (:code-aliases base)\n2060\t        used (atom (into fixed-resource-keys (keys (:resources base))))\n2061\t        identities (sort-by str (distinct (map #(first (:slots %)) (rows-of task :stream true))))\n2062\t        stream-keys (into {} (map (fn [identity] [identity (fresh-key! used)])) identities)\n2063\t        pairs (mapv vec (partition 2 (:slots census)))\n2064\t        cell-keys (into {} (map (fn [[c _]] [c (fresh-key! used)])) pairs)\n2065\t        bodies (into {} pairs)\n2066\t        stream-key #(get stream-keys (first (:slots %)))\n2067\t        parked-index (into {} (map vec) (partition 2 (:slots parked)))\n2068\t        cache (atom {})\n2069\t        resolving (atom #{})]\n2070\t    (letfn [(value\n2071\t              [v]\n2072\t              (case (first v)\n2073\t                :lit (second v)\n2074\t                :cursor-cell (engine/issue-ref base :cursor-ref (get cell-keys (second v)))\n2075\t                :row (row (second v))))\n2076\t            (row\n2077\t              [n]\n2078\t              (let [ss (:slots n)]\n2079\t                (case (:kind n)\n2080\t                  :vec (mapv value ss)\n2081\t                  :list (apply list (map value ss))\n2082\t                  :set (into #{} (map value) ss)\n2083\t                  :map (into {} (map (fn [[k x]] [(value k) (value x)])) (partition 2 ss))\n2084\t                  :prim (vm/primitive-function (get (:primitives base) (first ss)))\n2085\t                  :stream (engine/issue-ref base :stream-ref (stream-key n))\n2086\t                  :closure (let [[a entry params bindings store-of] ss]\n2087\t                             (module/lower-closure base\n2088\t                                                   (cond-> {:yin.k/binding :named\n2089\t                                                            :yin.k/format :yin.semantic-register/code\n2090\t                                                            :yin.k/segment a :yin.k/entry entry :yin.k/params params\n2091\t                                                            :yin.k/env (keyed bindings)}\n2092\t                                                     (some? store-of) (assoc :yin.k/store-of store-of))\n2093\t                                                   identity))\n2094\t                  :reified (values/continuation (:owner base) (assoc (payload (first ss)) :type :reified-continuation))\n2095\t                  :parked-ref (parked-record (first ss)))))\n2096\t            (keyed\n2097\t              [n]\n2098\t              (into {} (map (fn [[k x]] [k (value x)])) (partition 2 (:slots n))))\n2099\t            (env\n2100\t              [n]\n2101\t              (let [[b store-of] (:slots n)]\n2102\t                (cond-> (keyed b) (some? store-of) (assoc engine/store-of-key store-of))))\n2103\t            (k-of\n2104\t              [n]\n2105\t              (mapv (fn [f]\n2106\t                      (let [[a pc e w rd] (:slots f)]\n2107\t                        {:type :return :segment (get aliases a) :pc pc :env (env e) :window (keyed w) :rd rd}))\n2108\t                    (:slots n)))\n2109\t            (payload\n2110\t              [n]\n2111\t              (if (= :tail (:kind n))\n2112\t                (let [[a site k] (:slots n)]\n2113\t                  {:segment (get aliases a) :site site :k (k-of k) :deliver {:deliver :return}})\n2114\t                (let [[a pc e w k rd] (:slots n)]\n2115\t                  {:segment (get aliases a) :pc pc :env (env e) :window (keyed w) :k (k-of k)\n2116\t                   :deliver {:deliver :rd :rd rd}})))\n2117\t            (parked-record\n2118\t              [p]\n2119\t              (or (get @cache p)\n2120\t                  (do (when (contains? @resolving p)\n2121\t                        (outcome! :yin.k/non-portable :non-canonicalizable {:yin.k/hint :parked-cycle}))\n2122\t                      (swap! resolving conj p)\n2123\t                      (let [r (assoc (payload (get parked-index p)) :type :parked-continuation :id p)]\n2124\t                        (swap! cache assoc p r)\n2125\t                        (swap! resolving disj p)\n2126\t                        r))))\n2127\t            (cell-stream\n2128\t              [c]\n2129\t              (stream-key (first (:slots (get bodies c)))))\n2130\t            (entry\n2131\t              [w]\n2132\t              (let [[state pending] (:slots w)\n2133\t                    [reason & xs] (:slots pending)\n2134\t                    p (payload state)]\n2135\t                (case reason\n2136\t                  :next (assoc p :reason :next :stream-id (cell-stream (first xs))\n2137\t                               :cursor-ref {:type :cursor-ref :id (get cell-keys (first xs))})\n2138\t                  :ffi (let [[c call-id op] xs]\n2139\t                         (cond-> (assoc p :reason :next :stream-id (cell-stream c) :call-id call-id\n2140\t                                        :cursor-ref {:type :cursor-ref :id (get cell-keys c)})\n2141\t                           (some? op) (assoc :op op)))\n2142\t                  :put (let [[s v op-id] xs]\n2143\t                         (cond-> (assoc p :reason :put :stream-id (stream-key s) :datom (value v))\n2144\t                           (some? op-id) (assoc :op-id op-id)))\n2145\t                  :ffi-request (let [[call-id envelope req resp c op-id] xs\n2146\t                                     datom (value envelope)]\n2147\t                                 (cond-> (assoc p :reason :put :stream-id (stream-key req) :datom datom\n2148\t                                                :request-sent true :call-id call-id :op (apply2/request-op datom)\n2149\t                                                :response-cursor (get cell-keys c) :response-stream (stream-key resp))\n2150\t                                   (some? op-id) (assoc :op-id op-id)))\n2151\t                  (:link-request :link-response)\n2152\t                  (let [[link-id mn _ _ c envelope op-id] xs]\n2153\t                    (cond-> (assoc p :reason reason :link-id link-id :name mn\n2154\t                                   :request module/link-request-resource :response module/link-response-resource\n2155\t                                   :cursor (second (:slots (get bodies c))))\n2156\t                      (= :link-request reason) (assoc :envelope envelope)\n2157\t                      (some? op-id) (assoc :op-id op-id)))\n2158\t                  :install (assoc p :reason :install :name (first xs)))))]\n2159\t      (let [store' (reduce (fn [s [k v]] (engine/store-put s k (value v))) {} (partition 2 (:slots store)))\n2160\t            stores (into {} (map (fn [ms]\n2161\t                                   (let [[mid s] (:slots ms)]\n2162\t                                     [mid (into {} (map (fn [[k v]] [k (value v)])) (partition 2 (:slots s)))])))\n2163\t                         module-stores)\n2164\t            parked' (into {} (map (fn [[p _]] [p (parked-record p)])) parked-index)\n2165\t            entries (mapv entry waits)\n2166\t            link (some #(let [[reason _ _ req resp] (:slots (second (:slots %)))]\n2167\t                          (when (contains? #{:link-request :link-response} reason) [req resp]))\n2168\t                       waits)\n2169\t            [base installs'] (reduce (fn [[r acc] inst]\n2170\t                                       (let [[mn phase parent response child] (:slots inst)\n2171\t                                             [spawned r'] (spawn-child r response mn)]\n2172\t                                         [r' (assoc acc mn {:phase phase :parent parent :response response\n2173\t                                                            :vm (restore-task spawned child handles custody false)})]))\n2174\t                                     [base {}] installs)\n2175\t            fe (keyed free-env)\n2176\t            resources (merge (:resources base)\n2177\t                             (into {} (map (fn [[identity k]] [k (get handles identity)])) stream-keys)\n2178\t                             (into {} (map (fn [[c body]]\n2179\t                                             [(get cell-keys c) {:stream-id (stream-key (first (:slots body)))\n2180\t                                                                 :cursor (second (:slots body))}]))\n2181\t                                   pairs)\n2182\t                             (when-let [[req resp] link]\n2183\t                               {module/link-request-resource (get handles (first (:slots req)))\n2184\t                                module/link-response-resource (get handles (first (:slots resp)))}))\n2185\t            machine (assoc base :store store' :module-stores stores :parked parked' :installs installs'\n2186\t                           :resources resources :env fe :free-env fe :window {} :k nil :control nil\n2187\t                           :ready-queue [] :id-counter (max (or (:id-counter base) 0) id-counter))]\n2188\t        (with-custody\n2189\t          (case kind\n2190\t            :halted (assoc machine :halted? true :blocked? false :value (value result) :wait-set [])\n2191\t            :parked (assoc machine :halted? true :blocked? false :value (get parked' parked-id) :wait-set entries)\n2192\t            (assoc machine :halted? false :blocked? true :value :yin/blocked :wait-set entries))\n2193\t          custody kind root?)))))\n2194\t\n2195\t\n2196\t(defn lower-task\n2197\t  \"The lower of §7.2 into recv, a fresh semantic-register machine of the\n2198\t   receiver's composition: gate to frames (decode) and the store keys,\n2199\t   then pendings and install records, dependency closure (code, closures,\n2200\t   primitives), each step over the whole tree before the next, then\n2201\t   custody (check-custody!), all before the first attach! (step 11); then\n2202\t   restore (step 12), which therefore meets no carrier defect. Answers the\n2203\t   restored machine, or throws the first refusal as ex-data.\n2204\t   opts: :budget; :exclusive, refuse a fork root; :grant and :protection,\n2205\t   required by a blocked or parked exclusive root (handoff.cljc's reader\n2206\t   contract: the grant names :checkpoint, the pack address, its lease,\n2207\t   holder, tenure and evidence; :protection maps every stream identity of\n2208\t   the tree to its class); :fenced, an administrative rehydration that\n2209\t   skips the grant.\"\n2210\t  ([recv wire attach!] (lower-task recv wire attach! {}))\n2211\t  ([recv wire attach! opts]\n2212\t   (let [task (decode wire (merge default-budget (:budget opts)))]\n2213\t     (when-not (= :task (:kind task)) (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :root {}))\n2214\t     ;; each step over the whole tree before the next (§3.3)\n2215\t     (doseq [step [check-stores! check-pendings! check-dependencies!]\n2216\t             [t role] (task-tree task :root)]\n2217\t       (step recv t role))\n2218\t     (let [custody (check-custody! task wire opts)]\n2219\t       (restore-task recv task (attach-streams! attach! task) custody true)))))"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"108e1cb8-f707-457b-be14-6feb1e135c49","uuid":"f3ae8bdd-c5b0-4c6e-aa25-a9ced260db03","timestamp":"2026-10-13T10:02:56.099Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p7b/src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc","content":";; =============================================================================\n;; Custody (draft §5.5 as ruled, UCF 7.2.1, 7.4.3, 7.7.8; phase-7 plan §3.1, §3.3)\n;; =============================================================================\n;;\n;; The root's slot 16 is the custody arm as plain data, by kind: nil for a\n;; fork root of any kind (owner, 2026-10-13: the fork is never spelled);\n;; {:yin.k/policy :yin.k/exclusive :yin.k/occurrence :yin.k/arbitration\n;; :yin.k/next-op-seq} plus :yin.k/origin on a successor for a blocked or\n;; parked exclusive root; {:yin.k/origin} alone for a halted exclusive\n;; root; nil on every install child. No other key: lease, epoch and holder\n;; never enter a body. `custody-baseline` is the one grammar over a task's\n;; slot and its carried operation ids: the rows inspector\n;; (yin.vm.ucf.rows.checkpoint) answers it, lower-task's custody stage runs\n;; it before the grant checks, and lift-task runs it before emitting.\n;; Refusals are :yin.k/undecodable with a path relative to the root task:\n;; [:custody k] for the slot, [:frames i :op-id] for a wait's id, both\n;; prefixed by [:installs <name>] inside an install child.\n\n(def max-exact\n  \"2^52-1, the largest sequence or counter (7.7.8).\"\n  4503599627370495)\n\n\n(def ^:private custody-keys\n  #{:yin.k/policy :yin.k/occurrence :yin.k/arbitration :yin.k/next-op-seq :yin.k/origin})\n\n\n(def write-slots\n  \"Retained write reason -> [target payload op-id], indices into its\n   :pending row's slots (the reason at 0).\"\n  {:put [1 2 3] :ffi-request [3 2 6] :link-request [3 6 7]})\n\n\n(defn- custody-refuse!\n  [kind path]\n  (refuse! :yin.k/undecodable kind path))\n\n\n(defn- check-origin!\n  [c]\n  (let [origin (get c :yin.k/origin) p [:custody :yin.k/origin]]\n    (when-not (and (map? origin)\n                   (custody/occurrence? (get origin :yin.k/occurrence))\n                   (some? (get origin :dao.lease/lease))\n                   (some? (get origin :yin.k/emitter)))\n      (custody-refuse! :malformed-origin p))\n    (when (cbor/content= (get origin :yin.k/occurrence) (get c :yin.k/occurrence))\n      (custody-refuse! :origin-is-self (conj p :yin.k/occurrence)))))\n\n\n(defn- check-root-custody!\n  \"A non-nil root slot by kind: the version-1 header rules\n   (checkpoint.cljc's check-root-header!) on the slot's map.\"\n  [c kind]\n  (when-not (map? c) (custody-refuse! :malformed-custody [:custody]))\n  (when-some [k (first (sort-by str (remove custody-keys (keys c))))]\n    (custody-refuse! :custody-key [:custody k]))\n  (if (= :halted kind)\n    (do (doseq [k [:yin.k/policy :yin.k/occurrence :yin.k/arbitration :yin.k/next-op-seq]\n                :when (contains? c k)]\n          (custody-refuse! :halted-header [:custody k]))\n        (when-not (contains? c :yin.k/origin) (custody-refuse! :missing-header [:custody :yin.k/origin]))\n        (check-origin! c))\n    (do (doseq [k [:yin.k/policy :yin.k/occurrence :yin.k/arbitration :yin.k/next-op-seq]\n                :when (not (contains? c k))]\n          (custody-refuse! :missing-header [:custody k]))\n        (when-not (= :yin.k/exclusive (get c :yin.k/policy))\n          (custody-refuse! :policy [:custody :yin.k/policy]))\n        (when (nil? (get c :yin.k/occurrence)) (custody-refuse! :nil-occurrence [:custody :yin.k/occurrence]))\n        (when-not (custody/occurrence? (get c :yin.k/occurrence))\n          (custody-refuse! :malformed-occurrence [:custody :yin.k/occurrence]))\n        (let [arb (get c :yin.k/arbitration)]\n          (when-not (and (map? arb) (some? (get arb :dao.stream/identity)) (map? (get arb :dao.stream/descriptor)))\n            (custody-refuse! :malformed-arbitration [:custody :yin.k/arbitration])))\n        (let [n (get c :yin.k/next-op-seq)]\n          (when-not (custody/exact? n) (custody-refuse! :inexact [:custody :yin.k/next-op-seq]))\n          (when (and (not (contains? c :yin.k/origin)) (not (cbor/num= 0 n)))\n            (custody-refuse! :first-export-counter [:custody :yin.k/next-op-seq])))\n        (when (contains? c :yin.k/origin) (check-origin! c)))))\n\n\n(defn- check-op-id!\n  \"One carried id against the root context: its shape, an origin present,\n   never the root's own occurrence, below the root counter (checkpoint.cljc's\n   check-op-id!, verbatim).\"\n  [ctx op-id p]\n  (when-not (and (map? op-id) (= 2 (count op-id))\n                 (custody/occurrence? (get op-id :yin.k/occurrence))\n                 (contains? op-id :yin.k/seq))\n    (custody-refuse! :malformed-op-id p))\n  (when-not (custody/exact? (get op-id :yin.k/seq)) (custody-refuse! :inexact (conj p :yin.k/seq)))\n  (when-not (contains? ctx :yin.k/origin) (custody-refuse! :op-id-without-origin p))\n  (when (cbor/content= (get op-id :yin.k/occurrence) (get ctx :yin.k/occurrence))\n    (custody-refuse! :op-id-own-occurrence p))\n  ;; a :halted root has no counter, so no id can be below it\n  (when-not (and (contains? ctx :yin.k/next-op-seq)\n                 (neg? (cbor/num-compare (get op-id :yin.k/seq) (get ctx :yin.k/next-op-seq))))\n    (custody-refuse! :op-seq-range (conj p :yin.k/seq))))\n\n\n(defn- wire-slot\n  \"A V slot as the wire holds it: a [:row n] is [:row id].\"\n  [x]\n  (if (and (vector? x) (= :row (first x))) [:row (first (emit-node (second x) {} {}))] x))\n\n\n(defn- task-ops\n  \"[path op-id intent] of every id the waits of task carry, then of each\n   install child in carried (module-name) order, in the root's context.\n   Checks each task's kind and role, each :install pending's install row,\n   and that a child's custody slot is nil.\"\n  [ctx task role path]\n  (let [[_ _ kind role' _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ installs waits] (:slots task)\n        names (into #{} (map #(first (:slots %))) installs)]\n    (when-not (contains? #{:blocked :parked :halted} kind) (custody-refuse! :kind (conj path :kind)))\n    (when-not (= role role') (custody-refuse! :role (conj path :role)))\n    (into (into []\n                (keep-indexed\n                  (fn [i w]\n                    (let [ss (:slots (second (:slots w)))\n                          reason (first ss)\n                          p (conj path :frames i)]\n                      (when (and (= :install reason) (not (contains? names (second ss))))\n                        (custody-refuse! :incomplete-install p))\n                      (when-let [[t payload o] (get write-slots reason)]\n                        (when-some [op-id (nth ss o)]\n                          (let [p (conj p :op-id)]\n                            (when (::fork ctx) (custody-refuse! :fork-op-id p))\n                            (check-op-id! ctx op-id p)\n                            [p op-id [:yin.k/append (first (:slots (nth ss t))) (wire-slot (nth ss payload))]]))))))\n                waits)\n          (mapcat (fn [inst]\n                    (let [[mn _ _ _ child] (:slots inst)\n                          p (conj path :installs mn)]\n                      (when (some? (nth (:slots child) 16)) (custody-refuse! :child-header (conj p :custody)))\n                      (task-ops ctx child :child p))))\n          installs)))\n\n\n(defn custody-baseline\n  \"The operation baseline of root task (decoded, or abstract before emit),\n   or the first refusal thrown as ex-data {:yin.k/status :yin.k/undecodable\n   :yin.k/kind :yin.k/path}. Answers {:yin.k/kind k :yin.k/ops {op-id\n   digest}} plus the slot's :yin.k/occurrence, :yin.k/origin,\n   :yin.k/arbitration and :yin.k/next-op-seq, or :yin.k/fork true for a nil\n   slot, whose tree carries no id. digest is the BLAKE3 hex of the canonical\n   bytes of [:yin.k/append target-identity payload], the payload as the wire\n   slot holds it ([:lit x], [:row id], or a :link-request's plain envelope).\"\n  [task]\n  (let [slots (:slots task) kind (nth slots 2) c (nth slots 16) fork? (nil? c)]\n    (when-not (contains? #{:blocked :parked :halted} kind) (custody-refuse! :kind [:kind]))\n    (when-not fork? (check-root-custody! c kind))\n    (let [ctx (cond-> (select-keys c [:yin.k/occurrence :yin.k/origin :yin.k/next-op-seq]) fork? (assoc ::fork true))\n          ops (reduce (fn [acc [p op-id in]]\n                        (let [k (cbor/content-key op-id)]\n                          (when (contains? (:seen acc) k) (custody-refuse! :duplicate-op-id p))\n                          (-> acc (update :seen conj k)\n                              (assoc-in [:ops op-id] (jing/digest-bytes :blake3 (cbor/encode in))))))\n                      {:seen #{} :ops {}}\n                      (task-ops ctx task :root []))]\n      (cond-> (merge (select-keys c [:yin.k/occurrence :yin.k/origin :yin.k/arbitration :yin.k/next-op-seq])\n                     {:yin.k/kind kind :yin.k/ops (:ops ops)})\n        fork? (assoc :yin.k/fork true)))))\n\n\n(defn pack-address\n  \"The storage identity of a carrier: the BLAKE3 segment address of its\n   canonical bytes, distinct from the semantic root id it carries (§3.3).\"\n  [wire]\n  (jing/segment-key wire))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Task transport (continuation design §7): lift-task and lower-task\n;; =============================================================================\n;;\n;; The lift walks a quiescent semantic-register machine into the abstract\n;; task the codec above emits: waits, parked records, the store, module\n;; stores, the free environment, the result and install children, every\n;; value classified as [:lit x], [:row n] or [:cursor-cell source]. A\n;; cursor cell's source is the resource id of a cursor reference, or\n;; [response-resource position] for a link wait's kept response cursor,\n;; so one resource reached twice is one cursor cell. The lower decodes the\n;; carrier (gate to frames, §3.3), checks pendings, dependencies and\n;; custody for every task of the tree, and only then attaches streams and\n;; restores state. Restoration delivers nothing, runs nothing.\n\n(defn- outcome!\n  [status kind data]\n  (throw (ex-info \"Task transport refused\"\n                  (merge data (cond-> {:yin.k/status status}\n                                (some? kind) (assoc :yin.k/kind kind))))))\n\n\n(defn- unliftable-hold\n  \"The first hold of m with no wire pending (UCF 7.4.1, 7.4.3), or nil.\"\n  [m]\n  (let [waits (:wait-set m)\n        cells (filter map? (vals (:resources m)))\n        held? #(and (map? %) (contains? % :yin.k/held))]\n    (cond\n      (some #(= :observe (:reason %)) waits) :observe\n      (or (some held? waits) (some held? cells)) :held\n      (some :yin.k/unminted cells) :unminted-cursor\n      (seq (:yin.k/closes m)) :pending-close\n      (some #(and (= :link-request (:reason %)) (not (contains? % :cursor))) waits)\n      :link-cursor-not-installed\n      :else nil)))\n\n\n(defn- stream-row!\n  \"The :stream row of resource sid, served once per resource.\"\n  [ctx sid]\n  (or (get-in @(:acc ctx) [:streams sid])\n      (let [h (get (:resources (:m ctx)) sid)]\n        (when (nil? h)\n          (outcome! :yin.k/non-portable :forged-resource-reference {:yin.k/hint sid}))\n        (let [marker (remote/lift-marker (:serve! ctx) h)]\n          (when (nil? marker) (outcome! :yin.k/unsatisfied nil {}))\n          (let [n (node :stream [(:dao.stream/identity marker) (:dao.stream/descriptor marker)])]\n            (swap! (:acc ctx) assoc-in [:streams sid] n)\n            n)))))\n\n\n(defn- cell!\n  [ctx source sid position]\n  (when-not (contains? (:cells @(:acc ctx)) source)\n    (let [stream (stream-row! ctx sid)]\n      (swap! (:acc ctx) assoc-in [:cells source] (node :cursor-cell-body [stream position]))))\n  source)\n\n\n(defn- cell-for!\n  [ctx cid]\n  (let [cell (get (:resources (:m ctx)) cid)]\n    (when-not (and (map? cell) (contains? cell :stream-id))\n      (outcome! :yin.k/non-portable :forged-resource-reference {:yin.k/hint cid}))\n    (cell! ctx cid (:stream-id cell) (:cursor cell))))\n\n\n(defn- address!\n  [ctx seg]\n  (if-some [a (get-in (:m ctx) [:code seg :address])]\n    (do (swap! (:acc ctx) update :segments conj a) a)\n    (outcome! :yin.k/non-portable :unaddressed-segment {:yin.k/hint seg})))\n\n\n(defn- scalar-literal?\n  [x]\n  (or (nil? x) (boolean? x) (string? x) (keyword? x) (symbol? x) (number? x)\n      (and (not (cbor/byte-payload? x)) (cbor/numeric? x))))\n\n\n(defn- primitive-name\n  [ctx f]\n  (let [m (:m ctx)\n        n (vm/name-of (:primitives m) (or (:primitive-canonical-names m) {}) f)\n        profile (when (symbol? n) (vm/profile-of (:primitives m) n))]\n    (cond\n      (nil? n) (outcome! :yin.k/non-portable :unnamed-function {})\n      (not (symbol? n)) (outcome! :yin.k/non-portable :ambiguous-primitive {})\n      (= :host (:yin.k/class profile)) (outcome! :yin.k/non-portable :host-state-primitive {:yin.k/name n})\n      :else n)))\n\n\n(declare lift-value state-node)\n\n\n(defn- collection-value\n  \"A guest collection: a literal when no member is a reference.\"\n  [ctx kind members original]\n  (let [vs (mapv #(lift-value ctx %) members)]\n    (if (every? #(= :lit (first %)) vs) [:lit original] [:row (node kind vs)])))\n\n\n(defn- bindings-node\n  [ctx e]\n  (node :bindings (mapcat (fn [[k v]] [k (lift-value ctx v)]) e)))\n\n\n(defn- context!\n  \"Record that segment a can run from pc at under environment e: a\n   closure's entry, an :act's or a return frame's pc (§7.1's discharge).\"\n  [ctx a at e]\n  (swap! (:acc ctx) update :contexts conj {:a a :at at :env (or e {})}))\n\n\n(defn- store-of!\n  [ctx e]\n  (let [store-of (engine/env-store-of e)]\n    (when (some? store-of) (swap! (:acc ctx) update :stores conj store-of))\n    store-of))\n\n\n(defn- lift-env-node\n  [ctx e]\n  (let [e (or e {})]\n    (node :env [(bindings-node ctx (engine/without-store-of e)) (store-of! ctx e)])))\n\n\n(defn- closure-node\n  [ctx c]\n  (let [e (or (:env c) {})\n        a (address! ctx (:segment c))]\n    (context! ctx a (:entry c) e)\n    (node :closure [a (:entry c) (vec (:params c))\n                    (bindings-node ctx (engine/without-store-of e)) (store-of! ctx e)])))\n\n\n(defn- lift-value\n  \"One machine value as a carrier value: [:lit x], [:row n] or\n   [:cursor-cell source]. A reference is authenticated before it is\n   encoded; a foreign value, a heap cell and a host object refuse.\"\n  [ctx x]\n  (let [m (:m ctx)]\n    (cond\n      (values/host-typed? x)\n      (cond\n        (not (values/owned-by? x (:owner m)))\n        (outcome! :yin.k/non-portable :foreign-value {:yin.k/hint (values/kind-of x)})\n        (values/closure? x) [:row (closure-node ctx (values/payload x))]\n        (values/continuation? x) [:row (node :reified [(state-node ctx (values/payload x))])]\n        :else (outcome! :yin.k/non-portable :non-canonicalizable {:yin.k/hint (values/kind-of x)}))\n      (fn? x) [:row (node :prim [(primitive-name ctx x)])]\n      (map? x)\n      (case (:type x)\n        :stream-ref (if (engine/authentic-ref? m :stream-ref x)\n                      [:row (stream-row! ctx (:id x))]\n                      (outcome! :yin.k/non-portable :forged-resource-reference {:yin.k/hint :stream-ref}))\n        :cursor-ref (if (engine/authentic-ref? m :cursor-ref x)\n                      [:cursor-cell (cell-for! ctx (:id x))]\n                      (outcome! :yin.k/non-portable :forged-resource-reference {:yin.k/hint :cursor-ref}))\n        :parked-continuation (if (contains? (:parked m) (:id x))\n                               [:row (node :parked-ref [(:id x)])]\n                               (outcome! :yin.k/non-portable :inconsistent-state {:yin.k/hint :parked-reference}))\n        :cell-ref (outcome! :yin.k/non-portable :cell {:yin.k/hint (:id x)})\n        (collection-value ctx :map (mapcat identity x) x))\n      (vector? x) (collection-value ctx :vec x x)\n      (set? x) (collection-value ctx :set (vec x) x)\n      (seq? x) (collection-value ctx :list (vec x) x)\n      (scalar-literal? x) [:lit x]\n      :else (outcome! :yin.k/non-portable :host-object {}))))\n\n\n(defn- window-node\n  [ctx w]\n  (node :window (mapcat (fn [[r v]] [r (lift-value ctx v)]) w)))\n\n\n(defn- k-node\n  [ctx k]\n  (node :k (mapv (fn [f]\n                   (let [a (address! ctx (:segment f))]\n                     (context! ctx a (:pc f) (:env f))\n                     (node :kframe [a (:pc f) (lift-env-node ctx (:env f))\n                                    (window-node ctx (:window f)) (:rd f)])))\n                 (or k []))))\n\n\n(defn- state-node\n  \"An evaluator payload (wait entry, parked record, reified payload) as\n   its :act or :tail row; engine fields are the pending's.\"\n  [ctx p]\n  (if (contains? p :site)\n    ;; a tail state resumes through its K: its own segment never runs again\n    (node :tail [(address! ctx (:segment p)) (:site p) (k-node ctx (:k p))])\n    (let [a (address! ctx (:segment p))]\n      (context! ctx a (:pc p) (:env p))\n      (node :act [a (:pc p) (lift-env-node ctx (:env p))\n                  (window-node ctx (:window p)) (k-node ctx (:k p)) (get-in p [:deliver :rd])]))))\n\n\n(defn- pending-node\n  \"The observed wait's pending (draft §5.3): the reason is the entry's,\n   never the site's static kind.\"\n  [ctx e]\n  (let [m (:m ctx)]\n    (case (:reason e)\n      :next (if (contains? e :call-id)\n              (node :pending [:ffi (cell-for! ctx (get-in e [:cursor-ref :id])) (:call-id e) (:op e)])\n              (node :pending [:next (cell-for! ctx (get-in e [:cursor-ref :id]))]))\n      :put (if (:request-sent e)\n             (let [carried? (and (:response-cursor e) (:response-stream e))\n                   cursor (if carried? (:response-cursor e) vm/call-out-cursor-key)\n                   response (if carried? (:response-stream e) vm/call-out-stream-key)]\n               (when-not (get (:resources m) cursor) (outcome! :yin.k/unsatisfied nil {}))\n               (node :pending [:ffi-request (:call-id e) (lift-value ctx (:datom e)) (stream-row! ctx (:stream-id e))\n                               (stream-row! ctx response) (cell-for! ctx cursor) (:op-id e)]))\n             (do (when-not (contains? e :datom) (outcome! :yin.k/non-portable :incomplete-write {}))\n                 (node :pending [:put (stream-row! ctx (:stream-id e)) (lift-value ctx (:datom e)) (:op-id e)])))\n      (:link-request :link-response)\n      (let [c (cell! ctx [(:response e) (:cursor e)] (:response e) (:cursor e))\n            base [(:reason e) (:link-id e) (:name e) (stream-row! ctx (:request e)) (stream-row! ctx (:response e)) c]]\n        (node :pending (if (= :link-request (:reason e)) (conj base (:envelope e) (:op-id e)) base)))\n      :install (do (when-not (contains? (:installs m) (:name e))\n                     (outcome! :yin.k/non-portable :incomplete-install {:yin.k/name (:name e)}))\n                   (node :pending [:install (:name e)]))\n      (outcome! :yin.k/non-portable :reason-mismatch {:yin.k/reason (:reason e)}))))\n\n\n(defn- store-node\n  [ctx s]\n  (node :store (mapcat (fn [[k v]]\n                         (when-not (= :lit (first (lift-value ctx k)))\n                           (outcome! :yin.k/non-portable :store-key {}))\n                         [k (lift-value ctx v)])\n                       s)))\n\n\n(defn- module-store-nodes\n  \"Every module store an environment or closure reaches, transitively.\"\n  [ctx]\n  (loop [done {}]\n    (if-let [mid (first (sort-by str (remove #(contains? done %) (:stores @(:acc ctx)))))]\n      (let [stores (:module-stores (:m ctx))]\n        (when-not (contains? stores mid)\n          (outcome! :yin.k/non-portable :missing-module-store {:yin.k/hint mid}))\n        (recur (assoc done mid (node :module-store [mid (store-node ctx (get stores mid))]))))\n      (mapv val (sort-by #(str (key %)) done)))))\n\n\n(defn- installing-names\n  [m]\n  (into #{} (mapcat (fn [[mn inst]]\n                      (map #(symbol (name mn) (name %))\n                           (get-in inst [:response :manifest :yin.module/exports]))))\n        (:installs m)))\n\n\n(defn live-pcs\n  \"The pcs of v control flow can still reach from at: the successor\n   relation (§8.1), so a backward jump makes earlier code live, and from\n   each reachable :closure its body from the entry, since reachable code\n   can still construct it.\"\n  [v at]\n  (loop [seen #{at}\n         todo [at]]\n    (if-let [p (peek todo)]\n      (let [t (nth v p)\n            fresh (remove seen (cond-> (analysis/successors v p)\n                                 (= :closure (nth t 0)) (conj (nth t 3))))]\n        (recur (into seen fresh) (into (pop todo) fresh)))\n      seen)))\n\n\n(defn- discharge!\n  \"The dependency closure over the v4 vectors (§7.1), after the walk that\n   found the contexts: every free occurrence control flow can still reach\n   from a carried context (live-pcs) is answered there, in resolve-var's\n   order: that context's\n   E, then the one store engine/active-store selects for it (the root\n   store, or the module store its store-of names; both travel), then a\n   primitive, an installing module's export, the module registry. Else\n   the lift is :yin.k/unsatisfied, discovery :incomplete.\"\n  [ctx code]\n  (let [m (:m ctx)\n        installing (installing-names m)\n        answered? (fn [sym e]\n                    (let [store-of (engine/env-store-of e)\n                          store (if (some? store-of) (get (:module-stores m) store-of {}) (:store m))]\n                      (or (vm/reserved-name? sym) (contains? e sym) (contains? store sym)\n                          (let [profile (vm/profile-of (:primitives m) sym)]\n                            (when (= :host (:yin.k/class profile))\n                              (outcome! :yin.k/non-portable :host-state-primitive {:yin.k/name sym}))\n                            (or (some? profile) (contains? installing sym)\n                                (and (some? (namespace sym))\n                                     (some? (module/resolve-module (:modules m)\n                                                                   (symbol (str (namespace sym) \".\" (name sym)))))))))))\n        scanned (into {} (map (fn [[a v]] [a (scan/free-occurrences v)])) code)\n        missing (into #{}\n                      (mapcat (fn [{:keys [a at env]}]\n                                (let [live (live-pcs (get code a) at)]\n                                  (keep (fn [o]\n                                          (when (and (contains? live (:at o))\n                                                     (not (answered? (:name o) env)))\n                                            (:name o)))\n                                        (get scanned a)))))\n                      (:contexts @(:acc ctx)))]\n    (when (seq missing)\n      (outcome! :yin.k/unsatisfied nil {:yin.k/discovery :incomplete :yin.k/missing {:obligations missing}}))))\n\n\n(declare lift-task*)\n\n\n(defn- install-node\n  [ctx mn inst opts]\n  (let [{:keys [phase parent response]} inst]\n    (when-not (contains? #{:running :parked} phase)\n      (outcome! :yin.k/non-portable :incomplete-install {:yin.k/name mn :yin.k/phase phase}))\n    (when-not (try (cbor/encode response) true\n                   (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _e false))\n      (outcome! :yin.k/non-portable :install-response {:yin.k/name mn}))\n    (node :install [mn phase parent response\n                    (lift-task* (:vm inst) (:serve! ctx) (dissoc opts :free-env) :child)])))\n\n\n(defn- lift-task*\n  [m serve! opts role]\n  (when (seq (:ready-queue m))\n    (outcome! :yin.k/not-quiescent nil {:yin.k/ready (count (:ready-queue m))}))\n  (when-some [h (unliftable-hold m)]\n    (outcome! :yin.k/non-portable :reason-mismatch {:yin.k/hold h}))\n  (when (some? (:control m))\n    (outcome! :yin.k/not-at-safepoint nil {:yin.k/pc (get-in m [:control :pc])}))\n  (let [value (:value m)\n        active? (and (map? value) (= :parked-continuation (:type value)) (contains? (:parked m) (:id value)))\n        kind (cond active? :parked\n                   (seq (:wait-set m)) :blocked\n                   (engine/halted-with-empty-queue? m) :halted\n                   :else (outcome! :yin.k/not-at-safepoint nil {}))\n        ;; §6.3: the explicit argument overrides the kernel's retained field\n        free-env (cond (some? (:free-env opts)) (:free-env opts)\n                       (some? (:free-env m)) (:free-env m)\n                       :else (outcome! :yin.k/non-portable :missing-free-env {}))\n        ctx {:m m :serve! serve! :acc (atom {:streams {} :cells {} :stores #{} :segments #{} :contexts #{}})}\n        free-node (bindings-node ctx free-env)\n        waits (mapv (fn [e] (node :wait [(state-node ctx e) (pending-node ctx e)])) (:wait-set m))\n        parked (node :parked-table (mapcat (fn [[p rec]] [p (state-node ctx rec)]) (:parked m)))\n        store (store-node ctx (:store m))\n        result (when (= :halted kind) (lift-value ctx value))\n        installs (mapv (fn [[mn inst]] (install-node ctx mn inst opts)) (sort-by #(str (key %)) (:installs m)))\n        module-stores (module-store-nodes ctx)\n        acc @(:acc ctx)\n        segments (:segments acc)\n        code (into {} (map (fn [a]\n                             (if-some [v (get-in m [:code (get (:code-aliases m) a) :vector])]\n                               [a v]\n                               (outcome! :yin.k/unsatisfied nil {:yin.k/segment a}))))\n                   segments)\n        _ (discharge! ctx code)\n        index (or (:source-index opts) {})\n        missing-trees (into #{} (remove #(seq (get index %))) segments)\n        _ (when (seq missing-trees)\n            (outcome! :yin.k/unsatisfied nil {:yin.k/discovery :incomplete :yin.k/missing {:yin.k/trees missing-trees}}))\n        requires {:yin.k/cursor-profiles (if (seq (:cells acc)) remote/cursor-profiles #{})\n                  :yin.k/segments segments\n                  :yin.k/trees (select-keys index segments)}\n        task (node :task [3 profile kind role (or (:id-counter m) 0) free-node store module-stores parked\n                          (node :cursor-cells (mapcat identity (:cells acc))) requires code installs waits\n                          (when (= :parked kind) (:id value)) result nil])]\n    ;; §3.3: a frame the evaluator itself minted that fails is inconsistent\n    (when-let [d (validate-frames task)]\n      (outcome! :yin.k/non-portable :inconsistent-state {:yin.k/defect d}))\n    task))\n\n\n(declare task-tree)\n\n\n(defn- header-custody\n  \"The root's custody slot from the caller's header, by kind: blocked or\n   parked takes the occurrence, arbitration, counter and the exclusive\n   policy, and the origin when the header names one; halted the origin\n   alone (an empty map without one, which the grammar refuses). A nil\n   value is an absent key (handoff.cljc's header-of).\"\n  [header kind]\n  (into {}\n        (filter (comp some? val))\n        (if (= :halted kind)\n          (select-keys header [:yin.k/origin])\n          (assoc (select-keys header [:yin.k/occurrence :yin.k/arbitration :yin.k/next-op-seq :yin.k/origin])\n                 :yin.k/policy :yin.k/exclusive))))\n\n\n(defn- protect!\n  \"Every retained write of the tree under the header's enrolled set (UCF\n   7.4.3, 7.7.8; handoff.cljc's protected!): an enrolled target without an\n   operation id is :unprotected-pending, an id on an unenrolled target is\n   :yin.k/unsatisfied naming the stream.\"\n  [task enrolled]\n  (doseq [[t _] (task-tree task :root)\n          w (nth (:slots t) 13)]\n    (let [ss (:slots (second (:slots w)))]\n      (when-let [[ti _ oi] (get write-slots (first ss))]\n        (let [identity (first (:slots (nth ss ti)))\n              enrolled? (contains? enrolled identity)\n              carried? (some? (nth ss oi))]\n          (cond\n            (and enrolled? (not carried?))\n            (outcome! :yin.k/non-portable :unprotected-pending {:dao.stream/identity identity})\n            (and carried? (not enrolled?))\n            (outcome! :yin.k/unsatisfied nil {:dao.stream/identity identity})\n            :else nil))))))\n\n\n(defn lift-task\n  \"The lift of §7.1: quiescent semantic-register machine m as a version-3\n   carrier, or a refusal thrown as ex-data {:yin.k/status :yin.k/kind}.\n   serve! is the exporter's remote-table entry (yin.vm.ucf.remote).\n   opts: :free-env, the task's initial free environment (default: the\n   kernel's retained :free-env field; the explicit value overrides it);\n   :source-index, {A #{tree-address}} the composition knows (§6.1), which\n   must cover every carried segment; :budget, the numbering budget;\n   :header, the exclusive custody header (occurrence, arbitration,\n   next-op-seq, origin when the task has a predecessor, and\n   :yin.k/enrolled, the enrolled stream identities, a lift input that\n   never travels). No header is the fork: custody nil. A header writes the\n   root's slot by kind (header-custody), refuses :op-seq-exhausted at\n   2^52-1 on a blocked or parked root, and protects every retained write\n   of the tree (protect!). Before emitting, the lift runs custody-baseline\n   over the task, so it never emits a carrier the inspector refuses.\"\n  ([m serve!] (lift-task m serve! {}))\n  ([m serve! opts]\n   (let [opts (or opts {})\n         header (:header opts)\n         task (lift-task* m serve! opts :root)\n         kind (nth (:slots task) 2)\n         task (if (nil? header)\n                task\n                (let [n (:yin.k/next-op-seq header)]\n                  (when (and (not= :halted kind) (cbor/numeric? n) (cbor/num= n max-exact))\n                    (outcome! :yin.k/non-portable :op-seq-exhausted {:yin.k/next-op-seq n}))\n                  (protect! task (or (:yin.k/enrolled header) #{}))\n                  (assoc-in task [:slots 16] (header-custody header kind))))]\n     (custody-baseline task)\n     (emit task (merge default-budget (:budget opts))))))\n\n\n(def ^:private fixed-resource-keys\n  #{vm/call-in-stream-key vm/call-out-stream-key vm/call-out-cursor-key\n    module/link-request-resource module/link-response-resource})\n\n\n(defn- fresh-key!\n  [used]\n  (loop [n (inc (count @used))]\n    (let [k (keyword \"yin.k\" (str \"k-\" n))]\n      (if (contains? @used k) (recur (inc n)) (do (swap! used conj k) k)))))\n\n\n(defn- rows-of\n  \"Every row of kind under n; install children too unless own-only.\"\n  [n kind own-only?]\n  (let [out (atom [])]\n    (letfn [(visit\n              [n]\n              (when (= kind (:kind n)) (swap! out conj n))\n              (doseq [[d x] (map vector (descriptors (:kind n) (:slots n)) (:slots n))]\n                (cond\n                  (and (ref? d) (= :task (:kind x))) (when-not own-only? (visit x))\n                  (ref? d) (visit x)\n                  (refs? d) (run! visit x)\n                  (and (value-slot? d) (vector? x) (= :row (first x))) (visit (second x))\n                  :else nil)))]\n      (visit n)\n      @out)))\n\n\n(defn- task-tree\n  \"[task role] for the root and every install child, pre-order.\"\n  [task role]\n  (into [[task role]] (mapcat #(task-tree (nth (:slots %) 4) :child)) (nth (:slots task) 12)))\n\n\n(defn- check-stores!\n  \"Step 7's task context, beside X1: no root or module store key is a\n   reserved name (Rule R), refused here rather than by restore's store-put.\"\n  [_recv task _role]\n  (let [[_ _ _ _ _ _ store module-stores] (:slots task)]\n    (doseq [s (cons store (map #(second (:slots %)) module-stores))\n            k (take-nth 2 (:slots s))]\n      (when (vm/reserved-name? k)\n        (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :reserved-name {:yin.k/role :store-key :yin.k/name k})))))\n\n\n(defn- attaches?\n  \"The receiving kernel admits vector v (its loader's validation), under\n   address a when a is given.\"\n  [recv v a]\n  (try (let [r (module/attach-module recv v)] (or (nil? a) (contains? (:code-aliases r) a)))\n       (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _e false)))\n\n\n(defn- check-install!\n  \"One install record: a phase the engine holds a carried child in, the\n   retained response link-install reads (status, manifest naming this\n   module, exports) with the image spawn-child loads, and a child that\n   is blocked: the engine links a halted child in the sweep it halts in.\"\n  [recv inst]\n  (let [[mn phase _ response child] (:slots inst)\n        manifest (when (map? response) (:manifest response))\n        child-kind (nth (:slots child) 2)]\n    (when-not (contains? #{:running :parked} phase)\n      (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :install-phase {:yin.k/name mn :yin.k/phase phase}))\n    (when-not (and (map? response) (= :ok (:status response)) (map? manifest)\n                   (= mn (:yin.module/name manifest))\n                   (coll? (:yin.module/exports manifest)) (every? symbol? (:yin.module/exports manifest))\n                   (map? (:image response)) (attaches? recv (:value (:image response)) nil))\n      (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :install-response {:yin.k/name mn}))\n    (when-not (= :blocked child-kind)\n      (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :install-child {:yin.k/name mn :yin.k/task-kind child-kind}))))\n\n\n(defn- check-pendings!\n  \"Step 8, pending and operations: role, kind, parked id, every :install\n   pending names a carried install, every install record.\"\n  [recv task role]\n  (let [[_ _ kind role' _ _ _ _ parked _ _ _ installs waits parked-id] (:slots task)]\n    (when-not (= role role') (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :role {:yin.k/role role'}))\n    (let [names (into #{} (map #(first (:slots %))) installs)]\n      (doseq [w waits]\n        (let [[reason n] (:slots (second (:slots w)))]\n          (when (and (= :install reason) (not (contains? names n)))\n            (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :incomplete-install {:yin.k/name n})))))\n    (case kind\n      :halted (when (seq waits) (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :kind {:yin.k/task-kind kind}))\n      :blocked (when (empty? waits) (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :kind {:yin.k/task-kind kind}))\n      :parked (when-not (some #(= parked-id %) (take-nth 2 (:slots parked)))\n                (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :parked-id {}))\n      (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :kind {:yin.k/task-kind kind}))\n    (run! #(check-install! recv %) installs)))\n\n\n(defn- check-closure!\n  \"A closure row names a :closure tuple of its carried vector: the entry\n   (:closure-origin) and that tuple's binders (:closure-binders), as\n   lower-closure will demand.\"\n  [code c]\n  (let [[a entry params] (:slots c)\n        v (get code a)\n        _ (when (nil? v) (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :segment {:yin.k/segment a}))\n        tuple (first (filter #(and (= :closure (nth % 0)) (= entry (nth % 3))) v))]\n    (cond\n      (nil? tuple) (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :closure-origin {:yin.k/segment a :yin.k/entry entry})\n      (not= params (nth tuple 2)) (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :closure-binders {:yin.k/segment a :yin.k/entry entry})\n      :else nil)))\n\n\n(defn- check-dependencies!\n  \"Step 9, dependency closure: requires and code agree, every segment has\n   its trees (§6.1), every closure's and frame's store-of names a module\n   store of this task (not a parent's or sibling's of the same key), every\n   segment is a vector the receiver's kernel admits under its A, every\n   closure names a closure of its code, every :prim is the receiver's.\"\n  [recv task _role]\n  (let [[_ _ _ _ _ _ _ module-stores _ _ requires code] (:slots task)]\n    (when-not (and (map? requires) (= (set (:yin.k/segments requires)) (set (keys code))))\n      (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :requires {}))\n    (let [trees (:yin.k/trees requires)\n          missing (into #{} (remove #(seq (get trees %))) (keys code))]\n      (when (seq missing)\n        (outcome! :yin.k/unsatisfied nil {:yin.k/discovery :incomplete :yin.k/missing {:yin.k/trees missing}})))\n    ;; §2.6: every store-of resolves to a module store this task carries\n    (let [census (into #{} (map #(first (:slots %))) module-stores)\n          missing (into #{} (comp (keep #(nth (:slots %) (if (= :closure (:kind %)) 4 1)))\n                                  (remove census))\n                        (concat (rows-of task :closure true) (rows-of task :env true)))]\n      (when (seq missing)\n        (outcome! :yin.k/unsatisfied nil {:yin.k/discovery :incomplete :yin.k/missing {:yin.k/stores missing}})))\n    (doseq [[a v] (sort-by #(str (key %)) code)]\n      (when-not (attaches? recv v a)\n        (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :segment {:yin.k/segment a})))\n    (run! #(check-closure! code %) (rows-of task :closure true))\n    (doseq [p (rows-of task :prim true)]\n      (when-not (contains? (:primitives recv) (first (:slots p)))\n        (outcome! :yin.k/unsatisfied nil {:yin.k/name (first (:slots p))})))))\n\n\n(defn- accept-grant!\n  \"The grant checks of a blocked or parked exclusive root (handoff.cljc's\n   accept-grant!, ported verbatim, keyed off the root's custody slot c and\n   the carrier's pack address): evidence, binding, lease, holder,\n   arbitration, epoch, tenure and the input prefix; then protection in both\n   directions over every stream row of the tree, and op-id presence equal\n   to enrollment on every retained write. Answers the custody state the\n   restored root holds, its counter the slot's exactly.\"\n  [task c address opts]\n  (let [grant (:grant opts)\n        evidence (:evidence grant)]\n    (when-not (and (or (nil? grant) (map? grant))\n                   (or (nil? evidence) (map? evidence)))\n      (throw (ex-info \"Malformed lower grant or evidence\" {})))\n    (when-not evidence\n      (outcome! :yin.k/awaiting-grant nil {}))\n    (when-not (= :yin.k/ready (:yin.k/status evidence))\n      (outcome! (if (= :yin.k/awaiting-grant (:yin.k/status evidence))\n                  :yin.k/awaiting-grant :yin.k/unsatisfied)\n                nil (dissoc evidence :yin.k/status)))\n    (let [binding (:yin.k/binding evidence)\n          prefix (:yin.k/prefix evidence)\n          tenure (:tenure grant)\n          occurrence (:yin.k/occurrence c)\n          lease (:dao.lease/lease grant)\n          holder (:dao.lease/holder grant)\n          frontier (:yin.k/frontier prefix)\n          records (:yin.k/inputs prefix)]\n      (when-not (and (map? binding) (map? tenure))\n        (throw (ex-info \"Malformed lower binding or tenure\" {})))\n      (when (or (nil? prefix) (:yin.k/status prefix))\n        (outcome! :yin.k/unsatisfied nil {:yin.k/reason (or (:yin.k/reason prefix) :unavailable)}))\n      (when-not (and (= (:checkpoint grant) address)\n                     (= occurrence (:yin.k/occurrence binding))\n                     (some? lease) (= lease (:dao.lease/lease binding))\n                     (some? holder) (= holder (:dao.lease/holder binding))\n                     (= (get-in c [:yin.k/arbitration :dao.stream/identity])\n                        (get-in binding [:yin.k/transaction :yin.k/arbitration]))\n                     (custody/exact? (:yin.k/epoch binding))\n                     (true? (:live tenure))\n                     (number? (:now tenure)) (number? (:bound tenure))\n                     (< (:now tenure) (:bound tenure))\n                     (= occurrence (:yin.k/occurrence prefix))\n                     (= lease (:dao.lease/lease prefix))\n                     (custody/exact? frontier) (vector? records)\n                     (= frontier (count records))\n                     (every? true? (map-indexed\n                                     (fn [index record]\n                                       (and (custody/exact? (:yin.k/input-seq record))\n                                            (= index (:yin.k/input-seq record))))\n                                     records)))\n        (outcome! :yin.k/not-holder nil {}))\n      (let [classes (:protection opts)\n            enrolled (:yin.k/enrolled evidence)]\n        (when-not (and (map? classes)\n                       (every? #{:enrolled :at-least-once :fail-stop} (vals classes))\n                       (set? enrolled))\n          (throw (ex-info \"Malformed lower protection or enrollment\" {})))\n        (doseq [s (rows-of task :stream false)]\n          (let [identity (first (:slots s))\n                class (get classes identity)]\n            (when-not (and class (= (= class :enrolled) (contains? enrolled identity)))\n              (outcome! :yin.k/unsatisfied nil {:dao.stream/identity identity}))))\n        (doseq [[t _] (task-tree task :root)\n                w (nth (:slots t) 13)\n                :let [ss (:slots (second (:slots w)))\n                      [ti _ oi] (get write-slots (first ss))]\n                :when ti]\n          (let [identity (first (:slots (nth ss ti)))]\n            (when-not (= (= :enrolled (get classes identity)) (some? (nth ss oi)))\n              (outcome! :yin.k/unsatisfied nil {:dao.stream/identity identity}))))\n        {:yin.k/occurrence occurrence\n         :dao.lease/lease lease :dao.lease/holder holder\n         :yin.k/epoch (:yin.k/epoch binding)\n         :yin.k/arbitration (:yin.k/arbitration c)\n         :yin.k/next-op-seq (:yin.k/next-op-seq c)\n         :protection classes :input {:next 0 :prefix prefix}\n         :tenure {:bound (:bound tenure)}}))))\n\n\n(defn- check-custody!\n  \"Step 10, once for the tree after the three staged checks: the custody\n   grammar (custody-baseline), then by the root's slot: a fork (nil) is\n   refused under :exclusive as :yin.k/profile-mismatch; an exclusive\n   blocked or parked root runs the grant checks unless :fenced (an\n   administrative rehydration: no grant, gate :exporting); a halted\n   exclusive root needs no grant and is gated :ended. Answers\n   {:exclusive? :fenced? :state}, which restore applies to every task.\"\n  [task wire opts]\n  (custody-baseline task)\n  (let [[_ _ kind] (:slots task) c (nth (:slots task) 16) fenced? (boolean (:fenced opts))]\n    (if (nil? c)\n      (do (when (:exclusive opts)\n            (outcome! :yin.k/profile-mismatch nil {:yin.k/policy :yin.k/exclusive}))\n          {:exclusive? false :fenced? fenced?})\n      {:exclusive? true :fenced? fenced?\n       :state (when-not (or fenced? (= :halted kind)) (accept-grant! task c (pack-address wire) opts))})))\n\n\n(defn- with-custody\n  \"Restore's custody for one task of the tree: an exclusive tree numbers\n   its retained :put waits (:yin.k/issue, :yin.k/issued, in carried\n   order) and gates :running, a halted exclusive root :ended, the root\n   holding the grant's custody state; a fenced tree gates :exporting with\n   its waits outside the scheduler (:yin.k/recovery-waits).\"\n  [m {:keys [exclusive? fenced? state]} kind root?]\n  (let [m (if exclusive?\n            (let [[entries issued] (reduce (fn [[acc i] e]\n                                             (if (= :put (:reason e))\n                                               [(conj acc (assoc e :yin.k/issue i)) (inc i)]\n                                               [(conj acc e) i]))\n                                           [[] 0] (:wait-set m))]\n              (cond-> (assoc m :wait-set entries :yin.k/issued issued\n                             :yin.k/gate (if (and root? (= :halted kind)) :ended :running))\n                (and root? (some? state)) (assoc :yin.k/custody state)))\n            m)]\n    (if fenced?\n      (assoc m :yin.k/gate :exporting :yin.k/recovery-waits (:wait-set m) :wait-set [])\n      m)))\n\n\n(defn- attach-streams!\n  \"Step 11: one attach per distinct stream identity of the whole tree.\"\n  [attach! task]\n  (reduce (fn [acc s]\n            (let [[identity descriptor] (:slots s)]\n              (if (contains? acc identity)\n                acc\n                (if-some [h (remote/lower-marker attach! {:dao.stream/descriptor descriptor})]\n                  (assoc acc identity h)\n                  (outcome! :yin.k/unsatisfied nil {:dao.stream/identity identity})))))\n          {} (rows-of task :stream false)))\n\n\n(defn- spawn-child\n  \"A fresh install child of recv's composition (the engine's spawn\n   discipline): answers [child recv'].\"\n  [recv response mn]\n  (let [n (or (:origins recv) 0)\n        origin (keyword (str (name (or (:origin recv) :t0)) \".\" n))\n        registry (reduce (fn [r [m e]] (module/assoc-module r m (dissoc e :bindings)))\n                         (:modules recv) (module/module-entries (:modules recv)))\n        source (:secret-source recv)]\n    [(module/spawn-module recv (:value (:image response))\n                          {:modules registry :origin origin\n                           :ancestry (conj (vec (:ancestry recv)) mn)\n                           :capability-secret (when (fn? source) (source origin))})\n     (assoc recv :origins (inc n))]))\n\n\n(defn- restore-task\n  \"Step 12 for one task: code by A, fresh resource keys, values re-sealed\n   under recv, waits as engine entries, parked records, installs, and the\n   custody check-custody! answered (with-custody).\"\n  [recv task handles custody root?]\n  (let [[_ _ kind _ id-counter free-env store module-stores parked census _ code installs waits parked-id result]\n        (:slots task)\n        base (reduce (fn [r [_ v]] (module/attach-module r v))\n                     (assoc recv :code {} :code-aliases {} :program nil)\n                     (sort-by #(str (key %)) code))\n        aliases (:code-aliases base)\n        used (atom (into fixed-resource-keys (keys (:resources base))))\n        identities (sort-by str (distinct (map #(first (:slots %)) (rows-of task :stream true))))\n        stream-keys (into {} (map (fn [identity] [identity (fresh-key! used)])) identities)\n        pairs (mapv vec (partition 2 (:slots census)))\n        cell-keys (into {} (map (fn [[c _]] [c (fresh-key! used)])) pairs)\n        bodies (into {} pairs)\n        stream-key #(get stream-keys (first (:slots %)))\n        parked-index (into {} (map vec) (partition 2 (:slots parked)))\n        cache (atom {})\n        resolving (atom #{})]\n    (letfn [(value\n              [v]\n              (case (first v)\n                :lit (second v)\n                :cursor-cell (engine/issue-ref base :cursor-ref (get cell-keys (second v)))\n                :row (row (second v))))\n            (row\n              [n]\n              (let [ss (:slots n)]\n                (case (:kind n)\n                  :vec (mapv value ss)\n                  :list (apply list (map value ss))\n                  :set (into #{} (map value) ss)\n                  :map (into {} (map (fn [[k x]] [(value k) (value x)])) (partition 2 ss))\n                  :prim (vm/primitive-function (get (:primitives base) (first ss)))\n                  :stream (engine/issue-ref base :stream-ref (stream-key n))\n                  :closure (let [[a entry params bindings store-of] ss]\n                             (module/lower-closure base\n                                                   (cond-> {:yin.k/binding :named\n                                                            :yin.k/format :yin.semantic-register/code\n                                                            :yin.k/segment a :yin.k/entry entry :yin.k/params params\n                                                            :yin.k/env (keyed bindings)}\n                                                     (some? store-of) (assoc :yin.k/store-of store-of))\n                                                   identity))\n                  :reified (values/continuation (:owner base) (assoc (payload (first ss)) :type :reified-continuation))\n                  :parked-ref (parked-record (first ss)))))\n            (keyed\n              [n]\n              (into {} (map (fn [[k x]] [k (value x)])) (partition 2 (:slots n))))\n            (env\n              [n]\n              (let [[b store-of] (:slots n)]\n                (cond-> (keyed b) (some? store-of) (assoc engine/store-of-key store-of))))\n            (k-of\n              [n]\n              (mapv (fn [f]\n                      (let [[a pc e w rd] (:slots f)]\n                        {:type :return :segment (get aliases a) :pc pc :env (env e) :window (keyed w) :rd rd}))\n                    (:slots n)))\n            (payload\n              [n]\n              (if (= :tail (:kind n))\n                (let [[a site k] (:slots n)]\n                  {:segment (get aliases a) :site site :k (k-of k) :deliver {:deliver :return}})\n                (let [[a pc e w k rd] (:slots n)]\n                  {:segment (get aliases a) :pc pc :env (env e) :window (keyed w) :k (k-of k)\n                   :deliver {:deliver :rd :rd rd}})))\n            (parked-record\n              [p]\n              (or (get @cache p)\n                  (do (when (contains? @resolving p)\n                        (outcome! :yin.k/non-portable :non-canonicalizable {:yin.k/hint :parked-cycle}))\n                      (swap! resolving conj p)\n                      (let [r (assoc (payload (get parked-index p)) :type :parked-continuation :id p)]\n                        (swap! cache assoc p r)\n                        (swap! resolving disj p)\n                        r))))\n            (cell-stream\n              [c]\n              (stream-key (first (:slots (get bodies c)))))\n            (entry\n              [w]\n              (let [[state pending] (:slots w)\n                    [reason & xs] (:slots pending)\n                    p (payload state)]\n                (case reason\n                  :next (assoc p :reason :next :stream-id (cell-stream (first xs))\n                               :cursor-ref {:type :cursor-ref :id (get cell-keys (first xs))})\n                  :ffi (let [[c call-id op] xs]\n                         (cond-> (assoc p :reason :next :stream-id (cell-stream c) :call-id call-id\n                                        :cursor-ref {:type :cursor-ref :id (get cell-keys c)})\n                           (some? op) (assoc :op op)))\n                  :put (let [[s v op-id] xs]\n                         (cond-> (assoc p :reason :put :stream-id (stream-key s) :datom (value v))\n                           (some? op-id) (assoc :op-id op-id)))\n                  :ffi-request (let [[call-id envelope req resp c op-id] xs\n                                     datom (value envelope)]\n                                 (cond-> (assoc p :reason :put :stream-id (stream-key req) :datom datom\n                                                :request-sent true :call-id call-id :op (apply2/request-op datom)\n                                                :response-cursor (get cell-keys c) :response-stream (stream-key resp))\n                                   (some? op-id) (assoc :op-id op-id)))\n                  (:link-request :link-response)\n                  (let [[link-id mn _ _ c envelope op-id] xs]\n                    (cond-> (assoc p :reason reason :link-id link-id :name mn\n                                   :request module/link-request-resource :response module/link-response-resource\n                                   :cursor (second (:slots (get bodies c))))\n                      (= :link-request reason) (assoc :envelope envelope)\n                      (some? op-id) (assoc :op-id op-id)))\n                  :install (assoc p :reason :install :name (first xs)))))]\n      (let [store' (reduce (fn [s [k v]] (engine/store-put s k (value v))) {} (partition 2 (:slots store)))\n            stores (into {} (map (fn [ms]\n                                   (let [[mid s] (:slots ms)]\n                                     [mid (into {} (map (fn [[k v]] [k (value v)])) (partition 2 (:slots s)))])))\n                         module-stores)\n            parked' (into {} (map (fn [[p _]] [p (parked-record p)])) parked-index)\n            entries (mapv entry waits)\n            link (some #(let [[reason _ _ req resp] (:slots (second (:slots %)))]\n                          (when (contains? #{:link-request :link-response} reason) [req resp]))\n                       waits)\n            [base installs'] (reduce (fn [[r acc] inst]\n                                       (let [[mn phase parent response child] (:slots inst)\n                                             [spawned r'] (spawn-child r response mn)]\n                                         [r' (assoc acc mn {:phase phase :parent parent :response response\n                                                            :vm (restore-task spawned child handles custody false)})]))\n                                     [base {}] installs)\n            fe (keyed free-env)\n            resources (merge (:resources base)\n                             (into {} (map (fn [[identity k]] [k (get handles identity)])) stream-keys)\n                             (into {} (map (fn [[c body]]\n                                             [(get cell-keys c) {:stream-id (stream-key (first (:slots body)))\n                                                                 :cursor (second (:slots body))}]))\n                                   pairs)\n                             (when-let [[req resp] link]\n                               {module/link-request-resource (get handles (first (:slots req)))\n                                module/link-response-resource (get handles (first (:slots resp)))}))\n            machine (assoc base :store store' :module-stores stores :parked parked' :installs installs'\n                           :resources resources :env fe :free-env fe :window {} :k nil :control nil\n                           :ready-queue [] :id-counter (max (or (:id-counter base) 0) id-counter))]\n        (with-custody\n          (case kind\n            :halted (assoc machine :halted? true :blocked? false :value (value result) :wait-set [])\n            :parked (assoc machine :halted? true :blocked? false :value (get parked' parked-id) :wait-set entries)\n            (assoc machine :halted? false :blocked? true :value :yin/blocked :wait-set entries))\n          custody kind root?)))))\n\n\n(defn lower-task\n  \"The lower of §7.2 into recv, a fresh semantic-register machine of the\n   receiver's composition: gate to frames (decode) and the store keys,\n   then pendings and install records, dependency closure (code, closures,\n   primitives), each step over the whole tree before the next, then\n   custody (check-custody!), all before the first attach! (step 11); then\n   restore (step 12), which therefore meets no carrier defect. Answers the\n   restored machine, or throws the first refusal as ex-data.\n   opts: :budget; :exclusive, refuse a fork root; :grant and :protection,\n   required by a blocked or parked exclusive root (handoff.cljc's reader\n   contract: the grant names :checkpoint, the pack address, its lease,\n   holder, tenure and evidence; :protection maps every stream identity of\n   the tree to its class); :fenced, an administrative rehydration that\n   skips the grant.\"\n  ([recv wire attach!] (lower-task recv wire attach! {}))\n  ([recv wire attach! opts]\n   (let [task (decode wire (merge default-budget (:budget opts)))]\n     (when-not (= :task (:kind task)) (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :root {}))\n     ;; each step over the whole tree before the next (§3.3)\n     (doseq [step [check-stores! check-pendings! check-dependencies!]\n             [t role] (task-tree task :root)]\n       (step recv t role))\n     (let [custody (check-custody! task wire opts)]\n       (restore-task recv task (attach-streams! attach! task) custody true)))))","numLines":1080,"startLine":1140,"totalLines":2220}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01VwmbbtDD3vU6RsUFrwoezm","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
