{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013ppm7HvK7NedijrmbgP4xZ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t(ns yin.vm.ucf.holder.driver\n2\t  \"The custody driver of M-next D slices D13 and D14 (UCF 7.7.2 to\n3\t   7.7.8, 7.8, 7.9; r3 1.5, 1.6, 1.7, 1.8, 1.9 and 1.10; the D9 header\n4\t   and D10 lower-inputs rulings; linker-dht 14.2.2): one explicit\n5\t   composition-local step state, stepped by the composition, that\n6\t   carries a candidate from bytes to a task under custody, drives that\n7\t   task's run, and -- D14 -- carries the source half (a first export\n8\t   and its offer) and the exit half (the successor, the report, the\n9\t   release and the closure) over a write-ahead progress journal.\n10\t\n11\t   The driver reaches the authority through exactly the three remote\n12\t   paths of r3 1.5, all composition-supplied functions: the front's\n13\t   request stream (`append-request!`), the version-1 positional\n14\t   `reply-inbox` and `outcome-inbox`, and the authenticated ledger\n15\t   reader (`read-ledger!`, whose attributed records D3's\n16\t   `read-evidence` and `custody/binding-evidence` fold).  The lease\n17\t   clock (`clock`) is the composition's too, and dao.lease's own holder\n18\t   discipline -- `observe-grant`, `holding?`, `due-to-renew?`,\n19\t   `observe-renewal`, `stop` -- is the tenure arithmetic over it.\n20\t\n21\t   The phases, one `:phase` key:\n22\t\n23\t   :validating -- fetch and validate with zero side effects: the D7\n24\t   reader over the bytes (`resume-task` before `checkpoint/inspect`, that\n25\t   supplies no grant, so nothing is attached and no machine is exposed)\n26\t   answers `:yin.k/awaiting-grant` for a valid version-1 blocked or\n27\t   parked root; anything else is a data refusal with no cleanup owed.  A\n28\t   halted version-1 root is not a lease subject: it lowers once, gated\n29\t   `:ended`, and the driver publishes it with no custody.\n30\t\n31\t   :proposing -- check the authority attachment (a missing one is\n32\t   `:yin.k/unsatisfied` naming the arbitration), propose through the\n33\t   front with a fresh proposal id, and observe the grant from the\n34\t   ledger: while the proposal is unanswered the step answers\n35\t   `:yin.k/awaiting-grant`; a grant to another, or an occurrence that\n36\t   can never be granted again, answers `:yin.k/not-holder` with the\n37\t   lease state observed and releases nothing.  A grant to this driver\n38\t   is accepted only whole: `custody/binding-evidence` over the same\n39\t   records (an invalid binding -- none, a duplicate, an inexact epoch,\n40\t   one outside the grant's transaction, one that mismatches its grant\n41\t   -- is `:yin.k/not-holder` followed by a release), then D3's\n42\t   `read-evidence` (unavailable history is `:yin.k/unsatisfied`, never\n43\t   an empty prefix, and never a release: custody was not accepted),\n44\t   then the admitted-variant rule (the address must be among the fold's\n45\t   admitted variants of the granted occurrence -- equality of supplied\n46\t   addresses proves nothing), then current tenure: the fold's live\n47\t   lease at the binding's epoch and dao.lease's bound, rechecked before\n48\t   any execution or IO is scheduled.  Only then D10's lower runs, with\n49\t   the checkpoint address, the composition's protection declaration and\n50\t   the grant evidence; a lower failure is after the grant, and releases\n51\t   first.  A regrant replays from the checkpoint: the lower starts\n52\t   input at zero under the evidence's prefix.\n53\t\n54\t   :activating -- an authenticated grant is retained with its original\n55\t   observation basis, without a machine. Control ticks may renew it;\n56\t   only a program tick revalidates and lowers it.\n57\t\n58\t   :running -- run under the gate and drive the writer's and reader's\n59\t   steps: tenure rechecked, the renewal sent through D2's\n60\t   `:yin.k/renewal` request before half the duration and never past the\n61\t   bound, the machine's internal computation, replay below the\n62\t   frontier, `writer/emit`, `reader/step`, and every attributed record\n63\t   the readers answer routed to the writer's `discharge`, the reader's\n64\t   `settle` or this driver's own control arm.  All IO stops at the\n65\t   bound; a run end (:stale, :intent-conflict, :input-conflict, a\n66\t   replay divergence, the bound) gates the machine `:ended`, appends\n67\t   one diagnostic, and releases -- cleanup, not recovery: a release\n68\t   never clears a quarantine, never completes without accepted\n69\t   completion evidence, and the occurrence of an ordinary failed run\n70\t   stays regrantable under the ordinary policy.\n71\t\n72\t   :safepoint -- the machine has nothing left to drive (halted, no wait\n73\t   entry, no queued work); the exit half (D14) owns what follows, under\n74\t   tenure that is still held: renewal and the recheck continue while it\n75\t   runs, and all IO stops at the bound.\n76\t\n77\t   :releasing -- a pending release is retried with the identical\n78\t   request until authenticated carriage is acknowledged, then its failure is\n79\t   the driver's answer.  :failed is terminal.\n80\t\n81\t   The D14 phases and entries beside these:\n82\t\n83\t   :exporting -- the source half over a machine the composition hands\n84\t   the driver (`source`, below): enter exporting, mint the occurrence\n85\t   once and journal it before prepare (the D9 ruling), prepare, encode,\n86\t   put the prepared record and the body bytes in the content store,\n87\t   journal the fenced record, then the bracketed offer -- an intent\n88\t   record durable before each send, an attempt record after it, an\n89\t   acknowledgment once the front's authenticated reply admits the offer.\n90\t   A nil :arbitration in the config is the composition's fork decision:\n91\t   the lift is version 0, nothing is minted, offered or journaled, and\n92\t   the driver answers the bytes (:lifted).\n93\t\n94\t   :exiting -- the exit half of a restarted holder, journaled but\n95\t   machine-less: it reconciles committed reports, carries release and\n96\t   watches for closure. An uncommitted report returns to candidacy,\n97\t   without borrowing old tenure. A live driver runs the exit body from\n98\t   :safepoint under its own tenure.\n99\t\n100\t   :exited -- the exit completed: the report committed, the release\n101\t   carried, the closure observed and, for a continuation, the\n102\t   successor's offer admitted.  :lifted and :aborted are the fork's and\n103\t   a legal abort's terminals.  :stalled is an uncertain journal append:\n104\t   everything stops -- program steps and sends alike -- until the\n105\t   composition reopens the journal and reconciles through `reopen`.\n106\t\n107\t   The source is a candidate like any other: the driver holds bytes,\n108\t   never the source's local machine, so the source itself resumes only\n109\t   through a grant to itself, never on data.  No transport is known\n110\t   here; the machine's own resource handles are the only ones touched,\n111\t   by the writer and the reader.\"\n112\t  (:require [dao.jing :as jing]\n113\t            [dao.jing.cbor :as cbor]\n114\t            [dao.lease :as lease]\n115\t            [dao.stream :as stream]\n116\t            [yin.vm :as vm]\n117\t            [yin.vm.ucf.authority.completion :as completion]\n118\t            [yin.vm.ucf.authority.front :as front]\n119\t            [yin.vm.ucf.checkpoint :as checkpoint]\n120\t            [yin.vm.ucf.custody :as custody]\n121\t            [yin.vm.ucf.handoff :as handoff]\n122\t            [yin.vm.ucf.holder.evidence :as evidence]\n123\t            [yin.vm.ucf.holder.export :as export]\n124\t            [yin.vm.ucf.holder.inbox :as inbox]\n125\t            [yin.vm.ucf.holder.reader :as reader]\n126\t            [yin.vm.ucf.holder.writer :as writer]\n127\t            [yin.vm.ucf.ledger :as ledger]))\n128\t\n129\t\n130\t;; =============================================================================\n131\t;; Assembly\n132\t;; =============================================================================\n133\t\n134\t(def ^:private classes\n135\t  \"The three protection classes of r3 1.11.\"\n136\t  #{:enrolled :at-least-once :fail-stop})\n137\t\n138\t\n139\t(def ^:private seams\n140\t  \"The composition-supplied functions the driver steps through.\"\n141\t  [:append-request! :read-ledger!\n142\t   :clock :observe! :append-diagnostic! :attach! :serve!])\n143\t\n144\t\n145\t(def ^:private optional-seams\n146\t  \"Composition-supplied functions the driver uses only when asked.\"\n147\t  [:enroll!])\n148\t\n149\t\n150\t(defn- check!\n151\t  [ok what data]\n152\t  (when-not ok\n153\t    (throw (ex-info (str \"The candidate driver needs \" what)\n154\t                    (into {} (cons {:yin.k/hint :assembly} data))))))\n155\t\n156\t\n157\t(defn- check-interval!\n158\t  \"The renewal interval's own shape gate, as dao.lease's holder runs it\n159\t   at assembly: a duration, in a unit of the table, within the per-unit\n160\t   bound.  The sizing against the granted duration -- strictly below\n161\t   half -- is checked where the two are known together, at the grant.\"\n162\t  [units interval]\n163\t  (check! (lease/duration? interval)\n164\t          \"a renewal interval: a single-entry {unit positive-integer} map\"\n165\t          {:renewal-interval interval})\n166\t  (let [[unit magnitude] (first interval)]\n167\t    (check! (some? (get units unit))\n168\t            \"a renewal interval whose unit is in the unit table\"\n169\t            {:renewal-interval interval :units units})\n170\t    (check! (<= magnitude (quot lease/magnitude-limit (get units unit)))\n171\t            \"a renewal interval within the per-unit bound\"\n172\t            {:renewal-interval interval})))\n173\t\n174\t\n175\t(defn- check-common!\n176\t  \"The checks every driver constructor runs: the identity, the\n177\t   protection declaration, the receiving machine, the renewal interval,\n178\t   the fn seams, the progress journal, the content store and the carrier\n179\t   medium -- the D14 seams beside the D13 ones.  A candidate that never\n180\t   exits still carries them: a grant may make it a holder whose run\n181\t   ends in an exit.\"\n182\t  [config units]\n183\t  (check! (some? (:me config)) \"an identity: the holder a grant would name\"\n184\t          {:me (:me config)})\n185\t  (check! (and (map? (:protection config))\n186\t               (every? classes (vals (:protection config))))\n187\t          \"a protection declaration over the three classes\"\n188\t          {:protection (:protection config)})\n189\t  (check! (map? (:receiver config)) \"a receiving machine\" {})\n190\t  (check-interval! units (:renewal-interval config))\n191\t  (doseq [s seams]\n192\t    (check! (fn? (get config s)) (str \"the seam \" (name s)) {}))\n193\t  (doseq [key (vals inbox/lanes)]\n194\t    (inbox/check-descriptor! (get config key)))\n195\t  (doseq [s optional-seams\n196\t          :when (some? (get config s))]\n197\t    (check! (fn? (get config s)) (str \"the seam \" (name s)) {}))\n198\t  (check! (some? (get config :journal))\n199\t          \"a progress journal: a dao.stream.journal handle\" {})\n200\t  (check! (and (map? (:store config))\n201\t               (fn? (:put-bytes-fn (:store config)))\n202\t               (fn? (:get-bytes-fn (:store config))))\n203\t          \"a content store: a dao.jing byte-store handle\"\n204\t          {})\n205\t  (check! (some? (:medium config)) \"a carrier medium name\" {}))\n206\t\n207\t\n208\t(defn- bare-state\n209\t  \"The step state every constructor fills from `config`.\"\n210\t  [config units]\n211\t  {:phase :validating\n212\t   :status nil\n213\t   :detail nil\n214\t   :me (:me config)\n215\t   :bytes (:bytes config)\n216\t   :address (:address config)\n217\t   :protection (:protection config)\n218\t   :renewal-interval (:renewal-interval config)\n219\t   :units units\n220\t   :receiver (:receiver config)\n221\t   :export-version (:export-version config)\n222\t   :seams (-> (select-keys config (into (into seams optional-seams) (vals inbox/lanes)))\n223\t              (assoc :journal (:journal config)\n224\t                     :content-store (:store config)\n225\t                     :medium (:medium config)))\n226\t   :occurrence nil\n227\t   :arbitration nil\n228\t   :kind nil\n229\t   :proposal nil\n230\t   :proposals 0\n231\t   :sent-proposals #{}\n232\t   :lease nil\n233\t   :holder nil\n234\t   :evidence nil\n235\t   :machine nil\n236\t   :renewals 0\n237\t   :renewal-pending? false\n238\t   :release nil\n239\t   :diagnostics []\n240\t   :export nil\n241\t   :exit nil\n242\t   :stopped? false\n243\t   :inbox {:positions {:reply 0 :outcome 0} :program [] :control []}})\n244\t\n245\t\n246\t(declare journal-records fold-journal restore-inbox)\n247\t\n248\t\n249\t(defn initial\n250\t  \"The candidate's composition-local step state over `config`:\n251\t\n252\t     :me                this candidate's holder identity\n253\t     :bytes             the checkpoint bytes the composition fetched\n254\t     :address           the segment address they were fetched under\n255\t     :protection        the composition's declaration, stream identity to\n256\t                        class (:enrolled, :at-least-once or :fail-stop)\n257\t     :renewal-interval  the composition's interval, sized strictly below\n258\t                        half the duration it arranges (H2/S1)\n259\t     :units             optional unit table, dao.lease's default\n260\t     :receiver          the receiving machine of the receiver's own\n261\t                        composition\n262\t     :attach!           the receiver's :dao.stream/attach dispatch\n263\t     :append-request!   (fn [request] append-outcome), the holder's\n264\t                        inbound stream\n265\t     :reply-inbox       {:version 1 :identity stable-id :read-at! f},\n266\t                        the completely retained front reply source\n267\t     :outcome-inbox     the same descriptor for admission outcomes;\n268\t                        f takes a dense portable position, without\n269\t                        consuming, and returns {:status :record\n270\t                        :position n :author a :record r}, {:status :empty}\n271\t                        at the tail, or {:status :unavailable} for\n272\t                        inaccessible history. No destructive fallback.\n273\t     :read-ledger!      (fn [] [[author record] ...] | nil), the\n274\t                        authority's ledger records from the origin, or\n275\t                        nil when the arbitration medium cannot be\n276\t                        attached at all\n277\t     :clock             (fn [] reading), the lease clock\n278\t     :observe!          (fn [handle op arg] outcome), the handle observer\n279\t     :append-diagnostic!  (fn [diagnostic] ...), the composition's\n280\t                        diagnostic stream\n281\t     :serve!            (fn [handle] descriptor), the exporter's server,\n282\t                        for the exit a grant may reach\n283\t     :journal           the composition's progress journal (a\n284\t                        dao.stream.journal handle): every durable act of\n285\t                        the driver -- each bracketed external action, the\n286\t                        mint, the fence, the accepted grant -- is\n287\t                        write-ahead in it\n288\t     :store             the composition's content store: the prepared\n289\t                        record and the body bytes are put in it before\n290\t                        the fenced record references them\n291\t     :medium            the carrier medium name the offer carries\n292\t     :enroll!           optional (fn [] enrollment-answer), the\n293\t                        composition's enrollment seam\n294\t\n295\t   A missing or mis-shaped seam throws here, at assembly, as\n296\t   dao.lease's own halves do.\"\n297\t  [{:keys [bytes address] :as config}]\n298\t  (let [units (or (:units config) lease/default-units)]\n299\t    (check! (some? bytes) \"the checkpoint bytes\" {})\n300\t    (check! (some? address) \"the address the bytes were fetched under\"\n301\t            {:address address})\n302\t    (check-common! config units)\n303\t    (restore-inbox (bare-state config units)\n304\t                   (:inbox (fold-journal (journal-records (:journal config)))))))\n305\t\n306\t\n307\t(defn source\n308\t  \"The source's composition-local step state over `config`: everything\n309\t   `initial` takes except :bytes and :address -- the driver mints those\n310\t   itself -- plus\n311\t\n312\t     :machine           the machine at its liftable safepoint (parked,\n313\t                        blocked or halted), gate :running; never one\n314\t                        that already holds custody (a holder exports its\n315\t                        successor through `hand-off`)\n316\t     :arbitration       the arbitration medium the composition names, a\n317\t                        version-1 exclusive export; nil is the\n318\t                        composition's fork decision: the lift is\n319\t                        version 0, nothing is minted, offered or\n320\t                        journaled, and the driver answers the bytes\n321\t\n322\t   The driver enters exporting, mints the occurrence once, journals it\n323\t   before prepare, prepares, encodes, fences and offers; once the offer\n324\t   is admitted it becomes a candidate like any other, over its own\n325\t   bytes.  The header is the driver's, never the composition's: a first\n326\t   export carries the composition's arbitration, next-op-seq 0 and no\n327\t   origin; the enrolled set is the ledger fold's.\"\n328\t  [{:keys [machine] :as config}]\n329\t  (let [units (or (:units config) lease/default-units)]\n330\t    (check! (map? machine) \"the machine to export\" {})"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"108e1cb8-f707-457b-be14-6feb1e135c49","uuid":"40e8c856-f38b-49c6-aacf-4a55bb0d5a4d","timestamp":"2026-10-13T10:03:05.567Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p7b/src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/holder/driver.cljc","content":"(ns yin.vm.ucf.holder.driver\n  \"The custody driver of M-next D slices D13 and D14 (UCF 7.7.2 to\n   7.7.8, 7.8, 7.9; r3 1.5, 1.6, 1.7, 1.8, 1.9 and 1.10; the D9 header\n   and D10 lower-inputs rulings; linker-dht 14.2.2): one explicit\n   composition-local step state, stepped by the composition, that\n   carries a candidate from bytes to a task under custody, drives that\n   task's run, and -- D14 -- carries the source half (a first export\n   and its offer) and the exit half (the successor, the report, the\n   release and the closure) over a write-ahead progress journal.\n\n   The driver reaches the authority through exactly the three remote\n   paths of r3 1.5, all composition-supplied functions: the front's\n   request stream (`append-request!`), the version-1 positional\n   `reply-inbox` and `outcome-inbox`, and the authenticated ledger\n   reader (`read-ledger!`, whose attributed records D3's\n   `read-evidence` and `custody/binding-evidence` fold).  The lease\n   clock (`clock`) is the composition's too, and dao.lease's own holder\n   discipline -- `observe-grant`, `holding?`, `due-to-renew?`,\n   `observe-renewal`, `stop` -- is the tenure arithmetic over it.\n\n   The phases, one `:phase` key:\n\n   :validating -- fetch and validate with zero side effects: the D7\n   reader over the bytes (`resume-task` before `checkpoint/inspect`, that\n   supplies no grant, so nothing is attached and no machine is exposed)\n   answers `:yin.k/awaiting-grant` for a valid version-1 blocked or\n   parked root; anything else is a data refusal with no cleanup owed.  A\n   halted version-1 root is not a lease subject: it lowers once, gated\n   `:ended`, and the driver publishes it with no custody.\n\n   :proposing -- check the authority attachment (a missing one is\n   `:yin.k/unsatisfied` naming the arbitration), propose through the\n   front with a fresh proposal id, and observe the grant from the\n   ledger: while the proposal is unanswered the step answers\n   `:yin.k/awaiting-grant`; a grant to another, or an occurrence that\n   can never be granted again, answers `:yin.k/not-holder` with the\n   lease state observed and releases nothing.  A grant to this driver\n   is accepted only whole: `custody/binding-evidence` over the same\n   records (an invalid binding -- none, a duplicate, an inexact epoch,\n   one outside the grant's transaction, one that mismatches its grant\n   -- is `:yin.k/not-holder` followed by a release), then D3's\n   `read-evidence` (unavailable history is `:yin.k/unsatisfied`, never\n   an empty prefix, and never a release: custody was not accepted),\n   then the admitted-variant rule (the address must be among the fold's\n   admitted variants of the granted occurrence -- equality of supplied\n   addresses proves nothing), then current tenure: the fold's live\n   lease at the binding's epoch and dao.lease's bound, rechecked before\n   any execution or IO is scheduled.  Only then D10's lower runs, with\n   the checkpoint address, the composition's protection declaration and\n   the grant evidence; a lower failure is after the grant, and releases\n   first.  A regrant replays from the checkpoint: the lower starts\n   input at zero under the evidence's prefix.\n\n   :activating -- an authenticated grant is retained with its original\n   observation basis, without a machine. Control ticks may renew it;\n   only a program tick revalidates and lowers it.\n\n   :running -- run under the gate and drive the writer's and reader's\n   steps: tenure rechecked, the renewal sent through D2's\n   `:yin.k/renewal` request before half the duration and never past the\n   bound, the machine's internal computation, replay below the\n   frontier, `writer/emit`, `reader/step`, and every attributed record\n   the readers answer routed to the writer's `discharge`, the reader's\n   `settle` or this driver's own control arm.  All IO stops at the\n   bound; a run end (:stale, :intent-conflict, :input-conflict, a\n   replay divergence, the bound) gates the machine `:ended`, appends\n   one diagnostic, and releases -- cleanup, not recovery: a release\n   never clears a quarantine, never completes without accepted\n   completion evidence, and the occurrence of an ordinary failed run\n   stays regrantable under the ordinary policy.\n\n   :safepoint -- the machine has nothing left to drive (halted, no wait\n   entry, no queued work); the exit half (D14) owns what follows, under\n   tenure that is still held: renewal and the recheck continue while it\n   runs, and all IO stops at the bound.\n\n   :releasing -- a pending release is retried with the identical\n   request until authenticated carriage is acknowledged, then its failure is\n   the driver's answer.  :failed is terminal.\n\n   The D14 phases and entries beside these:\n\n   :exporting -- the source half over a machine the composition hands\n   the driver (`source`, below): enter exporting, mint the occurrence\n   once and journal it before prepare (the D9 ruling), prepare, encode,\n   put the prepared record and the body bytes in the content store,\n   journal the fenced record, then the bracketed offer -- an intent\n   record durable before each send, an attempt record after it, an\n   acknowledgment once the front's authenticated reply admits the offer.\n   A nil :arbitration in the config is the composition's fork decision:\n   the lift is version 0, nothing is minted, offered or journaled, and\n   the driver answers the bytes (:lifted).\n\n   :exiting -- the exit half of a restarted holder, journaled but\n   machine-less: it reconciles committed reports, carries release and\n   watches for closure. An uncommitted report returns to candidacy,\n   without borrowing old tenure. A live driver runs the exit body from\n   :safepoint under its own tenure.\n\n   :exited -- the exit completed: the report committed, the release\n   carried, the closure observed and, for a continuation, the\n   successor's offer admitted.  :lifted and :aborted are the fork's and\n   a legal abort's terminals.  :stalled is an uncertain journal append:\n   everything stops -- program steps and sends alike -- until the\n   composition reopens the journal and reconciles through `reopen`.\n\n   The source is a candidate like any other: the driver holds bytes,\n   never the source's local machine, so the source itself resumes only\n   through a grant to itself, never on data.  No transport is known\n   here; the machine's own resource handles are the only ones touched,\n   by the writer and the reader.\"\n  (:require [dao.jing :as jing]\n            [dao.jing.cbor :as cbor]\n            [dao.lease :as lease]\n            [dao.stream :as stream]\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.authority.completion :as completion]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.authority.front :as front]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.checkpoint :as checkpoint]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.custody :as custody]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.handoff :as handoff]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.holder.evidence :as evidence]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.holder.export :as export]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.holder.inbox :as inbox]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.holder.reader :as reader]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.holder.writer :as writer]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.ledger :as ledger]))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Assembly\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(def ^:private classes\n  \"The three protection classes of r3 1.11.\"\n  #{:enrolled :at-least-once :fail-stop})\n\n\n(def ^:private seams\n  \"The composition-supplied functions the driver steps through.\"\n  [:append-request! :read-ledger!\n   :clock :observe! :append-diagnostic! :attach! :serve!])\n\n\n(def ^:private optional-seams\n  \"Composition-supplied functions the driver uses only when asked.\"\n  [:enroll!])\n\n\n(defn- check!\n  [ok what data]\n  (when-not ok\n    (throw (ex-info (str \"The candidate driver needs \" what)\n                    (into {} (cons {:yin.k/hint :assembly} data))))))\n\n\n(defn- check-interval!\n  \"The renewal interval's own shape gate, as dao.lease's holder runs it\n   at assembly: a duration, in a unit of the table, within the per-unit\n   bound.  The sizing against the granted duration -- strictly below\n   half -- is checked where the two are known together, at the grant.\"\n  [units interval]\n  (check! (lease/duration? interval)\n          \"a renewal interval: a single-entry {unit positive-integer} map\"\n          {:renewal-interval interval})\n  (let [[unit magnitude] (first interval)]\n    (check! (some? (get units unit))\n            \"a renewal interval whose unit is in the unit table\"\n            {:renewal-interval interval :units units})\n    (check! (<= magnitude (quot lease/magnitude-limit (get units unit)))\n            \"a renewal interval within the per-unit bound\"\n            {:renewal-interval interval})))\n\n\n(defn- check-common!\n  \"The checks every driver constructor runs: the identity, the\n   protection declaration, the receiving machine, the renewal interval,\n   the fn seams, the progress journal, the content store and the carrier\n   medium -- the D14 seams beside the D13 ones.  A candidate that never\n   exits still carries them: a grant may make it a holder whose run\n   ends in an exit.\"\n  [config units]\n  (check! (some? (:me config)) \"an identity: the holder a grant would name\"\n          {:me (:me config)})\n  (check! (and (map? (:protection config))\n               (every? classes (vals (:protection config))))\n          \"a protection declaration over the three classes\"\n          {:protection (:protection config)})\n  (check! (map? (:receiver config)) \"a receiving machine\" {})\n  (check-interval! units (:renewal-interval config))\n  (doseq [s seams]\n    (check! (fn? (get config s)) (str \"the seam \" (name s)) {}))\n  (doseq [key (vals inbox/lanes)]\n    (inbox/check-descriptor! (get config key)))\n  (doseq [s optional-seams\n          :when (some? (get config s))]\n    (check! (fn? (get config s)) (str \"the seam \" (name s)) {}))\n  (check! (some? (get config :journal))\n          \"a progress journal: a dao.stream.journal handle\" {})\n  (check! (and (map? (:store config))\n               (fn? (:put-bytes-fn (:store config)))\n               (fn? (:get-bytes-fn (:store config))))\n          \"a content store: a dao.jing byte-store handle\"\n          {})\n  (check! (some? (:medium config)) \"a carrier medium name\" {}))\n\n\n(defn- bare-state\n  \"The step state every constructor fills from `config`.\"\n  [config units]\n  {:phase :validating\n   :status nil\n   :detail nil\n   :me (:me config)\n   :bytes (:bytes config)\n   :address (:address config)\n   :protection (:protection config)\n   :renewal-interval (:renewal-interval config)\n   :units units\n   :receiver (:receiver config)\n   :export-version (:export-version config)\n   :seams (-> (select-keys config (into (into seams optional-seams) (vals inbox/lanes)))\n              (assoc :journal (:journal config)\n                     :content-store (:store config)\n                     :medium (:medium config)))\n   :occurrence nil\n   :arbitration nil\n   :kind nil\n   :proposal nil\n   :proposals 0\n   :sent-proposals #{}\n   :lease nil\n   :holder nil\n   :evidence nil\n   :machine nil\n   :renewals 0\n   :renewal-pending? false\n   :release nil\n   :diagnostics []\n   :export nil\n   :exit nil\n   :stopped? false\n   :inbox {:positions {:reply 0 :outcome 0} :program [] :control []}})\n\n\n(declare journal-records fold-journal restore-inbox)\n\n\n(defn initial\n  \"The candidate's composition-local step state over `config`:\n\n     :me                this candidate's holder identity\n     :bytes             the checkpoint bytes the composition fetched\n     :address           the segment address they were fetched under\n     :protection        the composition's declaration, stream identity to\n                        class (:enrolled, :at-least-once or :fail-stop)\n     :renewal-interval  the composition's interval, sized strictly below\n                        half the duration it arranges (H2/S1)\n     :units             optional unit table, dao.lease's default\n     :receiver          the receiving machine of the receiver's own\n                        composition\n     :attach!           the receiver's :dao.stream/attach dispatch\n     :append-request!   (fn [request] append-outcome), the holder's\n                        inbound stream\n     :reply-inbox       {:version 1 :identity stable-id :read-at! f},\n                        the completely retained front reply source\n     :outcome-inbox     the same descriptor for admission outcomes;\n                        f takes a dense portable position, without\n                        consuming, and returns {:status :record\n                        :position n :author a :record r}, {:status :empty}\n                        at the tail, or {:status :unavailable} for\n                        inaccessible history. No destructive fallback.\n     :read-ledger!      (fn [] [[author record] ...] | nil), the\n                        authority's ledger records from the origin, or\n                        nil when the arbitration medium cannot be\n                        attached at all\n     :clock             (fn [] reading), the lease clock\n     :observe!          (fn [handle op arg] outcome), the handle observer\n     :append-diagnostic!  (fn [diagnostic] ...), the composition's\n                        diagnostic stream\n     :serve!            (fn [handle] descriptor), the exporter's server,\n                        for the exit a grant may reach\n     :journal           the composition's progress journal (a\n                        dao.stream.journal handle): every durable act of\n                        the driver -- each bracketed external action, the\n                        mint, the fence, the accepted grant -- is\n                        write-ahead in it\n     :store             the composition's content store: the prepared\n                        record and the body bytes are put in it before\n                        the fenced record references them\n     :medium            the carrier medium name the offer carries\n     :enroll!           optional (fn [] enrollment-answer), the\n                        composition's enrollment seam\n\n   A missing or mis-shaped seam throws here, at assembly, as\n   dao.lease's own halves do.\"\n  [{:keys [bytes address] :as config}]\n  (let [units (or (:units config) lease/default-units)]\n    (check! (some? bytes) \"the checkpoint bytes\" {})\n    (check! (some? address) \"the address the bytes were fetched under\"\n            {:address address})\n    (check-common! config units)\n    (restore-inbox (bare-state config units)\n                   (:inbox (fold-journal (journal-records (:journal config)))))))\n\n\n(defn source\n  \"The source's composition-local step state over `config`: everything\n   `initial` takes except :bytes and :address -- the driver mints those\n   itself -- plus\n\n     :machine           the machine at its liftable safepoint (parked,\n                        blocked or halted), gate :running; never one\n                        that already holds custody (a holder exports its\n                        successor through `hand-off`)\n     :arbitration       the arbitration medium the composition names, a\n                        version-1 exclusive export; nil is the\n                        composition's fork decision: the lift is\n                        version 0, nothing is minted, offered or\n                        journaled, and the driver answers the bytes\n\n   The driver enters exporting, mints the occurrence once, journals it\n   before prepare, prepares, encodes, fences and offers; once the offer\n   is admitted it becomes a candidate like any other, over its own\n   bytes.  The header is the driver's, never the composition's: a first\n   export carries the composition's arbitration, next-op-seq 0 and no\n   origin; the enrolled set is the ledger fold's.\"\n  [{:keys [machine] :as config}]\n  (let [units (or (:units config) lease/default-units)]\n    (check! (map? machine) \"the machine to export\" {})","numLines":330,"startLine":1,"totalLines":2918}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_013ppm7HvK7NedijrmbgP4xZ","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
