{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01F57HUcGwFxVKeUzLUtNeQ4","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t(ns yin.vm.ucf.rows-support\n2\t  \"Test support for the row carrier under custody (phase 7a): real\n3\t   semantic-register machines the engine parks, the composition's source\n4\t   index, a deterministic exporter, the custody header parts and `lift`,\n5\t   rows/lift-task over one machine. It mirrors yin.vm.ucf.lift-support,\n6\t   whose AST helpers, one-slot streams, exporter and header parts it\n7\t   reuses, over yin.vm.semantic-register instead of the old kernel.\n8\t\n9\t   Every pack the 7a tests and the rows checkpoint fixtures check comes\n10\t   out of `lift`, never from a hand-built map. The one thing set by hand\n11\t   is an operation id on a wait entry (`with-op-id`), as in lift-support.\n12\t   The streams carry no random identity and `serve-table` answers s0, s1\n13\t   ... in first-asked order, so a pack's bytes are the same on every run\n14\t   and host.\"\n15\t  (:require [dao.jing :as jing]\n16\t            [dao.stream :as stream]\n17\t            [dao.stream.ringbuffer :as ringbuffer]\n18\t            [yin.vm :as vm]\n19\t            [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\n20\t            [yin.vm.module :as module]\n21\t            [yin.vm.semantic-register :as sr]\n22\t            [yin.vm.semantic-register.code :as code]\n23\t            [yin.vm.semantic-register.linearize :as linearize]\n24\t            [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]\n25\t            [yin.vm.ucf.lift-support :as ls]\n26\t            [yin.vm.ucf.rows :as rows]\n27\t            [yin.vm.values :as values]))\n28\t\n29\t\n30\t;; =============================================================================\n31\t;; The composition: code by A and the source index\n32\t;; =============================================================================\n33\t\n34\t(def source-index\n35\t  \"The composition's {A #{tree-address}} (continuation §6.1): every vector\n36\t   `project` makes is recorded beside the address of its AST.\"\n37\t  (atom {}))\n38\t\n39\t\n40\t(defn project\n41\t  [ast]\n42\t  (let [v (:vector (linearize/project ast))]\n43\t    (swap! source-index update (jing/segment-key v) (fnil conj #{}) (jing/segment-key [:yin/tree ast]))\n44\t    v))\n45\t\n46\t\n47\t(def lit ls/lit)\n48\t(def v ls/v)\n49\t(def lam ls/lam)\n50\t(def app ls/app)\n51\t(def then ls/then)\n52\t(def let1 ls/let1)\n53\t(def def! ls/def!)\n54\t(def cursor-of ls/cursor-of)\n55\t(def next-of ls/next-of)\n56\t(def one-slot-stream ls/one-slot-stream)\n57\t(def serve-table ls/serve-table)\n58\t(def with-op-id ls/with-op-id)\n59\t(def occurrence ls/occurrence)\n60\t(def predecessor ls/predecessor)\n61\t(def origin ls/origin)\n62\t(def arbitration ls/arbitration)\n63\t(def op-id ls/op-id)\n64\t(def header ls/header)\n65\t\n66\t\n67\t(defn- ring\n68\t  [capacity]\n69\t  (:dao.stream/handle\n70\t    (ringbuffer/create! {:dao.stream/type ringbuffer/transport-type ringbuffer/capacity-key capacity})))\n71\t\n72\t\n73\t(defn- make-det-stream\n74\t  []\n75\t  (let [n (atom 0)]\n76\t    (fn [_capacity]\n77\t      {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n78\t       :dao.stream/handle (one-slot-stream (str \"made-\" (swap! n inc)))})))\n79\t\n80\t\n81\t(def stream-modules (module/register-stream-module (module/default-registry)))\n82\t\n83\t\n84\t(defn new-machine\n85\t  ([] (new-machine {}))\n86\t  ([opts]\n87\t   (sr/create-vm (merge {:make-stream (make-det-stream)\n88\t                         :capability-secret tu/secret\n89\t                         :modules stream-modules\n90\t                         :secret-source (fn [origin] (str tu/secret \"/\" (name origin)))}\n91\t                        opts))))\n92\t\n93\t\n94\t(defn load-ast\n95\t  [machine ast]\n96\t  (sr/load-vector machine (project ast) code/contract))\n97\t\n98\t\n99\t;; =============================================================================\n100\t;; Machines\n101\t;; =============================================================================\n102\t\n103\t(defn parked-reader\n104\t  \"Parked on the second read of the stream it makes, A consumed: one :next\n105\t   wait over one cursor cell.\"\n106\t  []\n107\t  (let [m0 (vm/run (load-ast (new-machine)\n108\t                             (let1 's {:type :stream/make :buffer 4}\n109\t                                   (let1 'c (cursor-of (v 's))\n110\t                                         (then (next-of (v 'c)) (next-of (v 'c)))))))\n111\t        src (get (:resources m0) (:stream-id (first (:wait-set m0))))]\n112\t    (stream/append! src \"A\")\n113\t    (vm/run m0)))\n114\t\n115\t\n116\t(defn parked-writer\n117\t  \"Parked on a blocked write: the warm one-slot stream keeps the value\n118\t   retained. One :put wait.\"\n119\t  []\n120\t  (let [w (one-slot-stream \"w\")]\n121\t    (stream/append! w :warmed)\n122\t    (let [m0 (load-ast (new-machine) {:type :stream/put :target (v 'w) :val (lit \"v\")})\n123\t          [ref m1] (engine/attach-resource m0 w)]\n124\t      (vm/run (assoc m1 :store {'w ref})))))\n125\t\n126\t\n127\t(defn parked-explicit\n128\t  \"At an explicit park, its record's environment holding a cursor.\"\n129\t  []\n130\t  (vm/run (load-ast (new-machine)\n131\t                    (let1 's {:type :stream/make :buffer 4}\n132\t                          (app (lam ['c] {:type :vm/park}) (cursor-of (v 's)))))))\n133\t\n134\t\n135\t(defn parked-linker\n136\t  \"Parked on a link request under the :running gate, so the entry carries\n137\t   no :cursor: the lift refuses it (:link-cursor-not-installed).\"\n138\t  []\n139\t  (vm/run (-> (new-machine {:link-request (ring 8) :link-response (ring 8)})\n140\t              (load-ast (app (v 'require) (lit 'host.mod)))\n141\t              (assoc :yin.k/gate :running))))\n142\t\n143\t\n144\t(defn module-response\n145\t  []\n146\t  {:status :ok\n147\t   :image {:value (project (let1 's {:type :stream/make :buffer 4}\n148\t                                 (then (next-of (cursor-of (v 's))) (def! 'f (lam [] (lit 42))))))}\n149\t   :manifest {:yin.module/name 'host.mod :yin.module/exports #{'f}}\n150\t   :obligations []})\n151\t\n152\t\n153\t(defn parked-installer\n154\t  \"Parked at :install with a live child blocked on its own read.\"\n155\t  []\n156\t  (let [request (ring 64) response (ring 64)\n157\t        m0 (vm/run (load-ast (new-machine {:link-request request :link-response response})\n158\t                             (then (app (v 'require) (lit 'host.mod)) (app (v 'host.mod/f)))))\n159\t        entry (first (:wait-set m0))]\n160\t    (stream/append! response (assoc (module-response) :yin.link/id (:link-id entry)))\n161\t    (vm/run m0)))\n162\t\n163\t\n164\t(defn halted-machine\n165\t  \"Halted with result 42.\"\n166\t  []\n167\t  (vm/run (load-ast (new-machine) (lit 42))))\n168\t\n169\t\n170\t(defn- fresh-cursors\n171\t  [machine]\n172\t  (let [w (one-slot-stream \"k1\") x (one-slot-stream \"k2\")\n173\t        [wa m1] (engine/attach-resource machine w)\n174\t        [xa m2] (engine/attach-resource m1 x)\n175\t        [c1 m3] (engine/handle-cursor m2 {:stream wa} :k1)\n176\t        [c2 m4] (engine/handle-cursor m3 {:stream xa} :k2)]\n177\t    {:c1 c1 :c2 c2 :machine m4}))\n178\t\n179\t\n180\t(defn halted-with-cursors\n181\t  \"Halted with result (f c1 c2) over two fresh cursor references nothing\n182\t   else reaches.\"\n183\t  [f]\n184\t  (let [{:keys [c1 c2 machine]} (fresh-cursors (halted-machine))]\n185\t    (assoc machine :value (f c1 c2))))\n186\t\n187\t\n188\t(defn parked-module-store-cursors\n189\t  \"At an explicit park whose host.mod module store holds two cursor\n190\t   references, named by a module closure in the task store.\"\n191\t  []\n192\t  (let [ast (app (lam ['p] {:type :vm/park}) (lit 1))\n193\t        vec* (project ast)\n194\t        m (vm/run (load-ast (new-machine) ast))\n195\t        {:keys [c1 c2 machine]} (fresh-cursors m)\n196\t        closure (first (filter #(= :closure (first %)) vec*))\n197\t        clo (values/closure (:owner machine)\n198\t                            {:type :closure :params (nth closure 2) :entry (nth closure 3)\n199\t                             :segment (get (:code-aliases machine) (jing/segment-key vec*))\n200\t                             :env {engine/store-of-key 'host.mod}})]\n201\t    (assoc machine :store {'mod clo} :module-stores {'host.mod {'c c1 'd c2}})))\n202\t\n203\t\n204\t;; =============================================================================\n205\t;; The lift, the lower's attacher\n206\t;; =============================================================================\n207\t\n208\t(defn lift-opts\n209\t  ([] (lift-opts nil))\n210\t  ([header]\n211\t   (cond-> {:source-index @source-index}\n212\t     (some? header) (assoc :header header))))\n213\t\n214\t\n215\t(defn lift\n216\t  \"rows/lift-task of machine under header (nil: the fork) with a fresh\n217\t   deterministic exporter: the pack, or the refusal's ex-data.\"\n218\t  [machine header]\n219\t  (try (rows/lift-task machine (serve-table) (lift-opts header))\n220\t       (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e\n221\t         (or (ex-data e) (throw e)))))\n222\t\n223\t\n224\t(defn attacher\n225\t  \"A receiver's attach!: a fresh one-slot stream per descriptor, counting\n226\t   attaches in the atom it answers beside.\"\n227\t  []\n228\t  (let [n (atom 0)]\n229\t    {:count n\n230\t     :attach! (fn [d]\n231\t                (swap! n inc)\n232\t                {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n233\t                 :dao.stream/handle (one-slot-stream (str \"attached-\" (:dao.stream/identity d)))})}))\n234\t\n235\t\n236\t(defn receiver\n237\t  ([] (receiver {}))\n238\t  ([opts] (new-machine opts)))\n239\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"108e1cb8-f707-457b-be14-6feb1e135c49","uuid":"351b7515-8626-4604-82f9-d199c808cd4e","timestamp":"2026-10-13T10:03:27.627Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p7b/test/yin/vm/ucf/rows_support.cljc","content":"(ns yin.vm.ucf.rows-support\n  \"Test support for the row carrier under custody (phase 7a): real\n   semantic-register machines the engine parks, the composition's source\n   index, a deterministic exporter, the custody header parts and `lift`,\n   rows/lift-task over one machine. It mirrors yin.vm.ucf.lift-support,\n   whose AST helpers, one-slot streams, exporter and header parts it\n   reuses, over yin.vm.semantic-register instead of the old kernel.\n\n   Every pack the 7a tests and the rows checkpoint fixtures check comes\n   out of `lift`, never from a hand-built map. The one thing set by hand\n   is an operation id on a wait entry (`with-op-id`), as in lift-support.\n   The streams carry no random identity and `serve-table` answers s0, s1\n   ... in first-asked order, so a pack's bytes are the same on every run\n   and host.\"\n  (:require [dao.jing :as jing]\n            [dao.stream :as stream]\n            [dao.stream.ringbuffer :as ringbuffer]\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\n            [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\n            [yin.vm.module :as module]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register :as sr]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.code :as code]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.linearize :as linearize]\n            [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.lift-support :as ls]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.rows :as rows]\n            [yin.vm.values :as values]))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The composition: code by A and the source index\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(def source-index\n  \"The composition's {A #{tree-address}} (continuation §6.1): every vector\n   `project` makes is recorded beside the address of its AST.\"\n  (atom {}))\n\n\n(defn project\n  [ast]\n  (let [v (:vector (linearize/project ast))]\n    (swap! source-index update (jing/segment-key v) (fnil conj #{}) (jing/segment-key [:yin/tree ast]))\n    v))\n\n\n(def lit ls/lit)\n(def v ls/v)\n(def lam ls/lam)\n(def app ls/app)\n(def then ls/then)\n(def let1 ls/let1)\n(def def! ls/def!)\n(def cursor-of ls/cursor-of)\n(def next-of ls/next-of)\n(def one-slot-stream ls/one-slot-stream)\n(def serve-table ls/serve-table)\n(def with-op-id ls/with-op-id)\n(def occurrence ls/occurrence)\n(def predecessor ls/predecessor)\n(def origin ls/origin)\n(def arbitration ls/arbitration)\n(def op-id ls/op-id)\n(def header ls/header)\n\n\n(defn- ring\n  [capacity]\n  (:dao.stream/handle\n    (ringbuffer/create! {:dao.stream/type ringbuffer/transport-type ringbuffer/capacity-key capacity})))\n\n\n(defn- make-det-stream\n  []\n  (let [n (atom 0)]\n    (fn [_capacity]\n      {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n       :dao.stream/handle (one-slot-stream (str \"made-\" (swap! n inc)))})))\n\n\n(def stream-modules (module/register-stream-module (module/default-registry)))\n\n\n(defn new-machine\n  ([] (new-machine {}))\n  ([opts]\n   (sr/create-vm (merge {:make-stream (make-det-stream)\n                         :capability-secret tu/secret\n                         :modules stream-modules\n                         :secret-source (fn [origin] (str tu/secret \"/\" (name origin)))}\n                        opts))))\n\n\n(defn load-ast\n  [machine ast]\n  (sr/load-vector machine (project ast) code/contract))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Machines\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn parked-reader\n  \"Parked on the second read of the stream it makes, A consumed: one :next\n   wait over one cursor cell.\"\n  []\n  (let [m0 (vm/run (load-ast (new-machine)\n                             (let1 's {:type :stream/make :buffer 4}\n                                   (let1 'c (cursor-of (v 's))\n                                         (then (next-of (v 'c)) (next-of (v 'c)))))))\n        src (get (:resources m0) (:stream-id (first (:wait-set m0))))]\n    (stream/append! src \"A\")\n    (vm/run m0)))\n\n\n(defn parked-writer\n  \"Parked on a blocked write: the warm one-slot stream keeps the value\n   retained. One :put wait.\"\n  []\n  (let [w (one-slot-stream \"w\")]\n    (stream/append! w :warmed)\n    (let [m0 (load-ast (new-machine) {:type :stream/put :target (v 'w) :val (lit \"v\")})\n          [ref m1] (engine/attach-resource m0 w)]\n      (vm/run (assoc m1 :store {'w ref})))))\n\n\n(defn parked-explicit\n  \"At an explicit park, its record's environment holding a cursor.\"\n  []\n  (vm/run (load-ast (new-machine)\n                    (let1 's {:type :stream/make :buffer 4}\n                          (app (lam ['c] {:type :vm/park}) (cursor-of (v 's)))))))\n\n\n(defn parked-linker\n  \"Parked on a link request under the :running gate, so the entry carries\n   no :cursor: the lift refuses it (:link-cursor-not-installed).\"\n  []\n  (vm/run (-> (new-machine {:link-request (ring 8) :link-response (ring 8)})\n              (load-ast (app (v 'require) (lit 'host.mod)))\n              (assoc :yin.k/gate :running))))\n\n\n(defn module-response\n  []\n  {:status :ok\n   :image {:value (project (let1 's {:type :stream/make :buffer 4}\n                                 (then (next-of (cursor-of (v 's))) (def! 'f (lam [] (lit 42))))))}\n   :manifest {:yin.module/name 'host.mod :yin.module/exports #{'f}}\n   :obligations []})\n\n\n(defn parked-installer\n  \"Parked at :install with a live child blocked on its own read.\"\n  []\n  (let [request (ring 64) response (ring 64)\n        m0 (vm/run (load-ast (new-machine {:link-request request :link-response response})\n                             (then (app (v 'require) (lit 'host.mod)) (app (v 'host.mod/f)))))\n        entry (first (:wait-set m0))]\n    (stream/append! response (assoc (module-response) :yin.link/id (:link-id entry)))\n    (vm/run m0)))\n\n\n(defn halted-machine\n  \"Halted with result 42.\"\n  []\n  (vm/run (load-ast (new-machine) (lit 42))))\n\n\n(defn- fresh-cursors\n  [machine]\n  (let [w (one-slot-stream \"k1\") x (one-slot-stream \"k2\")\n        [wa m1] (engine/attach-resource machine w)\n        [xa m2] (engine/attach-resource m1 x)\n        [c1 m3] (engine/handle-cursor m2 {:stream wa} :k1)\n        [c2 m4] (engine/handle-cursor m3 {:stream xa} :k2)]\n    {:c1 c1 :c2 c2 :machine m4}))\n\n\n(defn halted-with-cursors\n  \"Halted with result (f c1 c2) over two fresh cursor references nothing\n   else reaches.\"\n  [f]\n  (let [{:keys [c1 c2 machine]} (fresh-cursors (halted-machine))]\n    (assoc machine :value (f c1 c2))))\n\n\n(defn parked-module-store-cursors\n  \"At an explicit park whose host.mod module store holds two cursor\n   references, named by a module closure in the task store.\"\n  []\n  (let [ast (app (lam ['p] {:type :vm/park}) (lit 1))\n        vec* (project ast)\n        m (vm/run (load-ast (new-machine) ast))\n        {:keys [c1 c2 machine]} (fresh-cursors m)\n        closure (first (filter #(= :closure (first %)) vec*))\n        clo (values/closure (:owner machine)\n                            {:type :closure :params (nth closure 2) :entry (nth closure 3)\n                             :segment (get (:code-aliases machine) (jing/segment-key vec*))\n                             :env {engine/store-of-key 'host.mod}})]\n    (assoc machine :store {'mod clo} :module-stores {'host.mod {'c c1 'd c2}})))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The lift, the lower's attacher\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn lift-opts\n  ([] (lift-opts nil))\n  ([header]\n   (cond-> {:source-index @source-index}\n     (some? header) (assoc :header header))))\n\n\n(defn lift\n  \"rows/lift-task of machine under header (nil: the fork) with a fresh\n   deterministic exporter: the pack, or the refusal's ex-data.\"\n  [machine header]\n  (try (rows/lift-task machine (serve-table) (lift-opts header))\n       (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e\n         (or (ex-data e) (throw e)))))\n\n\n(defn attacher\n  \"A receiver's attach!: a fresh one-slot stream per descriptor, counting\n   attaches in the atom it answers beside.\"\n  []\n  (let [n (atom 0)]\n    {:count n\n     :attach! (fn [d]\n                (swap! n inc)\n                {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok\n                 :dao.stream/handle (one-slot-stream (str \"attached-\" (:dao.stream/identity d)))})}))\n\n\n(defn receiver\n  ([] (receiver {}))\n  ([opts] (new-machine opts)))\n","numLines":239,"startLine":1,"totalLines":239}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01F57HUcGwFxVKeUzLUtNeQ4","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
