{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01APyKKmBEb8TJKpmgMCmzq7","type":"tool_result","content":"1400\t   for a stream that cannot be served, a cursor that cannot survive\n1401\t   the canonical codec, or -- when `opts` names cursor profiles that\n1402\t   do not cover the cells -- a claim the body cannot make.\n1403\t   `serve!` is the exporter's remote-table entry, exactly\n1404\t   `yin.vm.ucf.remote`'s.  A task that holds an `:observe` entry, an\n1405\t   entry or cell carrying `:yin.k/held`, an unminted cursor cell, a\n1406\t   pending close, or a cursorless `:link-request` entry -- itself or any\n1407\t   install child -- refuses `:yin.k/non-portable` of kind\n1408\t   `:reason-mismatch` before anything is lifted, the same holds\n1409\t   `yin.vm.ucf.holder.export/enter` refuses (UCF 7.4.1, 7.4.3).\n1410\t\n1411\t   `opts` may name `:header`, the version-1 custody header\n1412\t   (`yin.vm.ucf.holder.export/prepare` validates its shape): occurrence,\n1413\t   arbitration, next-op-seq, origin when the task has a predecessor, and\n1414\t   `:yin.k/enrolled`, the set of enrolled stream identities, which is a\n1415\t   lift input and never travels.  No header is the version-0 fork lift,\n1416\t   byte for byte as before; a header is the version-1 exclusive lift in\n1417\t   `dao.jing.cbor`, with `:yin.k/policy :yin.k/exclusive` added here.\n1418\t   The root carries the header by its kind (blocked or parked: all of\n1419\t   it; halted: the origin alone; an install child: none), refuses\n1420\t   `:op-seq-exhausted` at 2^52-1, `:unprotected-pending` and a stream\n1421\t   `:yin.k/unsatisfied` by the enrolled set, orders every map and set\n1422\t   by canonical key bytes, and before answering runs the version-1\n1423\t   inspector over its own bytes and address and then `validate-body`:\n1424\t   whatever either refuses is the lift's refusal, and nothing is\n1425\t   answered.  `:serve-keyed`, `(f [path resource-id] handle)`, replaces\n1426\t   `serve!` and retains each answer under the task path and the\n1427\t   resource id.\n1428\t\n1429\t   `:version 2` selects the version-2 body of the four execution\n1430\t   profiles (semantic, stack, register, walker), the profile being the\n1431\t   kernel's own: no header is the fork, a header the exclusive lift, and\n1432\t   the roles are structural (the v2 amendment, section 3).  The\n1433\t   composition chooses it; it is never inferred, and without it the lift\n1434\t   is exactly the version-0 or version-1 lift as before.\"\n1435\t  ([vm serve!]\n1436\t   (export-task vm serve! nil))\n1437\t  ([vm serve! opts]\n1438\t   (call!\n1439\t     (fn []\n1440\t       (when (seq (:ready-queue vm))\n1441\t         (refuse! :yin.k/not-quiescent\n1442\t                  {:yin.k/ready (count (:ready-queue vm))}))\n1443\t       (when-some [h (unliftable-hold vm)]\n1444\t         (non-portable! :reason-mismatch h))\n1445\t       (let [header (:header opts)\n1446\t             child? (::child opts)\n1447\t             v2? (= 2 (:version opts))\n1448\t             engine (when v2? (engine-of vm))\n1449\t             ;; `jing-codec?` names the jing wire and the exclusive-style\n1450\t             ;; lift, not \"version 1\": version 2 selects it too, and the\n1451\t             ;; version is dispatched separately, by `v2?` and the body's\n1452\t             ;; validated structural role (v2 amendment, section 10).\n1453\t             jing-codec? (boolean (or (some? header) (::jing-codec opts) v2?))\n1454\t             keyed (or (:serve-keyed opts) (fn [_ h] (serve! h)))\n1455\t             ;; grounded: ClojureDart compiles a many-key assoc onto nil\n1456\t             ;; as a conj, whose answer is a list no dissoc accepts\n1457\t             opts (assoc (or opts {})\n1458\t                         :path (or (:path opts) [])\n1459\t                         ::jing-codec jing-codec?\n1460\t                         ::enrolled (or (:yin.k/enrolled header)\n1461\t                                        (::enrolled opts)\n1462\t                                        #{})\n1463\t                         :serve-keyed keyed)\n1464\t             serve! (fn [id h] (keyed [(:path opts) id] h))\n1465\t             {:keys [encode-bytes decode-bytes]}\n1466\t             (if jing-codec?\n1467\t               {:encode-bytes jing.cbor/encode :decode-bytes jing.cbor/decode}\n1468\t               {:encode-bytes cbor/encode :decode-bytes cbor/decode})\n1469\t             walked (if (and v2? (not= :semantic engine))\n1470\t                      (census-v2 engine vm)\n1471\t                      (completion/complete\n1472\t                        {:vm vm\n1473\t                         :cursor-profile (constantly :dao.stream.remote/v1)\n1474\t                         :modules (module-decls vm)}))\n1475\t             _ (export-refusals (:yin.k/refusals walked))\n1476\t             ;; the pending-child gap the walk cannot close itself: an\n1477\t             ;; obligation a live install child will bind when it\n1478\t             ;; completes is discharged by the child this body carries\n1479\t             ;; beside the waiter, not by a store the emitter holds\n1480\t             installing (into #{}\n1481\t                              (mapcat (fn [[m inst]]\n1482\t                                        (map (fn [x]\n1483\t                                               (symbol (str (name m) \"/\"\n1484\t                                                            (name x))))\n1485\t                                             (get-in inst\n1486\t                                                     [:response :manifest\n1487\t                                                      :yin.module/exports])))\n1488\t                                      (:installs vm)))\n1489\t             missing (update (:yin.k/missing walked) :obligations\n1490\t                             #(set/difference (set %) installing))\n1491\t             discovery (cond\n1492\t                         (seq (:segments missing)) :blocked\n1493\t                         (some seq (vals (dissoc missing :segments)))\n1494\t                         :incomplete\n1495\t                         :else :complete)]\n1496\t         (when-not (= :complete discovery)\n1497\t           (refuse! :yin.k/unsatisfied\n1498\t                    {:yin.k/discovery discovery\n1499\t                     :yin.k/missing missing}))\n1500\t         (let [value (:value vm)\n1501\t               active (and (map? value)\n1502\t                           (= :parked-continuation (:type value))\n1503\t                           (contains? (:parked vm) (:id value)))\n1504\t               active-rec (when active (get (:parked vm) (:id value)))\n1505\t               kind (cond\n1506\t                      active :parked\n1507\t                      (engine/halted-with-empty-queue? vm) :halted\n1508\t                      (seq (:wait-set vm)) :blocked\n1509\t                      :else (not-at-safepoint!\n1510\t                              (get-in vm [:control :pc])))\n1511\t               _ (when (and (= :halted kind) (seq (:wait-set vm)))\n1512\t                   (non-portable! :inconsistent-halt {}))\n1513\t               _ (when (and jing-codec? (not child?) (not= :halted kind)\n1514\t                            (let [n (:yin.k/next-op-seq header)]\n1515\t                              (and (jing.cbor/numeric? n)\n1516\t                                   (jing.cbor/num= n checkpoint/max-exact))))\n1517\t                   (non-portable! :op-seq-exhausted\n1518\t                                  {:yin.k/next-op-seq\n1519\t                                   (:yin.k/next-op-seq header)}))\n1520\t               _ (when (and active\n1521\t                            (not (explicit-park? engine vm active-rec)))\n1522\t                   (non-portable! :reason-mismatch\n1523\t                                  {:yin.k/pc (:pc active-rec)}))\n1524\t               found (atom (cond-> (assoc (new-found)\n1525\t                                          :jing-codec jing-codec?\n1526\t                                          :full-census (::recovery opts)\n1527\t                                          :recovery-cell-ids (:yin.k/recovery-cell-ids vm)\n1528\t                                          :enrolled (::enrolled opts))\n1529\t                             v2? (assoc :v2 {:engine engine})\n1530\t                             jing-codec? (assoc :order\n1531\t                                                (canonical-order\n1532\t                                                  vm serve!\n1533\t                                                  (when v2? {:engine engine})))))\n1534\t               encode (value-encoder vm serve! found)\n1535\t               frames (mapv (partial lift-frame! vm serve! found encode)\n1536\t                            (:wait-set vm))\n1537\t               parked (into {}\n1538\t                            (map (fn [[pid rec]]\n1539\t                                   (when-not (and v2? (not= :semantic engine))"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"108e1cb8-f707-457b-be14-6feb1e135c49","uuid":"3122c2ac-7231-459d-802e-d9361faa375d","timestamp":"2026-10-13T10:03:41.559Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p7b/src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/handoff.cljc","content":"   for a stream that cannot be served, a cursor that cannot survive\n   the canonical codec, or -- when `opts` names cursor profiles that\n   do not cover the cells -- a claim the body cannot make.\n   `serve!` is the exporter's remote-table entry, exactly\n   `yin.vm.ucf.remote`'s.  A task that holds an `:observe` entry, an\n   entry or cell carrying `:yin.k/held`, an unminted cursor cell, a\n   pending close, or a cursorless `:link-request` entry -- itself or any\n   install child -- refuses `:yin.k/non-portable` of kind\n   `:reason-mismatch` before anything is lifted, the same holds\n   `yin.vm.ucf.holder.export/enter` refuses (UCF 7.4.1, 7.4.3).\n\n   `opts` may name `:header`, the version-1 custody header\n   (`yin.vm.ucf.holder.export/prepare` validates its shape): occurrence,\n   arbitration, next-op-seq, origin when the task has a predecessor, and\n   `:yin.k/enrolled`, the set of enrolled stream identities, which is a\n   lift input and never travels.  No header is the version-0 fork lift,\n   byte for byte as before; a header is the version-1 exclusive lift in\n   `dao.jing.cbor`, with `:yin.k/policy :yin.k/exclusive` added here.\n   The root carries the header by its kind (blocked or parked: all of\n   it; halted: the origin alone; an install child: none), refuses\n   `:op-seq-exhausted` at 2^52-1, `:unprotected-pending` and a stream\n   `:yin.k/unsatisfied` by the enrolled set, orders every map and set\n   by canonical key bytes, and before answering runs the version-1\n   inspector over its own bytes and address and then `validate-body`:\n   whatever either refuses is the lift's refusal, and nothing is\n   answered.  `:serve-keyed`, `(f [path resource-id] handle)`, replaces\n   `serve!` and retains each answer under the task path and the\n   resource id.\n\n   `:version 2` selects the version-2 body of the four execution\n   profiles (semantic, stack, register, walker), the profile being the\n   kernel's own: no header is the fork, a header the exclusive lift, and\n   the roles are structural (the v2 amendment, section 3).  The\n   composition chooses it; it is never inferred, and without it the lift\n   is exactly the version-0 or version-1 lift as before.\"\n  ([vm serve!]\n   (export-task vm serve! nil))\n  ([vm serve! opts]\n   (call!\n     (fn []\n       (when (seq (:ready-queue vm))\n         (refuse! :yin.k/not-quiescent\n                  {:yin.k/ready (count (:ready-queue vm))}))\n       (when-some [h (unliftable-hold vm)]\n         (non-portable! :reason-mismatch h))\n       (let [header (:header opts)\n             child? (::child opts)\n             v2? (= 2 (:version opts))\n             engine (when v2? (engine-of vm))\n             ;; `jing-codec?` names the jing wire and the exclusive-style\n             ;; lift, not \"version 1\": version 2 selects it too, and the\n             ;; version is dispatched separately, by `v2?` and the body's\n             ;; validated structural role (v2 amendment, section 10).\n             jing-codec? (boolean (or (some? header) (::jing-codec opts) v2?))\n             keyed (or (:serve-keyed opts) (fn [_ h] (serve! h)))\n             ;; grounded: ClojureDart compiles a many-key assoc onto nil\n             ;; as a conj, whose answer is a list no dissoc accepts\n             opts (assoc (or opts {})\n                         :path (or (:path opts) [])\n                         ::jing-codec jing-codec?\n                         ::enrolled (or (:yin.k/enrolled header)\n                                        (::enrolled opts)\n                                        #{})\n                         :serve-keyed keyed)\n             serve! (fn [id h] (keyed [(:path opts) id] h))\n             {:keys [encode-bytes decode-bytes]}\n             (if jing-codec?\n               {:encode-bytes jing.cbor/encode :decode-bytes jing.cbor/decode}\n               {:encode-bytes cbor/encode :decode-bytes cbor/decode})\n             walked (if (and v2? (not= :semantic engine))\n                      (census-v2 engine vm)\n                      (completion/complete\n                        {:vm vm\n                         :cursor-profile (constantly :dao.stream.remote/v1)\n                         :modules (module-decls vm)}))\n             _ (export-refusals (:yin.k/refusals walked))\n             ;; the pending-child gap the walk cannot close itself: an\n             ;; obligation a live install child will bind when it\n             ;; completes is discharged by the child this body carries\n             ;; beside the waiter, not by a store the emitter holds\n             installing (into #{}\n                              (mapcat (fn [[m inst]]\n                                        (map (fn [x]\n                                               (symbol (str (name m) \"/\"\n                                                            (name x))))\n                                             (get-in inst\n                                                     [:response :manifest\n                                                      :yin.module/exports])))\n                                      (:installs vm)))\n             missing (update (:yin.k/missing walked) :obligations\n                             #(set/difference (set %) installing))\n             discovery (cond\n                         (seq (:segments missing)) :blocked\n                         (some seq (vals (dissoc missing :segments)))\n                         :incomplete\n                         :else :complete)]\n         (when-not (= :complete discovery)\n           (refuse! :yin.k/unsatisfied\n                    {:yin.k/discovery discovery\n                     :yin.k/missing missing}))\n         (let [value (:value vm)\n               active (and (map? value)\n                           (= :parked-continuation (:type value))\n                           (contains? (:parked vm) (:id value)))\n               active-rec (when active (get (:parked vm) (:id value)))\n               kind (cond\n                      active :parked\n                      (engine/halted-with-empty-queue? vm) :halted\n                      (seq (:wait-set vm)) :blocked\n                      :else (not-at-safepoint!\n                              (get-in vm [:control :pc])))\n               _ (when (and (= :halted kind) (seq (:wait-set vm)))\n                   (non-portable! :inconsistent-halt {}))\n               _ (when (and jing-codec? (not child?) (not= :halted kind)\n                            (let [n (:yin.k/next-op-seq header)]\n                              (and (jing.cbor/numeric? n)\