{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017Gz8gnb4a1M5rJ2Bc2JzBX","type":"tool_result","content":"380\tResource entries never appear in `:store`; streams and cursor cells lower into\n381\tthe receiver's private resource table beside the program store (linker\n382\tM4, `yin.vm.linker.md` 7.3). `:module-store` rows are the per-module\n383\tsnapshots of §7.6.2's M4 paragraph. The parked table holds exactly the\n384\treachable records. An `:install` row carries the complete entry of\n385\t§7.4.3 r5: phase `:running` or `:parked`, parent link id (nil where the\n386\tcontract permits), the response verbatim as structural data, and the\n387\tchild as a cref to a whole `:task` row in the child role. \"Verified\"\n388\tmeans verified by the **receiver**, never trusted because it decodes:\n389\tthe response's manifest names the module the row is keyed by, its link\n390\tid equals `parent`, its image is well formed, hashes to the address it\n391\tis delivered under, is the image the manifest names, and its format,\n392\tcontract and the child's profile agree (`yin.vm.linker.md` §5, §9;\n393\tamendment §2). A failure is `:yin.k/undecodable` naming the row.\n394\t**Amended after 6b (2026-10-13; continuation §5.2 B1, §7.2):** the\n395\tmerged lower (`rows/check-install!`) verifies, before any attachment:\n396\tthe phase is one of `#{:running :parked}` (`:install-phase`); the\n397\tresponse is a map with `:status :ok`, a `:manifest` whose\n398\t`:yin.module/name` is the row's module and whose `:yin.module/exports`\n399\tis a collection of symbols, and an `:image` map whose `:value` the\n400\treceiving kernel's loader admits (`:install-response`); and the carried\n401\tchild task's kind is `:blocked` (`:install-child`), the only kind the\n402\tengine retains at a safepoint (a halted or parked child is linked in the\n403\tsweep it halts in, so phase `:running` is a wire phase the codec accepts\n404\tbut the engine never exposes at a safepoint). The link-id-equals-parent\n405\tand image-address-equals-manifest checks of the paragraph above are\n406\t**not** implemented (continuation §11 Q3).\n407\t\n408\t### 5.5 The root\n409\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"108e1cb8-f707-457b-be14-6feb1e135c49","uuid":"81833608-39a3-4f35-a8dd-5218b67d682b","timestamp":"2026-10-13T10:05:14.288Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p7b/docs/design/yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md","content":"Resource entries never appear in `:store`; streams and cursor cells lower into\nthe receiver's private resource table beside the program store (linker\nM4, `yin.vm.linker.md` 7.3). `:module-store` rows are the per-module\nsnapshots of §7.6.2's M4 paragraph. The parked table holds exactly the\nreachable records. An `:install` row carries the complete entry of\n§7.4.3 r5: phase `:running` or `:parked`, parent link id (nil where the\ncontract permits), the response verbatim as structural data, and the\nchild as a cref to a whole `:task` row in the child role. \"Verified\"\nmeans verified by the **receiver**, never trusted because it decodes:\nthe response's manifest names the module the row is keyed by, its link\nid equals `parent`, its image is well formed, hashes to the address it\nis delivered under, is the image the manifest names, and its format,\ncontract and the child's profile agree (`yin.vm.linker.md` §5, §9;\namendment §2). A failure is `:yin.k/undecodable` naming the row.\n**Amended after 6b (2026-10-13; continuation §5.2 B1, §7.2):** the\nmerged lower (`rows/check-install!`) verifies, before any attachment:\nthe phase is one of `#{:running :parked}` (`:install-phase`); the\nresponse is a map with `:status :ok`, a `:manifest` whose\n`:yin.module/name` is the row's module and whose `:yin.module/exports`\nis a collection of symbols, and an `:image` map whose `:value` the\nreceiving kernel's loader admits (`:install-response`); and the carried\nchild task's kind is `:blocked` (`:install-child`), the only kind the\nengine retains at a safepoint (a halted or parked child is linked in the\nsweep it halts in, so phase `:running` is a wire phase the codec accepts\nbut the engine never exposes at a safepoint). The link-id-equals-parent\nand image-address-equals-manifest checks of the paragraph above are\n**not** implemented (continuation §11 Q3).\n\n### 5.5 The root\n","numLines":30,"startLine":380,"totalLines":993}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_017Gz8gnb4a1M5rJ2Bc2JzBX","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
