{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01AHkRhDkKvLmLCuZ6Xy72uS","type":"tool_result","content":"50\t   :yin.k/version 0})\n51\t\n52\t\n53\t(defn derive-record\n54\t  \"§5.2/§8.2's `:derive` record: `output` was computed from `input` by\n55\t   `:yin.vm/lower` under `lowering-profile`. A plain map, so it is\n56\t   content-addressed by `dao.jing/segment-key`, immutable, and\n57\t   verifiable; its own address is what the ledger publishes. The\n58\t   addresses are the only coordinates — the record holds no log-local\n59\t   id, so it is hashed once, when built.\"\n60\t  [input output]\n61\t  {:yin.ledger/op :derive\n62\t   :yin.ledger/input input\n63\t   :yin.ledger/output output\n64\t   :yin.ledger/function :yin.vm/lower\n65\t   :yin.ledger/profile lowering-profile})\n66\t\n67\t\n68\t(defn derive-event\n69\t  \"§8.2's ledger event tx-data for one record: a local entity with the\n70\t   record's fields as attributes and the record's address as one more.\n71\t   `ev` is a tempid — distinct tempids for distinct events, whether in\n72\t   one transaction or several. The profile travels as the structured map,\n73\t   exactly as it appears in the record; no string rendering is defined.\"\n74\t  [ev {:yin.ledger/keys [op input output function profile] :as record}]\n75\t  [[:db/add ev :yin.ledger/op op]\n76\t   [:db/add ev :yin.ledger/input input]\n77\t   [:db/add ev :yin.ledger/output output]\n78\t   [:db/add ev :yin.ledger/function function]\n79\t   [:db/add ev :yin.ledger/profile profile]\n80\t   [:db/add ev :yin.ledger/record (jing/segment-key record)]])\n81\t\n82\t\n83\t(defn derive-lowering\n84\t  \"The `:derive` material for one row-lane lowering, written by\n85\t   `linearize/lower-rows`'s caller (§5.2): `lower-rows` produces the\n86\t   vector and provenance and knows no ledger; its caller names the two\n87\t   addresses and mints the record. Returns the record, its address, the\n88\t   event tx-data for tempid `ev`, and the addresses the ledger names —\n89\t   `:tree-address` is the row set's root id, `:segment-address` the\n90\t   vector's `(jing/segment-key vector)`.\"\n91\t  [{:keys [root]} {:keys [vector]} ev]\n92\t  (let [segment (jing/segment-key vector)\n93\t        record (derive-record root segment)]\n94\t    {:tree-address root\n95\t     :segment-address segment\n96\t     :record record\n97\t     :record-address (jing/segment-key record)\n98\t     :event (derive-event ev record)}))\n99\t\n100\t\n101\t(defn name-entity\n102\t  \"§8.3's name entity — a local entity carrying `:yin/name` — as tx-data,\n103\t   written once when the entity is created. A later naming assertion or\n104\t   retraction goes through `assert-name`/`retract-name` on the same\n105\t   entity id.\"\n106\t  [name sym]\n107\t  [[:db/add name :yin/name sym]])\n108\t\n109\t\n110\t(defn assert-name\n111\t  \"§8.3's naming row `[t :assert tree-addr name]` as tx-data:\n112\t   `[:db/add name :yin/code tree-addr]` on the name entity\n113\t   (`name-entity` writes its identity datom).\n114\t\n115\t   With an `event` tempid shared with a `derive-event`'s tx-data, the\n116\t   assertion's `m` resolves to the event's allocated id — the provenance\n117\t   link from the naming datom to its event through the metadata-entity\n118\t   path (§8.2). `naming-event` walks it back. Without one, `m` defaults\n119\t   to the `:db/assert` marker.\""}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"108e1cb8-f707-457b-be14-6feb1e135c49","uuid":"87bc24af-bbdf-4423-bed0-793f56abb64e","timestamp":"2026-10-13T10:06:08.228Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p7b/src/cljc/yin/vm/ledger.cljc","content":"   :yin.k/version 0})\n\n\n(defn derive-record\n  \"§5.2/§8.2's `:derive` record: `output` was computed from `input` by\n   `:yin.vm/lower` under `lowering-profile`. A plain map, so it is\n   content-addressed by `dao.jing/segment-key`, immutable, and\n   verifiable; its own address is what the ledger publishes. The\n   addresses are the only coordinates — the record holds no log-local\n   id, so it is hashed once, when built.\"\n  [input output]\n  {:yin.ledger/op :derive\n   :yin.ledger/input input\n   :yin.ledger/output output\n   :yin.ledger/function :yin.vm/lower\n   :yin.ledger/profile lowering-profile})\n\n\n(defn derive-event\n  \"§8.2's ledger event tx-data for one record: a local entity with the\n   record's fields as attributes and the record's address as one more.\n   `ev` is a tempid — distinct tempids for distinct events, whether in\n   one transaction or several. The profile travels as the structured map,\n   exactly as it appears in the record; no string rendering is defined.\"\n  [ev {:yin.ledger/keys [op input output function profile] :as record}]\n  [[:db/add ev :yin.ledger/op op]\n   [:db/add ev :yin.ledger/input input]\n   [:db/add ev :yin.ledger/output output]\n   [:db/add ev :yin.ledger/function function]\n   [:db/add ev :yin.ledger/profile profile]\n   [:db/add ev :yin.ledger/record (jing/segment-key record)]])\n\n\n(defn derive-lowering\n  \"The `:derive` material for one row-lane lowering, written by\n   `linearize/lower-rows`'s caller (§5.2): `lower-rows` produces the\n   vector and provenance and knows no ledger; its caller names the two\n   addresses and mints the record. Returns the record, its address, the\n   event tx-data for tempid `ev`, and the addresses the ledger names —\n   `:tree-address` is the row set's root id, `:segment-address` the\n   vector's `(jing/segment-key vector)`.\"\n  [{:keys [root]} {:keys [vector]} ev]\n  (let [segment (jing/segment-key vector)\n        record (derive-record root segment)]\n    {:tree-address root\n     :segment-address segment\n     :record record\n     :record-address (jing/segment-key record)\n     :event (derive-event ev record)}))\n\n\n(defn name-entity\n  \"§8.3's name entity — a local entity carrying `:yin/name` — as tx-data,\n   written once when the entity is created. A later naming assertion or\n   retraction goes through `assert-name`/`retract-name` on the same\n   entity id.\"\n  [name sym]\n  [[:db/add name :yin/name sym]])\n\n\n(defn assert-name\n  \"§8.3's naming row `[t :assert tree-addr name]` as tx-data:\n   `[:db/add name :yin/code tree-addr]` on the name entity\n   (`name-entity` writes its identity datom).\n\n   With an `event` tempid shared with a `derive-event`'s tx-data, the\n   assertion's `m` resolves to the event's allocated id — the provenance\n   link from the naming datom to its event through the metadata-entity\n   path (§8.2). `naming-event` walks it back. Without one, `m` defaults\n   to the `:db/assert` marker.\"","numLines":70,"startLine":50,"totalLines":272}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01AHkRhDkKvLmLCuZ6Xy72uS","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
