{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BEeHJejbQXnXq5tc4WmHct","type":"tool_result","content":"(ns yin.vm.semantic-register.safepoint-harness-test\n  \"Phase 6b: the safepoint harness on the :semantic-register lane\n   (docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md §5, §8.2).\n\n   Each row of the §5.2 matrix is built twice under each of the four\n   segment wrappers: the reference build is satisfied and run on its own\n   machine; the handoff build is lifted with rows/lift-task, lowered with\n   rows/lower-task into a fresh receiver over the toy channel, relifted at\n   once, then satisfied through the source's streams. Result and effect\n   trace equal the reference (law 1); the relift equals the lift by root\n   id under rows/canonical-under (law 2); the pending's reason is the\n   observed wait's (law 3); every lifted frame passes the validator\n   (law 6). Row 20 runs once, outside the wrappers.\n\n   Phase 6c adds the two de Bruijn lanes (§5.3): a world built under\n   *lane* :stack or :register runs A's derived image on that kernel and\n   lifts and lowers through yin.vm.semantic-register.layout. Law 4 (one\n   root id on all three lanes under canonical-under), law 5 (six ordered\n   lowering pairs, each continuing to the reference result) and the\n   layout refusals close the file.\"\n  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n            [dao.jing :as jing]\n            [dao.stream :as stream]\n            [dao.stream.apply :as apply2]\n            [dao.test-slow :as slow]\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\n            [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\n            [yin.vm.ffi :as ffi]\n            [yin.vm.module :as module]\n            [yin.vm.values :as values]\n            [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register :as sr]\n            [yin.vm.debruijn.register :as rvm]\n            [yin.vm.debruijn.stack :as dvm]\n            [yin.vm.parity-test :as b0]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.analysis :as analysis]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.code :as code]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.corpus :as corpus]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.frame :as frame]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.frame-test :as ft]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.layout :as layout]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.linearize :as linearize]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.lift-support :as support]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.rows :as rows]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.v2-support :as s]))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The composition: code by A, the source index, one machine builder\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(def source-index\n  \"The composition's {A #{tree-address}} (§6.1): every vector this\n   harness projects is recorded beside the address of its AST.\"\n  (atom {}))\n\n\n(def code-index\n  \"{A v}: every vector this harness projects, for the layouts' spaces.\"\n  (atom {}))\n52:(def source-index\n70:(defn project\n74:    (swap! source-index update a (fnil conj #{}) (jing/segment-key [:yin/tree ast]))\n190:  {:source-index @source-index})\n960:          d (error #(rows/lift-task (:machine world) (:serve! (served #{:reader})) {:source-index {}}))]","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"108e1cb8-f707-457b-be14-6feb1e135c49","uuid":"5dc9389d-e6a6-4563-b7d2-d44702f115b4","timestamp":"2026-10-13T10:14:25.269Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"(ns yin.vm.semantic-register.safepoint-harness-test\n  \"Phase 6b: the safepoint harness on the :semantic-register lane\n   (docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md §5, §8.2).\n\n   Each row of the §5.2 matrix is built twice under each of the four\n   segment wrappers: the reference build is satisfied and run on its own\n   machine; the handoff build is lifted with rows/lift-task, lowered with\n   rows/lower-task into a fresh receiver over the toy channel, relifted at\n   once, then satisfied through the source's streams. Result and effect\n   trace equal the reference (law 1); the relift equals the lift by root\n   id under rows/canonical-under (law 2); the pending's reason is the\n   observed wait's (law 3); every lifted frame passes the validator\n   (law 6). Row 20 runs once, outside the wrappers.\n\n   Phase 6c adds the two de Bruijn lanes (§5.3): a world built under\n   *lane* :stack or :register runs A's derived image on that kernel and\n   lifts and lowers through yin.vm.semantic-register.layout. Law 4 (one\n   root id on all three lanes under canonical-under), law 5 (six ordered\n   lowering pairs, each continuing to the reference result) and the\n   layout refusals close the file.\"\n  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n            [dao.jing :as jing]\n            [dao.stream :as stream]\n            [dao.stream.apply :as apply2]\n            [dao.test-slow :as slow]\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\n            [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\n            [yin.vm.ffi :as ffi]\n            [yin.vm.module :as module]\n            [yin.vm.values :as values]\n            [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register :as sr]\n            [yin.vm.debruijn.register :as rvm]\n            [yin.vm.debruijn.stack :as dvm]\n            [yin.vm.parity-test :as b0]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.analysis :as analysis]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.code :as code]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.corpus :as corpus]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.frame :as frame]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.frame-test :as ft]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.layout :as layout]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.linearize :as linearize]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.lift-support :as support]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.rows :as rows]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.v2-support :as s]))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The composition: code by A, the source index, one machine builder\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(def source-index\n  \"The composition's {A #{tree-address}} (§6.1): every vector this\n   harness projects is recorded beside the address of its AST.\"\n  (atom {}))\n\n\n(def code-index\n  \"{A v}: every vector this harness projects, for the layouts' spaces.\"\n  (atom {}))\n52:(def source-index\n70:(defn project\n74:    (swap! source-index update a (fnil conj #{}) (jing/segment-key [:yin/tree ast]))\n190:  {:source-index @source-index})\n960:          d (error #(rows/lift-task (:machine world) (:serve! (served #{:reader})) {:source-index {}}))]","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01BEeHJejbQXnXq5tc4WmHct","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"subcommandResults"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfz4Seri5tmLpQVqvDyNb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JqTTd7gsDWmQPWFo3hTFHQ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'EOF'\np='test/yin/vm/semantic_register/safepoint_harness_test.cljc'\ns=open(p).read()\na=\"\"\"(defn module-response\n  [body exports]\n  {:status :ok :image {:value (project body)}\n   :manifest {:yin.module/name 'host.mod :yin.module/exports exports} :obligations []})\"\"\"\nb=\"\"\"(defn module-response\n  \"A link response as the linker answers one (yin.vm.linker/link-manifest):\n   the image, the manifest naming its tree and its :yin.semantic/code\n   derivation record, and that record, from the tree to the image's A.\"\n  [body exports]\n  (let [v (project body)\n        tree (jing/segment-key [:yin/tree body])\n        record (ledger/derive-record tree (jing/segment-key v))]\n    {:status :ok :image {:value v}\n     :manifest {:yin.module/name 'host.mod :yin.module/exports exports\n                :yin.module/tree tree :yin.module/derivations {:yin.semantic/code (jing/segment-key record)}}\n     :derivation record :obligations []}))\"\"\"\nassert s.count(a)==1\ns=s.replace(a,b)\na2=\"\"\"            [yin.vm.ffi :as ffi]\n            [yin.vm.module :as module]\"\"\"\nassert s.count(a2)==1\ns=s.replace(a2,\"\"\"            [yin.vm.ffi :as ffi]\n            [yin.vm.ledger :as ledger]\n            [yin.vm.module :as module]\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\n\np='test/yin/vm/ucf/rows_support.cljc'\ns=open(p).read()\na=\"\"\"(defn module-response\n  []\n  {:status :ok\n   :image {:value (project (let1 's {:type :stream/make :buffer 4}\n                                 (then (next-of (cursor-of (v 's))) (def! 'f (lam [] (lit 42))))))}\n   :manifest {:yin.module/name 'host.mod :yin.module/exports #{'f}}\n   :obligations []})\"\"\"\nb=\"\"\"(defn linked-response\n  \"A link response as the linker answers one (yin.vm.linker/link-manifest):\n   the image of ast, the manifest naming its tree and its :yin.semantic/code\n   derivation record, and that record, from the tree to the image's A. The\n   lower checks that chain (rows/check-install!, continuation §11 Q3).\"\n  [ast module-name exports]\n  (let [image (project ast)\n        tree (jing/segment-key [:yin/tree ast])\n        record (ledger/derive-record tree (jing/segment-key image))]\n    {:status :ok\n     :image {:value image}\n     :manifest {:yin.module/name module-name :yin.module/exports exports\n                :yin.module/tree tree\n                :yin.module/derivations {:yin.semantic/code (jing/segment-key record)}}\n     :derivation record\n     :obligations []}))\n\n\n(defn module-response\n  []\n  (linked-response (let1 's {:type :stream/make :buffer 4}\n                         (then (next-of (cursor-of (v 's))) (def! 'f (lam [] (lit 42)))))\n                   'host.mod #{'f}))\"\"\"\nassert s.count(a)==1\ns=s.replace(a,b)\na2=\"\"\"            [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\n            [yin.vm.module :as module]\"\"\"\nassert s.count(a2)==1\ns=s.replace(a2,\"\"\"            [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\n            [yin.vm.ledger :as ledger]\n            [yin.vm.module :as module]\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -rn \"module-response\\|rs/linked\\|parked-installer\" test/yin/vm/ucf/rows_checkpoint_fixtures.cljc test/yin/vm/ucf/rows_custody_test.cljc | head","description":"Real derivation chain in test responses"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1876,"cache_read_input_tokens":317694,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1876},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"108e1cb8-f707-457b-be14-6feb1e135c49","uuid":"7e61e3