{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016dGsHVREWv2ss5TdvyxFyU","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t(ns yin.vm.ucf.lift-support\n2\t  \"Test support for the version-1 lift (M-next D9): real machines the\n3\t   engine parks, a deterministic exporter, the custody header parts, and\n4\t   `lift`, the whole enter / prepare / encode path over one machine.\n5\t\n6\t   Every body the D9 tests and the regenerated C4 fixtures check comes\n7\t   out of `lift`, never from a hand-built map.  The one thing set by\n8\t   hand is an operation id on a wait entry (`with-op-id`): no code\n9\t   assigns ids until D11, whose fenced writer replaces that helper, and\n10\t   whose tests must show a real run produces entries equal in shape to\n11\t   what it sets.\"\n12\t  (:require [dao.stream :as stream]\n13\t            [dao.stream.ringbuffer :as ringbuffer]\n14\t            [yin.vm :as vm]\n15\t            [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\n16\t            [yin.vm.linearize :as linearize]\n17\t            [yin.vm.module :as module]\n18\t            [yin.vm.semantic :as semantic]\n19\t            [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]\n20\t            [yin.vm.ucf.holder.export :as export]\n21\t            [yin.vm.values :as values]))\n22\t\n23\t\n24\t;; =============================================================================\n25\t;; Machines\n26\t;; =============================================================================\n27\t\n28\t(defn- ring\n29\t  [capacity]\n30\t  (:dao.stream/handle"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"108e1cb8-f707-457b-be14-6feb1e135c49","uuid":"ab501708-2854-4cfc-bf44-b54d62e53092","timestamp":"2026-10-13T10:23:57.279Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p7b/test/yin/vm/ucf/lift_support.cljc","content":"(ns yin.vm.ucf.lift-support\n  \"Test support for the version-1 lift (M-next D9): real machines the\n   engine parks, a deterministic exporter, the custody header parts, and\n   `lift`, the whole enter / prepare / encode path over one machine.\n\n   Every body the D9 tests and the regenerated C4 fixtures check comes\n   out of `lift`, never from a hand-built map.  The one thing set by\n   hand is an operation id on a wait entry (`with-op-id`): no code\n   assigns ids until D11, whose fenced writer replaces that helper, and\n   whose tests must show a real run produces entries equal in shape to\n   what it sets.\"\n  (:require [dao.stream :as stream]\n            [dao.stream.ringbuffer :as ringbuffer]\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\n            [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\n            [yin.vm.linearize :as linearize]\n            [yin.vm.module :as module]\n            [yin.vm.semantic :as semantic]\n            [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.holder.export :as export]\n            [yin.vm.values :as values]))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Machines\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- ring\n  [capacity]\n  (:dao.stream/handle","numLines":30,"startLine":1,"totalLines":473}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_016dGsHVREWv2ss5TdvyxFyU","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
